#' Batched matrix product over the last two axes, like TF BatchMatMulV2.
#'
#' Leading axes broadcast. CPU operands use dtype promotion; CUDA operands must share one context and the same Float32/Float64 dtype. CUDA uses cuBLAS with native packing for strided views and no host numerical fallback. Both inputs need rank >= 2. Zero inner dimension produces zeros. The result retains the CUDA context, or uses the default CPU context for CPU inputs. Gradients with matching batch shapes run on CUDA; gradients requiring batch broadcast reduction currently fail until native reductions are implemented. Floating results can vary in their last bits with batch shape/backend.
#' @usage
#' matmul(a, b, transpose_a = FALSE, transpose_b = FALSE)
#' @param a `Tensor`. Left operand, with stored final axes \[m,k\] (or \[k,m\] when transposed).
#' @param b `Tensor`. Right operand, with stored final axes \[k,n\] (or \[n,k\] when transposed).
#' @param transpose_a `logical`. Transpose the final two axes of a; default false.
#' @param transpose_b `logical`. Transpose the final two axes of b; default false.
#' @return `Tensor`: Packed tensor with broadcast batch shape followed by \[m,n\].
