#' implicit. Use existing ImqMmd() separately; its signed value is not a quality
#' score. O(N*784) work/storage with host finite validation; input unchanged.
#' @usage
#' GanCoarsePixels(pixels)
#' @param pixels `Tensor`. Finite floating CPU samples with first axis N and trailing product784.
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning live matching-dtype CPU\[N,16\] coarse features.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' const auto coarse=dm::nn::models::GanCoarsePixels(dm::nn::ones({2,784}));
#' // coarse is [2,16], all values approximately .25. No kernel or model is fitted.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid geometry/dtype/values or nonfinite output.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @seealso ImqMmd(), ImqKernel(), AuxiliaryClassifierGan()
#' @md
#'
`GanCoarsePixels` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_432`, NULL, list(...))
#' Predict real/fake source and auxiliary classes from images alone.
#'
#' Dense hidden tanh H feeds class logits C and a raw source logit. Creates
#' hidden/W,b, class/W,b, source/W,b in that order: the class head precedes the
#' source head in the initialization stream. Defaults create six leaves/25483
#' values. Images are finite signed Float32/64 CPU \[N,F\], matching store dtype;
#' strides and all continuous first/higher paths are retained. No class condition,
#' target, noise, sigmoid source probability, loss, RNG draw beyond missing-leaf
#' creation, fitting or update is hidden. Inputs remain unchanged; outputs own
#' lifetime. Invalid inputs fail before leaves; incompatible existing leaves or
#' nonfinite computation may fail later. Work O(N*H*(F+C+1)), activation storage
#' O(N*(H+C+1)); synchronize callers sharing a mutable store.
#' @usage
#' AuxiliaryGanDiscriminate(discriminator, image, features = 784, classes = 10, hidden = 32)
#' @param discriminator `ParameterStore`. Caller-owned floating store, mutated only for missing leaves.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Finite signed CPU matrix \[N,features\], N>0, matching store dtype.
#' @param features `integer`. Positive image width F, default 784.
#' @param classes `integer`. Positive auxiliary class count C, default 10.
#' @param hidden `integer`. Positive tanh hidden width H, default 32.
#' @return `AuxiliaryDiscriminator`: Owning source logits, class logits and softmax class probabilities.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore d(5219,n::DType::Float64);
#' const auto
#' out=n::models::AuxiliaryGanDiscriminate(d,n::full({2,3},-.2,n::DType::Float64),3,2,4);
#' // No labels enter D; out.class_probability has two columns.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid widths/products, inputs, stored leaves or computed
#'   nonfinite values.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Odena, Olah and Shlens (2017), Conditional Image Synthesis with Auxiliary
#'   Classifier GANs, https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.09585 . This compact dense
#'   teaching discriminator differs from the paper's convolutional architecture.
#' @seealso ConditionalGanGenerate(), AuxiliaryClassLoss(), AuxiliaryClassifierGan()
#' @md
#'
`AuxiliaryGanDiscriminate` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_433`, NULL, list(...))
#' Average source-grouped categorical cross entropy against integer class targets.
#'
#' Computes mean(-sum(one_hot(labels,C)*log_softmax(logits),axis=1)), preserving
#' the teaching source's operation grouping. Finite Float32/64 CPU \[N,C\] logits
#' and Int32/64 CPU \[N\] labels in \[0,C) are required, N,C>0; strides are allowed.
#' No clipping, label smoothing, fitting, RNG or optimizer. First/higher logit
