#' AuxiliaryClassLoss(logits, labels)
#' @param logits `Tensor`. Finite floating CPU class logits \[N,C\], N,C>0.
#' @param labels `Tensor`. Integer CPU class targets \[N\], in \[0,C).
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning live scalar mean categorical cross entropy, in logits dtype.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' const auto
#' loss=dm::nn::models::AuxiliaryClassLoss(dm::nn::zeros({2,10}),dm::nn::zeros({2},dm::nn::DType::Int32));
#' // Uniform predictions give log(10), independent of the two target IDs.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid geometry, dtype, targets, product overflow or
#'   nonfinite computation.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Odena, Olah and Shlens (2017), https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.09585 ,
#'   auxiliary class log likelihood, expressed here as a minimized mean loss.
#' @seealso AuxiliaryGanDiscriminate(), AuxiliaryClassifierGan()
#' @md
#'
`AuxiliaryClassLoss` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_434`, NULL, list(...))
#' Evaluate a conditional generator and image-only auxiliary discriminator with explicit losses.
#'
#' ConditionalGanGenerate() concatenates noise \[N,Z\] with one-hot labels \[N,C\],
#' then uses hidden tanh H and output sigmoid F. AuxiliaryGanDiscriminate() sees
#' only real or generated coordinates and predicts source plus class. Source
#' objectives come from LogisticGanObjectives(); D minimizes source_D+(CE_real+
#' CE_fake), G minimizes source_G+CE_fake, with unit class weights. The supplied
#' labels condition G and serve as CE targets; they never enter D's forward.
#' Defaults with Z=16 create G four leaves/26736 and D six leaves/25483 values,
#' in hidden/output and hidden/class/source order (each W then b), respectively.
#'
#' All mathematical paths remain live. Select only D parameters for D loss,
#' then recompute through the updated D and select only G parameters for G loss.
#' There is no hidden optimizer, alternating write, fit, noise draw except initial
#' leaf creation, checkpoint, evaluation guard or O(N^2) MMD. Use GanCoarsePixels()
#' and ImqMmd() explicitly for the separate source game diagnostic. Finite signed
#' Float32/64 CPU image/noise matrices and two distinct matching-dtype stores are
#' required; integer labels are discrete. Strides and higher continuous gradients
#' are retained. All input/width checks precede any leaf creation; incompatible
#' existing leaves or nonfinite computed states may fail later. Inputs unchanged,
#' output fields own lifetime; synchronize shared stores. Work O(N*H*(Z+C+F))
#' plus the two O(N*H*(F+C)) discriminator branches; activation storage
#' O(N*(Z+C+H+F)). No claim of convergence or image quality is implied.
#' @usage
#' AuxiliaryClassifierGan(generator, discriminator, image, noise, labels, features = 784, classes = 10, hidden = 32)
#' @param generator `ParameterStore`. Mutable independent floating generator store.
#' @param discriminator `ParameterStore`. Mutable independent floating discriminator store, matching dtype.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Finite signed CPU real matrix \[N,features\], matching dtype.
#' @param noise `Tensor`. Finite signed CPU explicit noise \[N,Z\], N,Z>0, matching dtype.
#' @param labels `Tensor`. Int32/64 CPU \[N\] requested classes and real/fake CE targets, in \[0,classes).
#' @param features `integer`. Positive image/output width F, default 784.
#' @param classes `integer`. Positive class count C, default 10.
#' @param hidden `integer`. Positive tanh hidden width H, default 32.
#' @return `AuxiliaryClassifierGanOutput`: Owning fifteen-field record with live endpoints and separate scalar objectives.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore g(5209),d(5219);
#' const auto
#' out=n::models::AuxiliaryClassifierGan(g,d,n::zeros({2,784}),n::zeros({2,16}),n::zeros({2},n::DType::Int32));
#' const auto dg=n::grad(out.discriminator_loss,d.parameters());
#' // Caller applies dg only to D, then recomputes before differentiating G loss.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs/geometry/products, aliased or mismatched
#'   stores, incompatible leaves or nonfinite computation.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Odena, Olah and Shlens (2017), Conditional Image Synthesis with Auxiliary
#'   Classifier GANs, https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.09585 . This compact MLP teaching
#'   variant uses the non-saturating source G loss, not the paper's architecture.
#' - Goodfellow et al. (2014), Generative Adversarial Networks,
#'   https://arxiv.org/abs/1406.2661 .
#' @seealso ConditionalGanGenerate(), AuxiliaryGanDiscriminate(), AuxiliaryClassLoss(), LogisticGanObjectives()
#' @md
#'
`AuxiliaryClassifierGan` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_435`, NULL, list(...))
#' Generate ordered Gaussian components on a two-dimensional ring with explicit noise seed.
#'
#' Row i uses component i%components at angle 2*pi*(i%components)/components,
#' then adds independent deviation*GaussianNoise coordinates. Centres, noise and
#' addition are computed in Double, using the source expression order; only the
#' final coordinates cast to dtype. Defaults reproduce the compact BiGAN fitting
#' distribution (eight components, radius 2, standard deviation .08), not a real
#' dataset. Rows cycle deterministically through components; there is no random
#' component assignment or shuffling. Counts need not divide components, so the
#' first rows get any remainder. Zero radius/deviation and one component are valid.
#'
#' Requires positive rows/components and representable rows*2, finite nonnegative radius
#' and deviation, and Float32/64 dtype. Every result is finite, owning, contiguous
#' CPU\[rows,2\], without gradients or retained RNG state; repeated calls with equal
#' arguments repeat bits. No fitting, train/test partition, external assets or
#' shared mutable state. O(rows) work/storage. Standard allocation failures can
#' propagate; finite Double or Float32 overflow is rejected, without clipping.
#' @usage
#' GaussianRingPoints(rows, seed = 5507, components = 8, radius = 2.0, deviation = 0.080000000000000002, dtype = "Float32")
#' @param rows `integer`. Positive sample count, with representable rows*2.
#' @param seed `integer`. Explicit uint32 Gaussian seed, default 5507; no global RNG is consumed.
#' @param components `integer`. Positive component count, default 8; component i%components.
#' @param radius `numeric`. Finite nonnegative ring radius in coordinate units, default 2.
#' @param deviation `numeric`. Finite nonnegative per-coordinate Gaussian standard deviation, default .08.
#' @param dtype `character (DType)`. Float32 default, or Float64; only final coordinates are cast.
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning detached finite CPU\[rows,2\] ordered point coordinates.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' const auto points=dm::nn::models::GaussianRingPoints(4,5507,4,2.,0.);
#' // Four ordered centres are approximately(2,0),(0,2),(-2,0),(0,-2).
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid dimensions, options, dtype or computed nonfinite
#'   coordinates.
#' @references - The migrated compact BiGAN experiment's ordered ring, not a published benchmark.
#'   GaussianNoise() supplies the canonical seeded Box-Muller stream.
#' @seealso GaussianNoise(), BidirectionalGan()
#' @md
#'
`GaussianRingPoints` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_436`, NULL, list(...))
#' Map signed coordinates through the source hidden-tanh/output-linear network.
#'
#' Delegates the canonical AaeDecode() tanh/linear computation without a sigmoid,
#' interpreting its raw outputs as coordinates. Input width I is inferred.
