#' order, with ordinary dense Glorot/zero initialization. I=O=2,H=16 gives four
#' leaves/82 values. Finite signed Float32/64 CPU\[N,I\] input matches store dtype;
#' positive axes and strides preserve all first/higher continuous paths. No
#' encoder, discriminator, fit, optimizer, random input draw or target is hidden.
#' Outputs are unbounded coordinates, not pixel probabilities or posterior samples.
#' Input checks precede creation; incompatible leaves/nonfinite computed output
#' may fail later. Input unchanged, output owns lifetime. O(N*H*(I+O)) work,
#' O(N*(H+O)) activations, plus host validation; synchronize shared mutable stores.
#' @usage
#' BiganMap(parameters, input, output = 2, hidden = 16)
#' @param parameters `ParameterStore`. Mutable matching floating map store; only missing leaves are initialized.
#' @param input `Tensor`. Finite signed floating CPU\[N,I\], N,I>0, matching store dtype.
#' @param output `integer`. Positive output-coordinate width O, default 2.
#' @param hidden `integer`. Positive hidden tanh width H, default 16.
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning live unbounded CPU\[N,output\] coordinates in input dtype.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' dm::nn::ParameterStore g(6007);
#' const auto points=dm::nn::models::BiganMap(g,dm::nn::zeros({3,2}));
#' // points is [3,2]; no encoder or image enters this prior-only generation.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid input/widths/products, incompatible leaves or
#'   nonfinite computation.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Donahue, Krähenbühl and Darrell (2016/2017), Adversarial Feature Learning,
#'   https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.09782 . This is the compact teaching MLP,
#'   not the paper's image-model architecture or benchmark.
#' @seealso AaeDecode(), BiganJointScore(), BidirectionalGan()
#' @md
#'
`BiganMap` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_437`, NULL, list(...))
#' Score supplied data/code pairs jointly, without pair labels or hidden encoding.
#'
#' Concatenates image\[N,F\],code\[N,Z\] in that order and delegates the canonical
#' tanh/linear AaeDecode() with one raw output. Creates hidden/W\[F+Z,H\],b\[H\],
#' output/W\[H,1\],b\[1\] in source order; F=Z=2,H=16 gives 97 values/four leaves.
#' Finite signed Float32/64 CPU pairs match row counts and store dtype; strides
#' and all first/higher paths through both pair parts remain live. Positive means
#' the (data,encoded-data) source, not a class probability. No E/G forward, target,
#' sigmoid, loss, fit or update is hidden. Checks precede creation; incompatible
#' leaves or nonfinite output may fail later. Inputs unchanged; output owns
#' lifetime. O(N*H*(F+Z)) work, O(N*(F+Z+H)) activations and host validation;
#' synchronize shared stores.
#' @usage
#' BiganJointScore(discriminator, image, code, hidden = 16)
#' @param discriminator `ParameterStore`. Mutable floating joint-discriminator store.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Finite signed CPU\[N,F\] data coordinates, N,F>0, matching dtype.
#' @param code `Tensor`. Finite signed CPU\[N,Z\] code coordinates, same N and dtype, Z>0.
#' @param hidden `integer`. Positive tanh hidden width H, default 16.
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning live raw source logits\[N,1\], depending on both supplied pair parts.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' dm::nn::ParameterStore d(6029);
#' const auto score=dm::nn::models::BiganJointScore(d,dm::nn::ones({3,2}),dm::nn::zeros({3,2}));
#' // score is [3,1]; both pair coordinates are explicit, with no encoder call.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid pairs/widths/products, incompatible leaves or
#'   nonfinite computation.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Donahue et al. (2016/2017), https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.09782 .
#' - Dumoulin et al. (2016/2017), Adversarially Learned Inference,
#'   https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.00704 . Both discriminate joint data/code sources.
#' @seealso BiganMap(), LogisticGanObjectives(), BidirectionalGan()
#' @md
#'
`BiganJointScore` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_438`, NULL, list(...))
#' Evaluate explicit data/prior joint sources and separate bidirectional adversarial losses.
#'
#' G maps prior\[M,Z\] through hidden tanh H to linear coordinates F; E maps data
#' \[N,F\] through the same architecture to Z. D scores (image,E(image)) and
#' (G(prior),prior), concatenating data before code. Stores are separate; each
#' creates hidden/W,b then output/W,b, in G,E,D order. F=Z=2,H=16 gives
#' G82+E82+D97=261 values in 12 leaves. Widths F/Z are inferred from inputs.
#' The reusable tanh/linear computation is AaeDecode(), with no sigmoid.
#'
#' D minimizes mean softplus(-real_score)+mean softplus(fake_score). E/G minimize
#' mean softplus(real_score)+mean softplus(-fake_score), the source's explicit
#' non-saturating reversed-source objective. Each pool is averaged separately;
#' N and M may differ. Reconstruction G(E(image)) and latent cycle E(G(prior))
#' stay live diagnostics, with no reconstruction/cycle term in either fit loss.
#' There is no inference-likelihood, learned inverse or convergence guarantee.
#'
#' All mathematical paths remain live. Caller selects D leaves, writes D,
#' recomputes for E, writes E, then recomputes for G. With D fixed, E's write
#' leaves G's loss partial unchanged because the two joint branches separate.
#' No optimizer, fit loop, noise draw except missing-leaf initialization, clipping,
#' target label, implicit freeze, evaluation guard or checkpoint is hidden.
#' All three distinct stores and finite signed CPU inputs share Float32/64 dtype.
#' Strides and higher continuous paths are preserved. All input/geometry checks
#' precede creation; incompatible leaves or nonfinite computed states may fail
#' later. Inputs unchanged; owning outputs retain lifetime. Work
#' O((N+M)*H*(F+Z)), including the two cycle diagnostics; activation storage
#' O((N+M)*(F+Z+H)). Synchronize callers sharing mutable stores.
#' @usage
#' BidirectionalGan(generator, encoder, discriminator, image, prior, hidden = 16)
#' @param generator `ParameterStore`. Mutable independent floating generator store G.
#' @param encoder `ParameterStore`. Mutable independent floating encoder store E, matching G dtype.
#' @param discriminator `ParameterStore`. Mutable independent floating joint store D, matching G dtype.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Finite signed CPU data\[N,F\], N,F>0, matching store dtype.
#' @param prior `Tensor`. Finite signed CPU prior\[M,Z\], M,Z>0, matching store dtype.
#' @param hidden `integer`. Positive tanh width H, default 16.
#' @return `BiganOutput`: Owning eight-field BiganOutput, with separate D and E/G scalar objectives.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore g(6007),e(6011),d(6029);
#' const auto out=n::models::BidirectionalGan(g,e,d,n::ones({2,2}),n::zeros({2,2}));
#' const auto dd=n::grad(out.discriminator_loss,d.parameters());
#' // Caller writes dd only to D, then recomputes the next selected-group loss.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs/dimensions/products, aliased or mismatched
#'   stores, incompatible leaves or nonfinite computation.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Donahue, Krähenbühl and Darrell (2016/2017), Adversarial Feature Learning,
#'   https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.09782 .
#' - Dumoulin et al. (2016/2017), Adversarially Learned Inference,
#'   https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.00704 . This compact deterministic MLP uses
#'   the teaching source's reversed-source non-saturating objective and schedule,
#'   not either paper's image benchmark or idealized optimum assumptions.
#' @seealso BiganMap(), BiganJointScore(), LogisticGanObjectives(), GaussianRingPoints()
#' @md
#'
`BidirectionalGan` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_439`, NULL, list(...))
#' Compute source-grouped least-squares GAN losses with a=0 and b=c=1.
#'
#' D=.5*(mean((real-1)^2)+mean(fake^2)); G=.5*mean((fake-1)^2).
#' The half factor follows the sum of pool means in D, preserving source
#' Float32 operation grouping. Raw scores are unbounded, not probabilities;
#' no sigmoid, clipping, cross entropy, smoothing or fitted threshold is applied.
#' Finite same-dtype Float32/64 CPU\[N,1\]/\[M,1\] scores allow unequal positive
#' pool sizes and strides. All applicable first/higher continuous paths remain
#' live; G depends only on fake. Inputs unchanged, scalar outputs own lifetime.
#' O(N+M) work/storage plus host validation; no global state or mutation. Finite
#' inputs whose square/reduction overflows are rejected rather than repaired.
#' @usage
#' LeastSquaresGanObjectives(real, fake)
#' @param real `Tensor`. Finite floating CPU real-score column\[N,1\], N>0.
#' @param fake `Tensor`. Finite matching floating CPU fake-score column\[M,1\], M>0.
#' @return `DenseGanLoss`: Owning DenseGanLoss in input dtype, with the two explicit scalar objectives.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' const auto
#' loss=dm::nn::models::LeastSquaresGanObjectives(dm::nn::zeros({2,1}),dm::nn::zeros({3,1}));
#' // D=.5 and G=.5, without a sigmoid on either score pool.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid pools/dtypes/values or nonfinite computed losses.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Mao et al. (2017), Least Squares Generative Adversarial Networks,
#'   https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.04076 , equation9 (0/1 coding), not the
#'   a=-1,b=1,c=0 parameterization used for the Pearson-divergence derivation.
#' @seealso HingeGanObjectives(), LogisticGanObjectives(), DenseGan()
#' @md
#'
`LeastSquaresGanObjectives` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_440`, NULL, list(...))
#' Compute positive D margin hinges and an unhinged negative-mean G objective.
#'
#' D=mean(relu(1-real))+mean(relu(1+fake)); G=-mean(fake). Scores are raw,
#' unbounded and need not lie in\[-1,1\]; G loss may be negative. D's real-score
#' derivative is -1/N for real<1 and0 otherwise; fake derivative is1/M for
#' fake>-1 and0 otherwise. Exact margins real=1/fake=-1 use the native ReLU
#' zero subgradient. G derivative remains -1/M at every score, including the
#' margins: there is no hinge or sigmoid on G. First/higher paths are retained
#' away from D's kinks; a classical second derivative at the kink is undefined.
#' Finite matching Float32/64 CPU\[N,1\]/\[M,1\] pools may differ in positive size
#' and have strides. No clipping, spectral normalization, fit, optimizer or
#' threshold is hidden. Inputs unchanged, outputs own lifetime. O(N+M)
#' work/storage plus host validation; synchronize external mutation. Computed
#' nonfinite losses are rejected without repair.
#' @usage
#' HingeGanObjectives(real, fake)
#' @param real `Tensor`. Finite floating CPU real scores\[N,1\], N>0.
#' @param fake `Tensor`. Finite matching floating CPU fake scores\[M,1\], M>0.
#' @return `DenseGanLoss`: Owning live DenseGanLoss with separate scalar D/G losses in input dtype.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' const auto loss=dm::nn::models::HingeGanObjectives(dm::nn::ones({2,1}),dm::nn::full({3,1},-1.));
#' // D=0 at both margins, G=1; G's fake-score derivative is still -1/3.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid pools/dtypes/values or nonfinite computation.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Miyato et al. (2018), Spectral Normalization for Generative Adversarial
#'   Networks, https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.05957 , equations16-17, with D's
#'   maximized negative hinge expressed as a minimized positive loss. This
#'   function supplies the loss only, without the paper's spectral normalization.
#' @seealso LeastSquaresGanObjectives(), LogisticGanObjectives(), DenseGan()
#' @md
#'
`HingeGanObjectives` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_441`, NULL, list(...))
#' Generate sigmoid data coordinates from explicit noise through the source dense MLP.
#'
#' Reuses canonical AaeDecode() tanh/linear computation and applies sigmoid.
#' Noise width Z is inferred. Creates hidden/W\[Z,H\],b\[H\],output/W\[H,F\],b\[F\]
#' in that order with dense Glorot/zero initialization; Z16,H32,F784 creates
#' four leaves/26416 values. Finite signed Float32/64 CPU\[M,Z\] matches store
#' dtype; positive axes and strides preserve first/higher continuous paths.
#' No data, class, D, optimizer, fitting or input RNG draw is hidden. Validation
#' precedes leaves; incompatible leaves/nonfinite output may fail later. Input
#' unchanged; output owns lifetime. O(M*H*(Z+F)) work, O(M*(H+F)) activations
#' plus host validation; synchronize shared stores.
#' @usage
#' MlpGanGenerate(generator, noise, features = 784, hidden = 32)
#' @param generator `ParameterStore`. Mutable matching floating generator store.
#' @param noise `Tensor`. Finite signed CPU\[M,Z\] explicit codes, M,Z>0, matching dtype.
#' @param features `integer`. Positive output width F, default784.
#' @param hidden `integer`. Positive hidden tanh width H, default32.
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning live sigmoid coordinates\[M,F\], not random pixel draws.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' dm::nn::ParameterStore g(5407);
#' const auto image=dm::nn::models::MlpGanGenerate(g,dm::nn::zeros({2,16}));
#' // image is[2,784]; G has four leaves/26416 values and requires no class label.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs/widths/products, incompatible leaves or
#'   nonfinite output.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - The migrated compact dense teaching architecture; AaeDecode() supplies its
#'   shared tanh/linear implementation, not a paper's convolutional benchmark.
#' @seealso MlpGanDiscriminate(), DenseGan(), ConditionalGanGenerate()
#' @md
#'
`MlpGanGenerate` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_442`, NULL, list(...))
#' Predict an unbounded source score from images alone with the source tanh/linear MLP.
#'
#' Reuses AaeDecode() with output width1. Creates hidden/W\[F,H\],b\[H\],
#' output/W\[H,1\],b\[1\] in that order; F784,H32 gives four leaves/25153 values.
#' Finite signed Float32/64 CPU\[N,F\] matches store dtype; positive axes and
#' strides retain input/parameter first/higher paths. No class, G, sigmoid,
#' fit, optimizer or target is hidden. Input checks precede leaves; incompatible
#' leaves/nonfinite output may fail later. Input unchanged; owning\[N,1\] output.
#' O(N*H*F) work, O(N*H) activations plus host validation; synchronize stores.
#' @usage
#' MlpGanDiscriminate(discriminator, image, features = 784, hidden = 32)
#' @param discriminator `ParameterStore`. Mutable matching floating source-score store.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Finite signed CPU\[N,features\], N>0, matching store dtype.
#' @param features `integer`. Positive input width F, default784.
#' @param hidden `integer`. Positive hidden tanh width H, default32.
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning live raw scores\[N,1\], without a probability interpretation.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' dm::nn::ParameterStore d(5413);
#' const auto score=dm::nn::models::MlpGanDiscriminate(d,dm::nn::zeros({2,784}));
#' // score is[2,1]; no sigmoid, class condition or generated input is supplied.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs/widths/products, incompatible leaves or
#'   nonfinite computation.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - The migrated compact teaching MLP; canonical AaeDecode() supplies its raw
#'   tanh/linear computation. Scores are not calibrated class probabilities.
#' @seealso MlpGanGenerate(), DenseGan(), ConditionalGanDiscriminate()
#' @md
#'
`MlpGanDiscriminate` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_443`, NULL, list(...))
#' Evaluate explicit unconditional dense-GAN data/noise with a chosen raw-source objective.
#'
#' MlpGanGenerate() maps noise\[M,Z\] to sigmoid coordinates F; the same
#' MlpGanDiscriminate() scores real\[N,F\] and fake\[M,F\]. Separate G/D stores
#' create hidden/output W,b in source order, using dense Glorot/zero initialization.
#' Defaults Z16,H32,F784 give G26416+D25153=51569 values in eight leaves.
#' Positive N/M may differ; each loss averages its own pool. Labels are absent.
#'
#' Logistic selects LogisticGanObjectives(); LeastSquares selects a0,b=c1;
#' Hinge selects positive D margins and unhinged -mean(fake). Raw scores are
#' returned for every objective; any logistic reporting sigmoid is explicit.
#' All mathematical paths stay live, with hinge derivatives piecewise-defined
#' and zero ReLU subgradient at its margins. Caller selects only D leaves,
#' writes D, recomputes through the updated D and selects only G leaves. No
#' optimizer, fitting, noise draw except initial leaf creation, implicit freeze,
#' checkpoint or O(N^2) diagnostic is hidden. Use GanCoarsePixels()/ImqMmd()
#' explicitly for the source game diagnostic, without a quality guarantee.
#'
#' Distinct stores and finite signed CPU inputs share Float32/64 dtype; strides
#' and applicable higher paths are retained. All input/options checks precede
#' leaves; incompatible leaves/nonfinite computed output may fail later. Inputs
#' unchanged, outputs own lifetime. Work O((N+M)*H*F+M*H*Z), activation storage
#' O((N+M)*(F+H)+M*Z), plus host validation. Synchronize shared stores.
#' @usage
#' DenseGan(generator, discriminator, image, noise, objective, features = 784, hidden = 32)
#' @param generator `ParameterStore`. Mutable independent floating generator store G.
#' @param discriminator `ParameterStore`. Mutable independent floating score store D, matching G dtype.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Finite signed CPU\[N,features\] real coordinates, N>0, matching dtype.
#' @param noise `Tensor`. Finite signed CPU\[M,Z\] explicit codes, M,Z>0, matching dtype.
#' @param objective `character (DenseGanObjective)`. Required valid DenseGanObjective; no default objective is selected.
#' @param features `integer`. Positive image/output width F, default784.
#' @param hidden `integer`. Positive hidden tanh width H, default32.
#' @return `DenseGanOutput`: Owning DenseGanOutput with raw scores and two selected scalar losses.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore g(5701),d(5711);
#' const auto
#' out=n::models::DenseGan(g,d,n::zeros({2,784}),n::zeros({2,16}),n::models::DenseGanObjective::Hinge);
#' const auto dd=n::grad(out.discriminator_loss,d.parameters());
#' // Apply dd only to D, then recompute before differentiating G's loss.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs/geometry/objective, aliased or mismatched
#'   stores, incompatible leaves or nonfinite computation.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Mao et al. (2017), https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.04076 , equation9.
#' - Miyato et al. (2018), https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.05957 , equations16-17.
#'   These compact teaching models preserve source losses, not paper architectures,
#'   spectral normalization, benchmark results or convergence claims.
#' @seealso LeastSquaresGanObjectives(), HingeGanObjectives(), LogisticGanObjectives(), ConditionalGan()
#' @md
#'
`DenseGan` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_444`, NULL, list(...))
#' Score image/class pairs with one-hot conditioning on the discriminator input.
#'
#' Concatenates image\[N,F\] then one-hot labels\[N,C\] and delegates the canonical
#' MlpGanDiscriminate() tanh/linear map. Creates hidden/W\[F+C,H\],b\[H\],
#' output/W\[H,1\],b\[1\] in source order. F784,C10,H32 creates four leaves/25473
#' values. Both image and discrete class condition enter D; there is no auxiliary
#' classifier, target CE, hidden G/E call, sigmoid, fit or optimizer. Finite signed
#' Float32/64 CPU images match store dtype, with positive axes and Int32/64
#' labels in\[0,C). Strides and applicable higher continuous image/weight paths
#' stay live; labels are discrete. All input checks precede leaves; incompatible
#' leaves/nonfinite output may fail later. Inputs unchanged; output owns lifetime.
#' O(N*H*(F+C)) work, O(N*(F+C+H)) activations plus host validation; synchronize
#' callers sharing a store. Raw scores are unbounded source logits.
#' @usage
#' ConditionalGanDiscriminate(discriminator, image, labels, features = 784, classes = 10, hidden = 32)
#' @param discriminator `ParameterStore`. Mutable matching floating conditional source store.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Finite signed CPU\[N,features\], N>0, matching store dtype.
#' @param labels `Tensor`. Int32/64 CPU\[N\] requested classes in\[0,classes).
#' @param features `integer`. Positive input width F, default784.
#' @param classes `integer`. Positive class count C, default10.
#' @param hidden `integer`. Positive hidden tanh width H, default32.
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning live conditional source logits\[N,1\], without a class prediction.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore d(5113);
#' const auto
#' score=n::models::ConditionalGanDiscriminate(d,n::zeros({2,784}),n::zeros({2},n::DType::Int32));
#' // score is[2,1]; changing only labels can change real-image source predictions.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs/labels/dimensions/products, incompatible leaves
#'   or nonfinite computation.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Mirza and Osindero (2014), Conditional Generative Adversarial Nets,
#'   https://arxiv.org/abs/1411.1784 . Both networks are conditioned here;
#'   this compact dense source architecture is not a reproduced paper benchmark.
#' @seealso ConditionalGanGenerate(), ConditionalGan(), AuxiliaryGanDiscriminate()
#' @md
#'
`ConditionalGanDiscriminate` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_445`, NULL, list(...))
#' Evaluate a class-conditioned generator and discriminator with explicit logistic losses.
#'
#' ConditionalGanGenerate() concatenates noise\[N,Z\] with one-hot classes\[N,C\],
#' then hidden tanh H/output sigmoid F. ConditionalGanDiscriminate() concatenates
#' image F with the same class condition and predicts one raw source logit. Both
#' real and generated D branches consume labels; there is no auxiliary class
#' head or categorical CE. Default Z16,C10,H32,F784 creates G26736+D25473=52209
#' values in eight leaves, each store's hidden then output W,b, in G,D order.
#' Source objectives are LogisticGanObjectives(), preserving stable softplus(-x)
#' grouping and non-saturating G. All mathematical paths remain live: select
#' only D leaves, write D, recompute through the updated D, then select G leaves.
#'
#' Requires distinct stores and finite signed CPU image\[N,F\]/noise\[N,Z\] sharing
#' Float32/64 dtype; the single Int32/64\[N\] class vector conditions both pools,
#' so row counts must match. Positive widths/products, strides and applicable
#' higher continuous paths are supported; labels are discrete. No noise draw
#' except initial leaf creation, optimizer, fitting, implicit freeze, evaluation
#' guard, checkpoint or O(N^2) MMD is hidden. Source sigmoid probabilities are
#' reporting fields, not a quality or requested-class accuracy score. All input
#' checks precede leaf creation; incompatible leaves/nonfinite output may fail
#' later. Inputs unchanged, outputs own lifetime. Work O(N*H*(Z+C+F)); activation
#' storage O(N*(Z+C+F+H)), plus host validation. Synchronize shared stores.
#' @usage
#' ConditionalGan(generator, discriminator, image, noise, labels, features = 784, classes = 10, hidden = 32)
#' @param generator `ParameterStore`. Mutable independent floating conditional generator store.
#' @param discriminator `ParameterStore`. Mutable independent floating conditional D store, matching G dtype.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Finite signed CPU\[N,features\] real coordinates, N>0, matching dtype.
#' @param noise `Tensor`. Finite signed CPU\[N,Z\] explicit codes, Z>0, matching dtype.
#' @param labels `Tensor`. Int32/64 CPU\[N\] classes in\[0,classes), supplied to both G and D.
#' @param features `integer`. Positive image/output width F, default784.
#' @param classes `integer`. Positive discrete class count C, default10.
#' @param hidden `integer`. Positive hidden tanh width H, default32.
#' @return `ConditionalGanOutput`: Owning seven-field ConditionalGanOutput with two explicit scalar objectives.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore g(5101),d(5113);
#' const auto
#' out=n::models::ConditionalGan(g,d,n::zeros({2,784}),n::zeros({2,16}),n::zeros({2},n::DType::Int32));
#' const auto dd=n::grad(out.discriminator_loss,d.parameters());
#' // Caller writes only D, then recomputes before selecting G's gradient.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs/options/products, aliased or mismatched stores,
#'   incompatible leaves or nonfinite computation.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Mirza and Osindero (2014), Conditional Generative Adversarial Nets,
#'   https://arxiv.org/abs/1411.1784 . This compact dense teaching model uses
#'   non-saturating logistic G loss and its own explicit source schedule.
#' @seealso ConditionalGanGenerate(), ConditionalGanDiscriminate(), LogisticGanObjectives(), DenseGan()
#' @md
#'
`ConditionalGan` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_446`, NULL, list(...))
#' Sample row-interleaved uniform categorical and continuous InfoGAN prior codes.
#'
#' A local std::mt19937(seed) supplies an accepted category word v below
#' floor(2^32/C)*C, then U continuous words, row by row. category=v modulo C.
#' Each continuous value is computed in Double as2*((word+.5)/2^32)-1,
#' then cast once to dtype. Float32 rounding can attain-1 or1; values therefore
#' lie in\[-1,1\]. Defaults C10/U2 reproduce the source stream including its
#' rejection limit4294967290. This differs from separately seeded draws for
#' each component. Category frequencies are random, not forced balanced.
#' All returned tensors own lifetime and are detached. No global RNG, data,
#' fitting, optimizer or mutable shared state is accessed; independent calls
#' are reentrant. Work/storage O(N*(U+1)), with rejection sampling of categories.
#' @usage
#' InfoPrior(rows, seed, classes = 10, continuous = 2, dtype = "Float32")
#' @param rows `integer`. Positive sample count N with representable output products.
#' @param seed `integer`. Explicit uint32 local engine seed; no global seed is consumed.
#' @param classes `integer`. Cardinality C in\[1,INT32_MAX\], default10, matching Int32 output IDs.
#' @param continuous `integer`. Positive continuous width U, default2.
#' @param dtype `character (DType)`. Float32(default) or Float64 continuous output; raw stays Float64.
#' @return `InfoCodes`: Owning InfoCodes with category\[N\],continuous\[N,U\],raw\[N,U+1\].
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' const auto a=dm::nn::models::InfoPrior(5,5382);
#' const auto b=dm::nn::models::InfoPrior(5,5382);
#' // All three a/b fields are bit exact, with no other random stream affected.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid counts, dtype, axes or int64 products.
#' * `std::length_error`: If standard output containers cannot represent the requested capacity.
#' * `std::bad_alloc`: If output storage cannot be allocated.
#' @references - Chen et al. (2016), InfoGAN, https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.03657, section7.2.
#'   The explicit row-wise engine, raw audit words and rejection protocol follow
#'   the migrated teaching source rather than prescribing the paper's RNG.
#' @seealso MidpointUniformNoise(), InfoGanGenerate(), InfoCodes
#' @md
#'
`InfoPrior` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_447`, NULL, list(...))
#' Generate sigmoid pixels from explicit noise and generated-prior codes only.
#'
#' Concatenates(noise\[M,Z\],onehot(category,C),continuous\[M,U\]) in that order
#' and reuses MlpGanGenerate(). All axes are positive; finite signed Float32/64
#' CPU noise and unit-interval continuous codes match the store dtype, while
#' categories are Int32/64\[M\] in\[0,C). Strides and continuous first/higher paths
#' are retained. No image, real digit label, D/Q, loss, fit or input RNG is hidden.
#' Hidden/output W,b creation with Z16,C10,U2,H32,F784 gives26800 values/four
#' leaves. Input/geometry checks precede leaves; incompatible existing leaves
#' or nonfinite output may fail later. Output owns lifetime, inputs unchanged.
#' Work O(M*H*(Z+C+U+F)), storage O(M*(Z+C+U+H+F)); synchronize shared stores.
#' @usage
#' InfoGanGenerate(generator, noise, category, continuous, features = 784, classes = 10, hidden = 32)
#' @param generator `ParameterStore`. Mutable floating G store.
#' @param noise `Tensor`. Finite matching CPU\[M,Z\], M,Z>0.
#' @param category `Tensor`. Integer generated categories\[M\], not supervised digit labels.
#' @param continuous `Tensor`. Finite matching CPU\[M,U\] in\[-1,1\], U>0.
#' @param features `integer`. Positive sigmoid output width F, default784.
#' @param classes `integer`. Positive categorical cardinality C, default10.
#' @param hidden `integer`. Positive hidden tanh width H, default32.
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning live generated coordinates\[M,F\].
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore g(5303);const auto c=n::models::InfoPrior(3,5351);
#' const auto image=n::models::InfoGanGenerate(g,n::zeros({3,16}),c.category,c.continuous);
#' // image:[3,784]; no training image or recognizer enters this call.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid codes/geometry/dtypes, incompatible leaves or
#'   nonfinite computation.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Chen et al. (2016), InfoGAN, https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.03657, latent-code input.
#'   This source uses a compact dense generator rather than the paper's convolutional model.
#' @seealso MlpGanGenerate(), InfoPrior(), InfoGan()
#' @md
#'
`InfoGanGenerate` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_448`, NULL, list(...))
#' Recognize generated-prior codes from an image alone with an independent tanh Q network.
#'
#' Hidden tanh H feeds categorical logits C then continuous means U. Parameter
#' creation order is hidden/W,b, category/W,b, continuous/W,b. Defaults give
#' 25516 values/six leaves. Q shares no parameters with D; no target/noise/code
#' is an input. Finite signed Float32/64 CPU\[N,F\] matches the store dtype;
#' strides and continuous first/higher paths remain live. Positive geometry
#' validates before leaves; incompatible existing leaves/nonfinite output may
#' fail later. Inputs unchanged; outputs own lifetime. Work O(N*H*(F+C+U)),
#' storage O(N*(H+C+U)); synchronize callers sharing a mutable store.
#' @usage
#' InfoGanRecognize(recognizer, image, features = 784, classes = 10, continuous = 2, hidden = 32)
#' @param recognizer `ParameterStore`. Mutable matching floating Q store, separate from D.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Finite signed CPU\[N,F\], N>0, matching store dtype.
#' @param features `integer`. Positive image width F, default784.
#' @param classes `integer`. Positive categorical width C, default10.
#' @param continuous `integer`. Positive linear mean width U, default2.
#' @param hidden `integer`. Positive shared tanh width H, default32.
#' @return `InfoRecognition`: Owning InfoRecognition with logits,softmax probability and means.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' dm::nn::ParameterStore q(5317);
#' const auto out=dm::nn::models::InfoGanRecognize(q,dm::nn::ones({3,784}));
#' // No original code, category target, G or D is consulted.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs/geometry, incompatible leaves or nonfinite
#'   computation.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Chen et al. (2016), InfoGAN, https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.03657, section6.
#'   This teaching variant uses a separate Q rather than a shared D/Q trunk.
#' @seealso InfoGanRecognitionLoss(), InfoGan(), AuxiliaryGanDiscriminate()
#' @md
#'
`InfoGanRecognize` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_449`, NULL, list(...))
#' Compute generated-code recognition NLL and its fixed-prior variational information bound.
#'
#' Reuses AuxiliaryClassLoss(logits,category). Continuous NLL is
#' .5*mean(sum((target-mean)^2,axis1))+.5*U*log(2*pi), preserving the source
#' grouping and log(2*pi) constant at U2. R=category NLL+continuous NLL;
#' lower_bound=(log(C)+U*log(2))-R. Priors are assumed independent uniform
#' categories and continuous\[-1,1\] coordinates; values alone cannot establish
#' that sampling assumption. Unit recognition variance is fixed, not fitted.
#' Q.probability is not consumed or validated. Finite Float32/64 CPU logits\[N,C\],
#' mean/target\[N,U\] share dtype and positive N,C,U; Int32/64 category\[N\] is
#' in\[0,C). Target continuous codes lie in\[-1,1\]. Strides and first/higher paths
#' through logits,mean and target remain live; categories are discrete.
#' Inputs unchanged; scalar outputs own lifetime. No fit, RNG, optimizer or
#' posterior sampler. Work/storage O(N*(C+U)); synchronize external mutation.
#' Finite inputs whose squared residual/reduction overflows are rejected.
#' @usage
#' InfoGanRecognitionLoss(prediction, category, continuous)
#' @param prediction `InfoRecognition`. Q logits and means; probability convenience field is unused.
#' @param category `Tensor`. Generated-prior integer targets\[N\], not supervised image labels.
#' @param continuous `Tensor`. Matching floating continuous-prior targets\[N,U\] in\[-1,1\].
#' @return `InfoRecognitionLoss`: Owning four-field InfoRecognitionLoss in computation dtype.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::models::InfoRecognition q{n::zeros({2,2}),{},n::zeros({2,1})};
#' const auto
#' loss=n::models::InfoGanRecognitionLoss(q,n::tensor({0,1},{2},n::DType::Int64),n::tensor({-1,1},{2,1}));
#' // categorical=log2, continuous=(1+log(2*pi))/2; lower_bound about-.72579.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid shapes/dtypes/ranges or nonfinite computation.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Chen et al. (2016), InfoGAN, https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.03657, equation5.
#'   This source fixes Gaussian recognition variance at one and uses a separate Q.
#' @seealso AuxiliaryClassLoss(), InfoGanRecognize(), InfoGan()
#' @md
#'
`InfoGanRecognitionLoss` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_450`, NULL, list(...))
#' Evaluate explicit InfoGAN inputs with separate G,D,Q stores and caller-owned writes.
#'
#' InfoGanGenerate() maps(noise,category,continuous) to sigmoid pixels;
#' MlpGanDiscriminate() scores real and fake images alone; InfoGanRecognize()
#' feeds only fake images to independent Q. D minimizes LogisticGanObjectives().
#' Q minimizes R=InfoGanRecognitionLoss().total. G minimizes non-saturating
#' source loss+R with weight1; no prior entropy constant is subtracted from G.
#' The diagnostic bound is separately Hprior-R and may be negative.
#' Defaults Z16,C10,U2,H32,F784 give G26800+D25153+Q25516=77469 values in
#' fourteen leaves, each store creating hidden before heads; Q category before
#' continuous. Positive real N/fake M may differ. Finite signed Float32/64 CPU
#' images/noise/continuous codes match all three distinct stores; Int32/64\[M\]
#' categories are generated-prior IDs in\[0,C), continuous\[M,U\] lies in\[-1,1\].
#' Strides and applicable first/higher continuous paths remain live. Continuous
#' input is also a recognition target, giving both direct and mapped paths.
#' All user input/options/geometry checks precede leaves; incompatible existing
#' leaves or computed nonfinite values can fail later. Inputs unchanged, fields
#' own lifetime. Synchronize shared stores. Caller recomputes D then Q then G
#' after each selected-store write using independent optimizer states. There is
#' no hidden RNG, fit, freeze, optimizer, step, checkpoint, real-label supervision
#' or MMD. Work O(M*H*(Z+C+U+F)+(N+M)*H*F+M*H*(F+C+U)); storage follows
#' dense activations plus host validation.
#' @usage
#' InfoGan(generator, discriminator, recognizer, image, noise, category, continuous, features = 784, classes = 10, hidden = 32)
#' @param generator `ParameterStore`. Mutable floating G store.
#' @param discriminator `ParameterStore`. Distinct matching floating image-only D store.
#' @param recognizer `ParameterStore`. Third distinct matching floating image-only Q store.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Finite matching signed CPU\[N,F\] real coordinates, N>0.
#' @param noise `Tensor`. Finite matching signed CPU\[M,Z\] explicit noise, M,Z>0.
#' @param category `Tensor`. Int32/64 CPU\[M\] generated-prior IDs in\[0,C).
#' @param continuous `Tensor`. Matching floating CPU\[M,U\] prior/recognition targets in\[-1,1\], U>0.
#' @param features `integer`. Positive image/output width F, default784.
#' @param classes `integer`. Positive categorical cardinality C, default10.
#' @param hidden `integer`. Positive tanh width H for each independent network, default32.
#' @return `InfoGanOutput`: Owning fifteen-field InfoGanOutput with live endpoints and selected objectives.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore g(5303),d(5309),q(5317);const auto c=n::models::InfoPrior(2,5382);
#' const auto
#' out=n::models::InfoGan(g,d,q,n::zeros({2,784}),n::zeros({2,16}),c.category,c.continuous); const
#' auto dq=n::grad(out.recognition_loss,q.parameters());
#' // Caller applies dq only to Q and recomputes before its next selected G step.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs/geometry, aliased/mismatched stores,
#'   incompatible leaves or nonfinite computation.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Chen, Duan, Houthooft, Schulman, Sutskever and Abbeel (2016), InfoGAN:
#'   Interpretable Representation Learning by Information Maximizing Generative
#'   Adversarial Nets, https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.03657, equations5-6.
#'   The migrated teaching variant has a separate unit-variance Q and explicit D-Q-G schedule.
#' @seealso InfoPrior(), InfoGanGenerate(), InfoGanRecognize(), InfoGanRecognitionLoss()
#' @md
#'
`InfoGan` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_451`, NULL, list(...))
#' Advance detached spectral columns without normalizing the supplied initial direction.
#'
#' Flatten W to M\[in,out\]. Each ordered iteration is v=M*u/sqrt(sum((M*u)^2)+epsilon),
#' then u=M^T*v/sqrt(sum((M^T*v)^2)+epsilon). Uses division and sqrt, not rsqrt;
#' epsilon is added to the squared norm. Default epsilon is double(1e-12f),
#' preserving the Float32-rounded guard even for Float64 inputs. No initial
#' normalization, sigma evaluation, store writes, RNG or graph is created.
#' W/u0 finite matching Float32/64 CPU, positive axes, rank(W)>=2, u0\[out,1\].
#' Strides allowed; results own storage and have no first/higher gradients.
#' O(iterations*in*out) work and O(in+out) temporary storage plus host validation.
#' Inputs unchanged; independent calls are safe without concurrent input writes.
#' @usage
#' cached_spectral_power_iteration(weight, u0, iterations = 1, epsilon = 9.99999996E-13)
#' @param weight `Tensor`. Finite floating kernel, flattened over all but the final axis.
#' @param u0 `Tensor`. Matching finite right column\[out,1\]; may be zero or non-unit.
#' @param iterations `integer`. Positive ordered iteration count, default1.
#' @param epsilon `numeric`. Positive representable squared-norm guard, default double(1e-12f).
#' @return `SpectralPowerPair`: Owning detached SpectralPowerPair; zero kernels give two zero columns.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' auto pair=n::cached_spectral_power_iteration(n::zeros({2,3}),n::ones({3,1}),2);
#' // pair.u[3,1] and pair.v[2,1] are finite zeros, detached from the inputs.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs/options/geometry or nonfinite intermediate
#'   values.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Miyato et al. (2018), https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.05957 , Algorithm 1.
#'   This explicit cached-column protocol adds a squared-norm guard and does not normalize u0
#'   first.
#' @seealso SpectralPowerPair, cached_spectral_kernel(), advance_cached_spectral_state()
#' @md
#'
`cached_spectral_power_iteration` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_452`, NULL, list(...))
#' Normalize a kernel using fixed cached columns and a differentiable signed sigma.
#'
#' M=flatten(W); sigma=sum(detach(v)*(M*detach(u))); weight=W/max(sigma,floor).
#' No abs, power iteration, cache write, RNG or implicit normalization of u/v.
#' Default floor=double(1e-6f). A negative/zero sigma therefore uses the positive
#' floor. Max uses the backend boundary subgradient. First/higher W paths remain
#' live including the sigma denominator; u/v paths are always stopped.
#' Finite matching Float32/64 CPU W of rank>=2 and columns u\[out,1\],v\[in,1\]
#' with positive axes; strides supported. Inputs unchanged; owning outputs retain
#' lifetime. O(in*out) work/storage plus host validation. Independent calls are
#' safe without concurrent input writes. This cached estimate is not an SVD bound.
#' @usage
#' cached_spectral_kernel(weight, u, v, floor = 9.99999997E-7)
#' @param weight `Tensor`. Finite floating kernel; all leading axes are flattened as input.
#' @param u `Tensor`. Matching finite right column\[out,1\], held constant in backpropagation.
#' @param v `Tensor`. Matching finite left column\[in,1\], held constant in backpropagation.
#' @param floor `numeric`. Positive representable denominator floor, default double(1e-6f).
#' @return `CachedSpectralKernel`: Owning CachedSpectralKernel with live effective weight and raw signed sigma.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' auto w=n::full({1,1},2.).requires_grad_();
#' auto result=n::cached_spectral_kernel(w,n::ones({1,1}),n::ones({1,1}));
#' auto derivative=n::grad(n::sum(result.weight),{w});
#' // derivative is zero: the differentiable denominator cancels this scalar scale.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs/geometry/guard or nonfinite computation.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Miyato et al. (2018), https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.05957 , equations 8 and 10.
#'   The positive signed-sigma floor is this library's explicit source protocol.
#' @seealso CachedSpectralKernel, cached_spectral_power_iteration(), spectral_norm_dense()
#' @md
#'
`cached_spectral_kernel` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_453`, NULL, list(...))
#' Explicitly advance every cached /W kernel pair, committing only after all computations pass.
#'
#' For each existing kernel "prefix/W", reads "prefix/u" and "prefix/v" in
#' state, validates both, then computes detached ordered iterations from u.
#' Biases/other names are ignored. All candidates are computed before any write,
#' so invalid/missing state or nonfinite computation leaves both stores unchanged.
#' No initialization, optimizer, gradient, RNG, weight write or mode switch is hidden.
#' Existing state Tensor handles see copied values; their requires_grad flags are
#' unchanged, but cache math always detaches them. Exclude state from optimizers.
#' Empty kernel sets are a no-op. Distinct matching Float32/64 stores are required.
#' Work O(iterations*sum(kernel sizes)); candidate storage O(sum(in+out)) plus
#' validation. Synchronize calls sharing either store; this is not a concurrent transaction.
#' @usage
#' advance_cached_spectral_state(parameters, state, iterations = 1, epsilon = 9.99999996E-13)
#' @param parameters `ParameterStore`. Mutable parameter owner, read only by this operation.
#' @param state `ParameterStore`. Distinct matching floating store of existing column pairs; only those pairs are
#'   written.
#' @param iterations `integer`. Positive iterations per kernel, default1.
#' @param epsilon `numeric`. Positive representable squared-norm guard, default double(1e-12f).
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(1),s(0);
#' p.get("layer/W",{2,3},n::init::ones());
#' s.get("layer/u",{3,1},n::init::ones());s.get("layer/v",{2,1},n::init::ones());
#' n::advance_cached_spectral_state(p,s); // only the two state arrays change.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For aliased/mismatched stores, invalid options, geometry or
#'   nonfinite computation.
#' * `std::out_of_range`: For a missing cached u or v; no writes occur.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Miyato et al. (2018), https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.05957 , Algorithm 1.
#' @seealso cached_spectral_power_iteration(), cached_spectral_kernel()
#' @md
#'
`advance_cached_spectral_state` <- function(...) invisible(.Call(`.rs_454`, NULL, list(...)))
#' Apply a dense map using cached singular columns and a live signed weight denominator.
#'
#' y=activate(x*W/max(sum(detach(v)*(W*detach(u))),double(1e-6f))+b).
#' Finite matching Float32/64 CPU x\[N,in\], positive axes, distinct matching stores,
#' nonempty name and positive units required. Creates name/W\[in,units\],b\[units\]
#' in parameters, and name/u\[units,1\],v\[in,1\] in state, in that order. W's uniform
#' limit is sqrt(6.f/float(in+units)); biases are zero; initial state columns are
#' 1.f/sqrt(float(length)). Constants preserve Float32 rounding in Float64 too.
#' All shape/product/input checks precede leaves; incompatible existing leaves,
#' invalid activation or nonfinite computation may fail later after earlier leaves
#' were created. Strides and applicable first/higher x/W/b paths stay live, including
#' sigma; both column paths stop. No initial power iteration, state advance, RNG
#' beyond missing leaf creation, fit, optimizer or implicit freeze is hidden.
#' Existing state is unchanged; exclude its store from optimizers despite its
#' ParameterStore flags. Inputs unchanged, output owns lifetime. Work O(N*in*units),
#' activations O(N*units) plus validation. Synchronize shared stores. The cached
#' estimate need not equal the exact operator norm; negative sigma uses the floor.
#' @usage
#' cached_spectral_dense(parameters, state, name, x, units, activation = "None")
#' @param parameters `ParameterStore`. Mutable floating weight/bias owner.
#' @param state `ParameterStore`. Distinct matching cache owner, unchanged after initialization.
#' @param name `character`. Nonempty prefix for W,b,u,v, without an added layer suffix.
#' @param x `Tensor`. Finite signed matching floating CPU\[N,in\] matrix with positive axes.
#' @param units `integer`. Positive output width, with representable sums/products.
#' @param activation `character (Activation)`. Output activation, default Activation::None (raw affine output).
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning live floating\[N,units\] dense output.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(1),s(0);
#' n::cached_spectral_dense(p,s,"layer",n::zeros({2,3}),4,n::Activation::Tanh);
#' n::advance_cached_spectral_state(p,s,16); // explicit warm-up outside the layer.
#' auto y=n::cached_spectral_dense(p,s,"layer",n::ones({2,3}),4,n::Activation::Tanh);
#' // y is[2,4]; subsequent scoring does not change existing u/v.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs/options/stores/geometry, incompatible leaves,
#'   or nonfinite weights, bias, cache or computed output.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Miyato et al. (2018), Spectral Normalization for Generative Adversarial Networks,
#'   https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.05957 . This explicit cached-column variant adds a
#'   signed denominator floor and uses source-rounded initialization constants.
#' @seealso cached_spectral_kernel(), advance_cached_spectral_state(), spectral_norm_dense()
#' @md
#'
`cached_spectral_dense` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_455`, NULL, list(...))
#' Score coordinates using two cached spectral kernels with tanh then a raw scalar output.
#'
#' image\[N,F\] -> hidden tanh H -> raw source score\[N,1\]. Each W is divided by
#' max(sum(detach(v)*(W*detach(u))),double(1e-6f)); biases are not normalized.
#' Creates hidden/W\[F,H\],b\[H\],output/W\[H,1\],b\[1\] in that order. Each layer's
#' state creates prefix/u\[out,1\],prefix/v\[in,1\]. W's uniform limit is computed
#' as sqrt(6.f/float(in+out)); initial columns are 1.f/sqrt(float(length)),
#' preserving Float32-rounded constants for both computation dtypes. Default
#' F784/H32 creates four trainable leaves/25153 values and four cache leaves/849
#' values. Cache flags follow ParameterStore but their math is always detached;
#' exclude the state store from optimization and checkpoint it explicitly.
#'
#' Does not advance existing state, warm up, normalize u initially, draw noise
#' beyond missing leaf initialization, fit, or choose an optimizer. Call
#' advance_cached_spectral_state() explicitly; repeated inference leaves existing
#' state bit exact. Finite signed Float32/64 CPU images match both distinct
#' stores, positive widths/products, strides supported. All applicable image/W
#' first/higher paths including sigma stay live. All input/geometry checks precede
#' leaves; incompatible/nonfinite existing leaves or computation may fail later
#' after earlier missing leaves were created. Inputs unchanged; outputs own lifetime.
#' Work O(N*F*H), activations O(N*(F+H)) plus kernel validation. Synchronize stores.
#' Finite power iteration does not certify exact unit kernel or network norms.
#' @usage
#' SpectralGanDiscriminate(discriminator, state, image, features = 784, hidden = 32)
#' @param discriminator `ParameterStore`. Mutable floating spectral dense weight/bias owner.
#' @param state `ParameterStore`. Distinct matching cache owner, read unchanged after initialization.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Finite signed matching floating CPU\[N,features\], N>0.
#' @param features `integer`. Positive image/input width F, default784.
#' @param hidden `integer`. Positive tanh width H, default32.
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning live raw source scores\[N,1\], without a sigmoid.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore d(5807),s(0);
#' n::models::SpectralGanDiscriminate(d,s,n::zeros({2,784}));
#' n::advance_cached_spectral_state(d,s,16); // explicit warm-up, outside inference.
#' auto score=n::models::SpectralGanDiscriminate(d,s,n::zeros({2,784}));
#' // Existing u/v are unchanged by scoring; sigma's W path remains live.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs/geometry, aliased/mismatched stores,
#'   incompatible leaves or nonfinite computation.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Miyato, Kataoka, Koyama and Yoshida (2018), Spectral Normalization for
#'   Generative Adversarial Networks, https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.05957 .
#'   This compact tanh MLP and explicit guarded cached-column protocol are teaching choices.
#' @seealso SpectralGan(), cached_spectral_kernel(), advance_cached_spectral_state()
#' @md
#'
`SpectralGanDiscriminate` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_456`, NULL, list(...))
#' Evaluate a compact sigmoid generator and cached spectral discriminator with hinge objectives.
#'
#' G is MlpGanGenerate(): noise\[M,Z\] -> tanh H -> sigmoid F. D is
#' SpectralGanDiscriminate(): real\[N,F\]/fake\[M,F\] -> spectral tanh H -> spectral
#' raw scalar. HingeGanObjectives() gives D=mean(relu(1-real))+mean(relu(1+fake))
#' with zero margin subgradient and G=-mean(fake), with no G hinge or sigmoid.
#' Default Z16/H32/F784 creates G26416/4 leaves, D25153/4 leaves, cache849/4 leaves
#' in G,D order, hidden then output W,b and state u,v per layer. Signed floating
#' images/noise match three distinct Float32/64 CPU stores. Unequal positive N/M,
#' positive widths/products, strides and applicable first/higher continuous paths
#' are supported. Fixed cache columns are stopped; the W-dependent sigma is live.
#'
#' No cache advance, warm-up, fitting, optimizer, implicit freeze, checkpoint,
#' MMD diagnostic or noise draw beyond missing leaf initialization is hidden.
#' Caller initializes, explicitly warms state, then for each batch advances state,
#' writes only D, recomputes through updated D with the SAME cache, and writes only G.
#' Cache requires_grad flags follow ParameterStore; exclude this store from Adam.
#' All input/geometry checks precede leaves; incompatible/nonfinite existing leaves
#' may fail later after earlier missing leaves were created. Inputs unchanged,
#' outputs own lifetime. Work O((N+M)*F*H+M*Z*H); activations O((N+M)*(F+H)+M*Z)
#' plus validation. Synchronize shared stores. An estimated norm is not a certificate.
#' @usage
#' SpectralGan(generator, discriminator, state, image, noise, features = 784, hidden = 32)
#' @param generator `ParameterStore`. Mutable floating generator owner.
#' @param discriminator `ParameterStore`. Distinct matching floating spectral dense weight/bias owner.
#' @param state `ParameterStore`. Third distinct matching cache owner; unchanged after initialization.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Finite signed matching floating CPU\[N,features\], N>0.
#' @param noise `Tensor`. Finite signed matching floating CPU\[M,Z\], M,Z>0; independent of N.
#' @param features `integer`. Positive image/output width F, default784.
#' @param hidden `integer`. Positive hidden tanh width H, default32 for both networks.
#' @return `DenseGanOutput`: Owning DenseGanOutput: fake, real/fake scores and scalar D/G objectives.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore g(5801),d(5807),s(0);
#' auto x=n::zeros({2,784}),z=n::zeros({3,16});
#' n::models::SpectralGan(g,d,s,x,z); // initialize only.
#' n::advance_cached_spectral_state(d,s,16);
#' n::advance_cached_spectral_state(d,s); // before the explicit D phase.
#' auto out=n::models::SpectralGan(g,d,s,x,z);
#' auto derivative=n::grad(out.discriminator_loss,d.parameters());
#' // Write only D, then recompute the G objective with unchanged s.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs/geometry, aliased/mismatched stores,
#'   incompatible leaves or nonfinite computation.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Miyato et al. (2018), https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.05957 , spectral normalization
#'   and raw-score hinge adversarial objectives. This small MNIST MLP is not a paper benchmark.
#' @seealso SpectralGanDiscriminate(), MlpGanGenerate(), HingeGanObjectives(), advance_cached_spectral_state()
#' @md
#'
`SpectralGan` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_457`, NULL, list(...))
#' Mix all spatial tokens with unscaled attention and cached spectral dense projections.
#'
#' input\[B,T,C\] flattens to\[B*T,C\]. Creates name/query, key, value and project
#' biased spectral maps C->Q,C->Q,C->V,V->C, then scalar name/gamma initialized0,
#' in this order. probability=softmax(Q*K^T), without sqrt(Q) scaling; output is
#' input+gamma*project(probability*V). Reuses scaled_dot_product_attention() with
#' explicit scale1, Plain and need_weights=true; no mask, dropout or fused path.
#' The initial zero gate makes output exactly input, while probability remains
#' a live computed field. Q/K/V/project partials of an output-only loss initially
#' vanish; the gate can still receive a gradient. Every projection uses
#' cached_spectral_dense() source-rounded initialization and stopped column paths,
#' while its signed sigma remains differentiable in W. No cache advance is hidden.
#'
#' Finite matching Float32/64 CPU tokens with positive B,T,C, positive Q/V,
#' representable products, strides and applicable first/higher continuous paths.
#' Distinct matching stores and nonempty name required. Input checks precede
#' leaves; existing-leaf/nonfinite failures can occur later after earlier leaves.
#' Inputs unchanged; owning outputs retain lifetime. Work O(B*T*C*(Q+V)+B*T*T*(Q+V)),
#' activation storage O(B*T*(C+Q+V)+B*T*T), plus validation. Synchronize stores.
#' Cache flags follow ParameterStore; exclude state from optimizers and checkpoint it.
#' @usage
#' SpectralSpatialAttention(parameters, state, input, query_width = 2, value_width = 4, name = "attention")
#' @param parameters `ParameterStore`. Mutable floating projection/gate owner.
#' @param state `ParameterStore`. Distinct matching cached-column owner; unchanged after initialization.
#' @param input `Tensor`. Finite signed matching floating CPU\[B,T,C\] tokens with positive axes.
#' @param query_width `integer`. Positive shared query/key width Q, default2.
#' @param value_width `integer`. Positive value width V, default4.
#' @param name `character`. Nonempty parameter/cache prefix, default "attention".
#' @return `SpectralSpatialOutput`: Owning SpectralSpatialOutput with input, probability and residual output.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(1),s(0);
#' auto x=n::ones({2,16,8});
#' n::models::SpectralSpatialAttention(p,s,x);n::advance_cached_spectral_state(p,s,16);
#' auto a=n::models::SpectralSpatialAttention(p,s,x);
#' // a.probability is[2,16,16]; scoring does not advance existing cache state.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs/options/stores/products, incompatible leaves or
#'   nonfinite output.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Zhang et al. (2018/2019), https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.08318 , self-attention
#'   residual with a zero-initialized scalar gate. This variant uses biased dense
#'   projections and explicit cached spectral normalization on every kernel.
#' @seealso cached_spectral_dense(), SelfAttentionGanGenerate(), SelfAttentionGanDiscriminate()
#' @md
#'
`SpectralSpatialAttention` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_458`, NULL, list(...))
#' Generate grayscale pixels from explicit noise through spectral spatial-patch attention.
#'
#' noise\[B,16\] -> spectral input dense128/tanh ->\[B,16,8\] tokens ->
#' SpectralSpatialAttention(Q2,V4) -> shared spectral patch dense49/sigmoid ->
#' MaeImage() raster permutation of sixteen row-major7x7 patches. Creates input
#' W,b; four attention maps W,b; scalar attention/gamma0; patch W,b, in this order.
#' Defaults are fixed architecture,2730 parameters/13 leaves and245 cache values/12
#' leaves; no labels or image enter G. Cached spectral guards and initialization
#' use source Float32 rounding. No power iteration, warm-up, noise draw beyond
#' missing leaves, optimizer or fitting is hidden. Existing cache is unchanged.
#' Finite matching Float32/64 CPU noise with positive B, strides, representable
#' activation products and applicable first/higher noise/W paths; cache paths stop.
#' Distinct matching stores required. Inputs validate before leaves; incompatible
#' leaves/nonfinite computation may fail later. Inputs unchanged, outputs own
#' lifetime. Work O(B*(16*128+16*8*49+16*16*6)); activations O(B*(784+16*16)),
#' plus validation. Synchronize shared stores; exclude cache from optimizers.
#' @usage
#' SelfAttentionGanGenerate(generator, state, noise)
#' @param generator `ParameterStore`. Mutable floating patch-generator weight/gate owner.
#' @param state `ParameterStore`. Distinct matching G cache owner, unchanged after initialization.
#' @param noise `Tensor`. Finite signed matching floating CPU\[B,16\], B>0.
#' @return `SelfAttentionGenerated`: Owning SelfAttentionGenerated, with pixels and all G attention endpoints.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore g(5903),s(0);
#' n::models::SelfAttentionGanGenerate(g,s,n::zeros({2,16}));
#' n::advance_cached_spectral_state(g,s,16);
#' auto out=n::models::SelfAttentionGanGenerate(g,s,n::zeros({2,16}));
#' // Every patch shares the same learned8->49 map; state is not advanced here.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs/stores/products, incompatible leaves or
#'   nonfinite computation.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Zhang et al. (2018/2019), https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.08318 . This compact
#'   dense spatial-patch teaching model is not the paper's convolutional benchmark.
#' @seealso SelfAttentionGanDiscriminate(), SpectralSpatialAttention(), MaeImage(), SelfAttentionGan()
#' @md
#'
`SelfAttentionGanGenerate` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_459`, NULL, list(...))
#' Score raster pixels through shared spectral patch embeddings and position-aware attention.
#'
#' image\[B,784\] -> MaePatches() row-major7x7 patches -> shared spectral49->8/tanh
#' -> learned normal(.01) position\[16,8\] -> SpectralSpatialAttention(Q2,V4) ->
#' mean over16 positions -> spectral8->1 raw score. Creates patch W,b, position,
#' four attention maps W,b, scalar attention/gamma0, output W,b, in that order:
#' 650 values/14 leaves and110 cached values/12 leaves. Both real and fake branches
#' share this store and cache. No label, noise or class head enters D.
#' No cache advance, warm-up, optimizer, fitting or RNG beyond missing leaves.
#' Finite signed matching Float32/64 CPU image with positive B, strides and
#' applicable first/higher image/weight paths. Cache columns stop, sigma stays
#' live. Distinct matching stores and representable products required. Input
#' checks precede leaves; incompatible/nonfinite leaves can fail later. Inputs
#' unchanged, outputs own lifetime. Work O(B*(16*49*8+16*16*6)); activations
#' O(B*(784+16*16)), plus validation. Synchronize stores; exclude cache from Adam.
#' @usage
#' SelfAttentionGanDiscriminate(discriminator, state, image)
#' @param discriminator `ParameterStore`. Mutable floating patch-discriminator owner.
#' @param state `ParameterStore`. Distinct matching D cache owner, unchanged after initialization.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Finite signed matching floating CPU\[B,784\], B>0.
#' @return `SelfAttentionDiscriminated`: Owning SelfAttentionDiscriminated with raw score and all D attention fields.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore d(5923),s(0);
#' n::models::SelfAttentionGanDiscriminate(d,s,n::zeros({2,784}));
#' n::advance_cached_spectral_state(d,s,16);
#' auto out=n::models::SelfAttentionGanDiscriminate(d,s,n::zeros({2,784}));
#' // out.score is raw; no sigmoid or class prediction is hidden.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs/stores/products, incompatible leaves or
#'   nonfinite computation.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Zhang et al. (2018/2019), https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.08318 . This compact
#'   dense patch variant adds learned spatial positions before attention.
#' @seealso SelfAttentionGanGenerate(), SpectralSpatialAttention(), MaePatches(), SelfAttentionGan()
#' @md
#'
`SelfAttentionGanDiscriminate` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_460`, NULL, list(...))
#' Evaluate a compact spectral patch GAN with unscaled attention in both networks.
#'
#' Composes SelfAttentionGanGenerate(), SelfAttentionGanDiscriminate() on real
#' and fake, and HingeGanObjectives(). Creates G2730/13 leaves, D650/14 leaves,
#' G cache245/12 leaves and D cache110/12 leaves:51 checkpoint tensors/3735 values,
#' of which3380 values are optimized. Stores initialize in G,D order with layer
#' orders documented by the two maps. Residual gates start0; all twelve kernels
#' use guarded cached spectral normalization with live sigma and stopped columns.
#'
#' Finite signed Float32/64 CPU image\[N,784\],noise\[M,16\], positive possibly unequal
#' N/M, strides, representable products and applicable first/higher continuous
#' paths. All four stores are distinct and dtype matched. No hidden advance,
#' warm-up, optimizer, fit, freeze, checkpoint or MMD. Caller initializes, warms
#' both cache stores16 iterations, then per batch advances D cache, writes D,
#' advances G cache and recomputes a fresh G objective through updated D with
#' unchanged D cache, writing only G. Exclude both cache stores from Adam even
#' though ParameterStore flags follow normal leaves. Input checks precede leaves;
#' incompatible/nonfinite leaves may fail later. Inputs unchanged, outputs own
#' lifetime. Work/storage are the sum of the three maps, with O((N+M)*16*16)
#' attention activations plus validation. Synchronize shared stores. Finite power
#' iteration is not an exact unit norm or network Lipschitz certificate.
#' @usage
#' SelfAttentionGan(generator, discriminator, generator_state, discriminator_state, image, noise)
#' @param generator `ParameterStore`. Mutable floating G parameter owner.
#' @param discriminator `ParameterStore`. Distinct matching floating D parameter owner.
#' @param generator_state `ParameterStore`. Third distinct matching cached G column owner.
#' @param discriminator_state `ParameterStore`. Fourth distinct matching cached D column owner.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Finite signed matching floating CPU\[N,784\], N>0.
#' @param noise `Tensor`. Finite signed matching floating CPU\[M,16\], M>0.
#' @return `SelfAttentionGanOutput`: Owning twelve-field SelfAttentionGanOutput with explicit scalar D/G losses.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore g(5903),d(5923),gs(0),ds(0);
#' auto x=n::zeros({2,784}),z=n::zeros({3,16});
#' n::models::SelfAttentionGan(g,d,gs,ds,x,z);
#' n::advance_cached_spectral_state(g,gs,16);n::advance_cached_spectral_state(d,ds,16);
#' n::advance_cached_spectral_state(d,ds);auto o=n::models::SelfAttentionGan(g,d,gs,ds,x,z);
#' auto derivative=n::grad(o.discriminator_loss,d.parameters());
#' // Write D, advance only G's cache, then recompute before selecting G partials.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs/stores/products, incompatible leaves or
#'   nonfinite computation.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Zhang, Goodfellow, Metaxas and Odena (2018/2019), Self-Attention Generative
