#' No optimizer, clipping, fitting, freeze, checkpoint or distance certification.
#' Caller chooses parameter gradients, RMSProp/clipping or Adam/penalty, three
#' fresh-noise critic steps then a fresh G step. Applicable higher paths live;
#' no existing leaves are mutated. Checks precede creation; stored-leaf/nonfinite
#' math errors may occur later. Owning outputs, inputs unchanged. O(N) work/storage
#' for fixed width; synchronize stores and exclude concurrent input writes.
#' @usage
#' WassersteinGan(generator, critic, real, noise, alpha, penalty_weight = 10.0, penalty_graph = TRUE)
#' @param generator `ParameterStore`. Mutable floating G owner, distinct from critic.
#' @param critic `ParameterStore`. Mutable matching floating C owner.
#' @param real `Tensor`. Finite signed matching CPU\[N,2\] real coordinates, N>0.
#' @param noise `Tensor`. Finite signed matching CPU\[N,2\] explicit latent bank, same N.
#' @param alpha `Tensor`. Finite matching CPU\[N,1\] interpolation coefficients in\[0,1\].
#' @param penalty_weight `numeric`. Finite nonnegative coefficient, default10;0 for clipped WGAN's base loss.
#' @param penalty_graph `logical`. Retain critic history through symbolic input gradient when true(default);
#'   detach it when false.
#' @return `WassersteinGanOutput`: Owning eleven-field WassersteinGanOutput with both Jacobians and explicit objectives.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore g(5501),c(5503);
#' auto
#' out=n::models::WassersteinGan(g,c,n::ones({2,2}),n::zeros({2,2}),n::full({2,1},.5),10.,true);
#' auto critic_gradient=n::grad(out.critic_loss,c.parameters());
#' // No Adam/clipping/update occurs; G gradient requires a fresh forward after C writes.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid geometry/stores/options/ranges or nonfinite
#'   computation.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Arjovsky,Chintala and Bottou (2017), https://arxiv.org/abs/1701.07875 .
#' - Gulrajani,Ahmed,Arjovsky,Dumoulin and Courville (2017), Improved Training of
#'   Wasserstein GANs, https://arxiv.org/abs/1704.00028 . The tiny teaching network
#'   and three-critic-step schedule are the repository source's choices.
#' @seealso WassersteinGanOutput, WassersteinGenerate(), WassersteinCritic(), ClipWassersteinCritic()
#' @md
#'
`WassersteinGan` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_481`, NULL, list(...))
#' Divide each last-axis feature vector by its RMS using explicit division and square root.
#'
#' Finite Float32/64 CPU input\[...,C\], rank>=1, positive axes and strides allowed.
#' Computes input/sqrt(mean(square(input),last_axis,keepdims=true)+epsilon).
#' Default epsilon=double(1e-8f) preserves the migrated progressive source guard
#' even for Float64. This is per-position channel normalization, without batch
#' coupling, mean centering, L2 unit-length scaling, learned gamma/beta or state.
#' The explicit division/sqrt grouping differs from multiplying by rsqrt in
#' Float32 and is retained for source rounding. Zero vectors remain zero with
#' finite guarded derivatives. Positive finite representable epsilon required.
#'
#' Applicable first/higher input paths remain live; owning output retains its
#' graph/storage after input collection. No mutation, RNG, optimizer or fitting.
#' Rejects nonfinite intermediate roots/output rather than repairing overflow.
#' O(input.numel()) work/storage plus validation; exclude concurrent input writes.
#' @usage
#' pixel_rms_normalize(input, epsilon = 9.99999993E-9)
#' @param input `Tensor`. Finite signed Float32/64 CPU\[...,C\], rank>=1, positive axes.
#' @param epsilon `numeric`. Positive finite representable mean-square guard, default double(1e-8f).
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning live tensor with input shape/dtype and independently normalized last-axis
#' vectors.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' auto out=dm::nn::pixel_rms_normalize(dm::nn::tensor({3.,4.},{1,2},dm::nn::DType::Float64));
#' // Approximately(.848528,1.131371); mean(square(out)) is near1, not its L2 norm.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid geometry/dtype/epsilon or nonfinite computation.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Karras,Aila,Laine and Lehtinen (2017/2018), Progressive Growing of GANs for
