#' @param image `Tensor`. Floating \[N,cfg.image_size,cfg.image_size,3\], matching store dtype.
#' @param cfg `ZFNetConfig`. Valid reference or explicitly compact dimensions.
#' @param training `logical`. Enable dropout when true; false by default.
#' @return `ZFNetOutputs`: All recorded stages and \[N,classes\] unnormalised logits, with autograd history.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace n = dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(17);
#' n::models::ZFNetConfig cfg;
#' cfg.image_size = 67;
#' cfg.classes = 3;
#' cfg.width_divisor = 8;
#' cfg.dense_width = 16;
#' const auto out = n::models::ZFNet(p, n::zeros({1, cfg.image_size, cfg.image_size, 3}), cfg);
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid cfg, RGB geometry, tensor dtype or parameter/state entries.
#' @references - Zeiler and Fergus (2014), https://cs.nyu.edu/~fergus/papers/zeilerECCV2014.pdf
#' @seealso ZFNetConfig
#' @md
#'
`ZFNet` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_600`, NULL, list(...))
#' Project a conv5 signal back to the resized RGB input grid using deconvnet rules.
#'
#' At every convolution, rectify the backward signal before applying its adjoint.
#' At pooling, reuse the forward argmax switches. Omit LRN inversion, bias
#' subtraction and inverse nonlinearities, then remove only the explicit stem pad.
#' No fitting, and no claim that the result is a gradient or an input reconstruction.
#' @usage
#' ZFNetDeconvolution(p, net, signal)
#' @param p `ParameterStore`. Existing ZFNet store with conv1 through conv5 HWIO kernels.
#' @param net `ZFNetOutputs`. Forward stage values used for shapes and pooling switches.
#' @param signal `Tensor`. Floating tensor with the same shape as net.convolution\[4\].
#' @return `Tensor`: RGB tensor shaped like net.image; switch unpooling breaks the autograd graph.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace n = dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(17);
#' n::models::ZFNetConfig cfg;
#' cfg.image_size = 67;
#' cfg.classes = 3;
#' cfg.width_divisor = 8;
#' cfg.dense_width = 16;
#' const auto out = n::models::ZFNet(p, n::zeros({1, cfg.image_size, cfg.image_size, 3}), cfg);
#' const auto reconstruction = n::models::ZFNetDeconvolution(p, out, out.convolution[4]);
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For incompatible stage/signal geometry or kernel entries.
#' * `std::out_of_range`: If a required convolution kernel is absent from p.
#' @references - Zeiler and Fergus (2014), https://cs.nyu.edu/~fergus/papers/zeilerECCV2014.pdf
#' @seealso UnpoolAtSwitches(), DeconvLayer()
#' @md
#'
`ZFNetDeconvolution` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_601`, NULL, list(...))
