#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid tensor/group geometry, BN settings, dtype or stored entries.
#' @references - Chen et al. (2017), Dual Path Networks, https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.01629; released model implementation, https://github.com/rwightman/pytorch-dpn-pretrained/blob/master/dpn.py
#' @seealso RawResidualConv(), DPNBlock()
#' @md
#'
`DPNPreActConv` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_630`, NULL, list(...))
#' Split a shared preactivation bottleneck into residual addition and dense concatenation.
#'
#' Projection initializes width residual channels and 2*inc dense channels.
#' The shared branch is preactivated 1x1, grouped 3x3 (the downsample), then
#' 1x1 to width+inc. First width channels add to residual; last inc append to
#' dense. Ordinary units require matching residual width and an existing dense
#' path. Signed old paths pass unchanged when both branch updates are zero.
#' No fitting occurs; convolution plus pointwise work dominates.
#' @usage
#' DPNBlock(p, state, name, x, width, bottleneck, inc, groups, project, stride = 1, norm = PreactivationNormConfig$new())
#' @param p `ParameterStore`. Mutable floating learnable store.
#' @param state `ParameterStore`. Distinct BN moving moments, matching p dtype.
#' @param name `character`. Prefix for projection and conv1/2/3 layers.
#' @param x `DPNPaths`. Initialized incoming paths, joined in residual-then-dense order.
#' @param width `integer`. Positive fixed residual output width.
#' @param bottleneck `integer`. Positive inner width divisible by groups.
#' @param inc `integer`. Positive new dense channels per unit.
#' @param groups `integer`. Positive grouped 3x3 cardinality dividing bottleneck.
#' @param project `logical`. True starts a stage with a separate BN/ReLU/1x1 projection to width+2*inc.
#' @param stride `integer`. One (default) or two; downsampling requires project=true.
#' @param norm `PreactivationNormConfig`. BN mode/momentum/update settings; every layer forces epsilon .001.
#' @return `DPNBlockOutputs`: Projected input, branch updates and output paths; no activation follows the path combination.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace n = dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(17), state(17);
#' const n::models::DPNPaths x{n::ones({2, 5, 5, 4}), {}, 4, 0};
#' const auto y = n::models::DPNBlock(p, state, "b", x, 4, 4, 1, 2, true);
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid path metadata, dimensions/cardinality, stride, BN or stored entries.
#' @references - Chen et al. (2017), Dual Path Networks, https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.01629; released model implementation, https://github.com/rwightman/pytorch-dpn-pretrained/blob/master/dpn.py
#' @seealso DPNPaths, DPN()
#' @md
#'
`DPNBlock` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_631`, NULL, list(...))
#' Build a complete released-depth dual-path network without fitting.
#'
#' Every stage starts a projected dual path, then grows dense width by inc per
#' unit while residual width stays fixed. Complete unit counts are retained at
#' scaled widths. Standard stem is strided with padded max-pool; DPN-68 uses
#' a 3x3 kernel, other releases 7x7. small_stem removes downsampling/pool.
#' All convolutions are bias-free He initialized; learned-scale BN epsilon is
#' .001 with unbiased EMA moving variance. Final BN/ReLU, GAP and a biased
#' linear classifier follow. No dropout, pretrained weights or optimizer is hidden.
#' @usage
#' DPN(p, state, image, cfg = DPNConfig$new(), training = FALSE)
#' @param p `ParameterStore`. Mutable floating learnable store.
#' @param state `ParameterStore`. Distinct BN moving moments, matching p dtype.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Nonempty floating NHWC RGB batch.
#' @param cfg `DPNConfig`. Valid released layout, exact dimensions/cardinality, stem and BN settings.
#' @param training `logical`. Use batch moments with optional eager moving updates when true; false by default.
#' @return `DPNOutputs`: Stem, all units/stages, final features and \[N,classes\] logits retaining their graphs.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace n = dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(17), state(17);
#' n::models::DPNConfig cfg;
#' cfg.classes = 10;
#' cfg.width_divisor = 4;
#' cfg.groups = 8;
#' cfg.small_stem = true;
#' const auto y = n::models::DPN(p, state, n::zeros({1, 16, 16, 3}), cfg);
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid cfg, RGB/path geometry, dtype, BN or stored entries.
#' @references - Chen et al. (2017), Dual Path Networks, https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.01629; released model implementation, https://github.com/rwightman/pytorch-dpn-pretrained/blob/master/dpn.py
#' @seealso DPNBlock(), DPNConfig
#' @md
#'
`DPN` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_632`, NULL, list(...))
#' Apply a Form-C grouped bottleneck followed by shortcut addition and ReLU.
#'
#' Middle width is cardinality*floor(planes*base_width/64). Reduction/expansion
#' are dense 1x1, with learned-scale BN when cfg.scale=true. The grouped kernel
#' is one HWIO leaf \[3,3,middle/cardinality,middle\]; no convolution bias.
#' Matching width/stride uses raw identity. No optimizer or preprocessing is hidden.
#' He-uniform fan-in replaces the authors normal fan-out initialization.
#' Work O(NHW*(Cin*middle+9*middle²/cardinality+4*planes*middle)).
#' @usage
#' ResNeXtBlock(p, state, name, input, planes, cardinality, base_width, cfg, stride = 1)
#' @param p `ParameterStore`. Mutable learnable store; lazily creates/reuses named leaves.
#' @param state `ParameterStore`. Mutable BN moving-moment store; updates only when cfg requests training updates.
#' @param name `character`. Prefix for conv1, conv2, conv3 and optional shortcut.
#' @param input `Tensor`. Nonempty floating NHWC tensor matching store dtype.
#' @param planes `integer`. Positive stage base width; output has 4*planes channels.
#' @param cardinality `integer`. Positive number of independent contiguous 3x3 channel groups.
#' @param base_width `integer`. Positive group-width coefficient; floor(planes*base_width/64) must be positive.
#' @param cfg `ResNetNormConfig`. BN/ReLU settings, including training, scale, momentum and epsilon.
#' @param stride `integer`. One or two, applied in the grouped 3x3 and projection.
#' @return `ResNetBlockOutputs`: Residual, shortcut, preactivation sum and post-ReLU output with gradients.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace n = dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(17), state(17);
#' n::models::ResNetNormConfig norm;
#' norm.scale = true;
#' const auto y = n::models::ResNeXtBlock(p, state, "b", n::ones({1, 5, 5, 8}), 4, 2, 16, norm);
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid input, widths, stride, BN options, dtype or stored shapes.
#' @references - Xie et al. (2017), https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.05431; authors Form C: https://github.com/facebookresearch/ResNeXt/blob/master/models/resnext.lua
#' @seealso ResNeXt(), ResNetBlockOutputs
#' @md
#'
`ResNeXtBlock` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_633`, NULL, list(...))
#' Build the complete ResNeXt tensor classifier without fitting.
#'
#' ImageNet has a 7x7 stride-two stem, padded 3x3 stride-two max-pool and
#' four 3/4/6/3 stages at depth 50. CIFAR uses 3x3 stride one, no initial
#' pool and three (depth-2)/9 stages. Stage outer widths are 4*stage_width*2^s.
#' Stride two is in the grouped 3x3 at later stage entries; final global mean
#' accepts variable spatial dimensions. Full 50 32x4d has 25028904 learned
#' scalars. Learned-scale BN epsilon 1e-5, no dropout.
#' No input preprocessing, loss, optimizer or fitting is hidden. Parameters
#' use He-uniform fan-in convolutions, with a Glorot dense classifier.
#' Moving moments update only when training && cfg.update_stats. Work sums
#' convolution MACs; storage includes intermediate activations and learned leaves.
#' @usage
#' ResNeXt(p, state, image, cfg = ResNeXtConfig$new(), training = FALSE)
#' @param p `ParameterStore`. Mutable learnable floating store; names are reused on repeated calls.
#' @param state `ParameterStore`. Mutable moving-moment store, matching p dtype.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Nonempty floating NHWC image tensor with positive channels.
#' @param cfg `ResNeXtConfig`. Validated ResNeXt configuration; default ImageNet 50 32x4d.
#' @param training `logical`. Use batch moments and training dropout when applicable; false uses saved moments.
#' @return `ResNeXtOutputs`: Stem, stages, every block and logits, all retaining gradients.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace n = dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(17), state(17);
#' n::models::ResNeXtConfig cfg;
#' cfg.depth = 11;
#' cfg.cifar_layout = true;
#' cfg.stage_width = 16;
#' cfg.cardinality = 2;
#' cfg.base_width = 16;
#' cfg.classes = 10;
#' const auto y = n::models::ResNeXt(p, state, n::zeros({1, 16, 16, 3}), cfg);
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid configuration, NHWC, normalization, dtype or stored shapes.
#' @references - Xie et al. (2017), https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.05431; authors Form C: https://github.com/facebookresearch/ResNeXt/blob/master/models/resnext.lua
#' @seealso ResNeXtConfig, ResNeXtBlock()
#' @md
