#' @param name `character`. Prefix for bn, W, mask and stage leaves.
#' @param x `Tensor`. Nonempty floating NHWC input matching stores.
#' @param out `integer`. Positive output width divisible by groups.
#' @param groups `integer`. Positive interleaved output-group count dividing input and output.
#' @param condense `integer`. Factor >=2 dividing input width.
#' @return `LearnedGroupConvOutputs`: Normalized input, output and detached pre-update mask snapshot with graphs.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace n = dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(17), state(17);
#' std::vector<n::models::MobileLayer> layers;
#' n::models::CondenseContext c{p, state, layers, false};
#' const auto y = n::models::LearnedGroupConv(c, "lgc", n::ones({2, 5, 5, 8}), 8, 2, 2);
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid dimensions, settings, masks/stages, dtype,
#'   normalization or stored shapes.
#' @references - Huang et al. (2018), https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.09224;
#'   https://github.com/ShichenLiu/CondenseNet
#' @seealso CondenseNet(), LearnedGroupConv(), Condense()
#' @md
#'
`LearnedGroupConv` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_692`, NULL, list(...))
#' Build the complete dense CondenseNet tensor classifier without fitting.
#'
#' Architecture tracing groups each dense stage, including its following transition.
#' The first stage includes the stem; layer/operation views remain expandable.
#'
#' Stem is bias-free 3x3 to twice first growth; each layer appends growth
#' channels from LGC to bottleneck*growth then BN/ReLU/grouped 3x3.
#' Stages have only 2x2 average-pool transitions, no compression convolution.
#' Final BN/ReLU, global mean and biased classifier. No dropout. He-uniform
#' filters, BN eps 1e-5. One enabled training forward advances run step
#' after all layers; progress before that increment drives masks. Warm all
#' leaves in inference before constructing an optimizer. Inference never
#' advances moments/masks/step. Caller must explicitly add returned penalties,
#' choose loss/optimizer, and own minibatches/checkpoints. Save state alongside
#' weights; a selected early checkpoint may not yet be fully condensed.
#' @usage
#' CondenseNet(p, state, image, cfg = CondenseNetConfig$new(), training = FALSE, total_steps = 0)
#' @param p `ParameterStore`. Mutable learned store, lazily creates/reuses named leaves.
#' @param state `ParameterStore`. Mutable BN/mask/stage store, plus condense/step on training calls.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Nonempty floating NHWC images matching stores.
#' @param cfg `CondenseNetConfig`. Valid dense stages, growth and condensation metadata.
#' @param training `logical`. True uses batch moments, collects lasso and optionally advances condensation.
#' @param total_steps `integer`. Positive total training-forward budget when training; ignored for inference.
#' @return `CondenseNetOutputs`: Features/logits, explicit penalty tensors and dense-mask arithmetic metadata.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace n = dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(17), state(17);
#' n::models::CondenseNetConfig cfg;
#' cfg.stages = {1, 1, 1};
#' const auto y = n::models::CondenseNet(p, state, n::ones({2, 8, 8, 3}), cfg);
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid dimensions, settings, masks/stages, dtype,
#'   normalization or stored shapes.
#' @references - Huang et al. (2018), https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.09224;
#'   https://github.com/ShichenLiu/CondenseNet
#' @seealso CondenseNet(), LearnedGroupConv(), Condense()
#' @md
#'
`CondenseNet` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_693`, NULL, list(...))
#' Pack a binary-masked learned kernel with tensor gathers, preserving dtype.
#'
#' Output o belongs to o mod G in the masked kernel. Packed outputs are
#' contiguous per group, requiring PaperChannelShuffle afterward. Gather
#' inputs, BN affine/moving values with index, normalize/ReLU, then grouped
#' conv2d with packed weights. Source weights are not mutated or cast through
#' host arrays. Discrete index selection is nondifferentiable; retained weight
#' gathers preserve gradients when enabled. Does not halve the classifier.
