`DropConnect` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_700`, NULL, list(...))
#' Apply an inverted or fused mobile bottleneck with optional SE and residual dropout.
#'
#' Architecture tracing records the complete residual/SE unit as a named block;
#' layer and operation detail remain available. Ordinary forwards return the same tensors.
#'
#' Nonfused: optional 1x1 expansion/BN/act, SAME depthwise/BN/act,
#' optional global-mean SE, linear 1x1/BN. SE reduces to max(1,floor(Cin*ratio))
#' and uses the chosen activation then logistic sigmoid. Fused replaces
#' expansion/depthwise with dense kxk/BN/act; expansion one instead uses
#' a single activated kxk projection and forbids SE. Raw shortcut applies
#' only if skip, stride one and equal widths; branch dropout uses c.p RNG.
#' He-uniform filters; BN epsilon 1e-3 with learned scale/center. Logged
#' MACs include kernels and pooled SE; no fitting or timing is hidden.
#' @usage
#' MBConv(c, name, x, out, b, stride, swish, drop_rate = 0.0)
#' @param c `MobileContext`. Borrowed learned/state stores, training options and measured-layer log.
#' @param name `character`. Parameter prefix for expand/depthwise/se/project leaves.
#' @param x `Tensor`. Nonempty floating NHWC input matching store dtype.
#' @param out `integer`. Positive actual output width.
#' @param b `BlockArgs`. Positive kernel/expansion and SE in \[0,1\]; table repeats/input/output unused here.
#' @param stride `integer`. Positive actual spatial step, independent of table first-repeat stride.
#' @param swish `logical`. True selects x*sigmoid(x), false ReLU.
#' @param drop_rate `numeric`. Residual drop probability in \[0,1), used only in training matching shortcuts.
#' @return `MBConvOutputs`: Intermediate maps and final NHWC output with full gradients.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace n = dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(17), state(17);
#' std::vector<n::models::MobileLayer> layers;
#' n::models::MobileContext c{p, state, layers, false};
#' const auto y = n::models::MBConv(c, "b", n::ones({1, 5, 5, 8}), 8,
#'                                  n::models::DecodeBlock("r1_k3_s1_e2_i8_o8_se0.25"), 1, true);
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid domain, unknown preset, unsupported dtype/shape,
#'   overflowing dimensions or incompatible stored entries.
#' @references - Tan et al. (2019), https://arxiv.org/abs/1807.11626; Tan and Le (2019),
#'   https://arxiv.org/abs/1905.11946; Tan and Le (2021), https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.00298;
#'   https://github.com/google/automl/tree/master/efficientnetv2
#' @seealso BlockArgs, MBConv(), MnasNet(), EfficientNet(), EfficientNetV2()
#' @md
#'
`MBConv` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_701`, NULL, list(...))
#' Return the seven released MnasNet stage specifications.
#'
#' A1 and B1 retain their distinct expansion/kernel/repeat/width tables.
#' Architecture metadata only, no search or fitting is performed.
#' @usage
#' MnasNetBlocks(variant)
#' @param variant `character`. a1 or b1, case-sensitive.
#' @return `vector<BlockArgs>`: Owned vector: A1 sixteen repeats with selective SE; B1 seventeen without SE.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' const auto blocks = dm::nn::models::MnasNetBlocks("a1");
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
