#' @param out `integer`. Positive total output channels.
#' @param alpha_out `numeric`. Low-output fraction in \[0,1).
#' @param kernel `integer`. Positive odd square side.
#' @param stride `integer`. One or two; two pre-pools streams, except LH in a high-only merge.
#' @param high_size `integer`. Positive nominal target high side before stride; exact pooling alignment required.
#' @param cost `OctaveCost or NULL`. Optional nonnegative accumulator; checked per-path nominal MAC terms added.
#' @return `OctaveMaps`: Differentiable high map and optional half-resolution low map.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace n = dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(17);
#' n::models::OctaveMaps x{n::ones({1, 8, 8, 6}), n::ones({1, 4, 4, 2}), 6, 2};
#' const auto y = n::models::OctaveConv(p, "o", x, 8, .25, 3, 1, 8);
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid dimensions/split/pooling alignment/BN settings, overflow, unsupported dtype or incompatible stored leaves.
#' @references - Chen et al. (2019), https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.05049; https://github.com/facebookresearch/OctConv
#' @seealso OctaveMaps, OctaveConv(), OctaveNorm(), OctResNet()
#' @md
