#' @param theta `Tensor`. Matching dtype/batch \[N,6\] or \[N,2,3\] output-to-input transforms.
#' @param out_height `integer`. Positive output row count.
#' @param out_width `integer`. Positive output column count.
#' @return `Tensor`: \[N,out_height,out_width,C\] bilinear zero-extended samples, differentiable in x/theta.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace n = dm::nn;
#' const auto theta = n::tensor({1., 0., 0., 0., 1., 0.}, {1, 6});
#' const auto y = n::models::AffineSample(n::ones({1, 9, 9, 1}), theta, 9, 9);
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid images, transform shape/batch/dtype, output sizes or incompatible stored leaves.
#' @references - Jaderberg et al. (2015), https://arxiv.org/abs/1506.02025
#' @seealso AffineSample(), SpatialTransformer(), StnMnistClassifier()
#' @md
#'
`AffineSample` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_737`, NULL, list(...))
#' Predict an identity-initialized affine map and differentiably warp input images.
#'
#' Localization uses biased He-uniform 5x5/20/ReLU, SAME 2x2/2 max
#' pool, another 5x5/20/ReLU/pool, Glorot dense 50/ReLU, then dense 6.
#' Theta head weights start at zero and bias (1,0,0,0,1,0), so new
#' transforms are identity within sampling roundoff. The localization
#' filters initially have zero derivatives through the zero head weights;
#' head updates can activate them later. No bounds constrain learned theta,
#' so off-image sampling can become blank and lose useful gradients.
#' No BN/dropout/loss/optimizer/fitting hidden. Store access needs caller
#' synchronization; leaves must outlive retained backward graphs.
