#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid images, transform shape/batch/dtype, output sizes or incompatible stored leaves.
#' @references - Jaderberg et al. (2015), https://arxiv.org/abs/1506.02025
#' @seealso AffineSample(), SpatialTransformer(), StnMnistClassifier()
#' @md
#'
`SpatialTransformer` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_738`, NULL, list(...))
#' Generate rotated/scaled/translated 42x42 MNIST using tensor affine sampling.
#'
#' Draw angles uniformly within +/-pi/4, scales .7..1.2 and independent
#' centre shifts in available room on a 42-pixel canvas. Extent is
#' 14*scale*(abs(cos)+abs(sin)); room=max(0,20.5-extent), matching
#' the source geometric ranges. Very large rotated squares can still crop.
#' Compute normalized inverse-map coefficients with tensors and AffineSample,
#' then floor(255*pixel+.5), clamp0..255 and divide255. All numerical
#' preprocessing stays in tensor operations under NoGradGuard; no host
#' pixel loops. The tensor RNG draw sequence differs from legacy interleaved
#' std::mt19937_64, so distributions/ranges match but images are not bitwise
#' identical to that source. Caller synchronizes shared RNG access. No fitting.
#' @usage
#' DistortMnist(images, generator)
#' @param images `Tensor`. Nonempty floating \[N,28,28,1\] normalized pixels in \[0,1\].
#' @param generator `Generator`. Borrowed mutable tensor RNG; advances for angle, scale and two shifts.
#' @return `DistortedMnistOutputs`: Detached warped/quantized images and their generated affine matrices.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace n = dm::nn;
#' n::Generator gen(101);
#' const auto data = n::models::DistortMnist(n::zeros({2, 28, 28, 1}), gen);
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid pixel shape/dtype/range or sampling arguments.
#' @references - Jaderberg et al. (2015), https://arxiv.org/abs/1506.02025
#' @seealso AffineSample(), SpatialTransformer()
#' @md
#'
`DistortMnist` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_739`, NULL, list(...))
#' Build the source 42-pixel MNIST CNN with an optional learned spatial transformer.
#'
#' Optional localization/affine sampling precedes biased He-uniform
