`PatchDetectorLogits` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_750`, NULL, list(...))
#' Match one class and compute tensor precision-envelope and sampled AP.
#'
#' The optional inclusive_voc switch preserves synthetic-scene source cutoffs;
#' it does not alter the default official VOC strict comparison.
#' Within each image, scores sort stably. VOC chooses maximum IoU even to an
#' already matched truth; duplicates become false positives and difficult hits
#' are ignored. COCO first prefers eligible noncrowd truths, skips matched regular
#' truths, allows repeated crowd hits, and uses intersection/detection-area for
#' crowds. Equal-IoU ties prefer first truth for VOC, last for COCO. COCO caps each
#' image/class at 100 detections before matching. All outcomes then sort stably
#' across images. No area ranges, segmentation, recall summary, or global max100
#' across classes is implied. No gradients or fitting. Tensor overlaps/cumsums,
#' precision envelopes and recall-grid sampling perform all metric arithmetic;
#' host flags and scalar extractions control discrete assignments. Recall grids use
#' k*(1./(S-1)), preserving source floating-point comparisons: 3*.1 lies
#' slightly above stored recall 3/10. Work includes
#' O(D*G) matching and O(D²+D*S) envelope/sampling for S=11 or101.
#' @usage
#' EvaluateDetectionClass(predictions, truth, images, label, threshold, coco, inclusive_voc = FALSE)
#' @param predictions `vector<DetectionEvaluationPrediction>`. Finite scored boxes; only selected image IDs and label contribute.
#' @param truth `vector<DetectionEvaluationTruth>`. Finite annotated boxes; difficult is ignored for VOC, crowd for COCO.
#' @param images `vector<integer>`. Unique nonnegative selected image IDs; input order breaks cross-image score ties.
#' @param label `integer`. Nonnegative category identifier.
#' @param threshold `numeric`. Finite IoU cutoff in (0,1\]; strict greater for VOC and greater-or-equal for COCO.
#' @param coco `logical`. True for COCO 101-point/crowd/max100 rules; false for VOC 11-point/difficult rules.
#' @param inclusive_voc `logical`. Use >= in VOC mode for the synthetic-scene source convention; false by default, ignored for COCO.
#' @return `DetectionClassEvaluation`: Float64 AP scalars, recall/envelope tensors and positive count; AP -1 if no nonignored truth.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace m = dm::nn::models;
#' const auto r = m::EvaluateDetectionClass({{1, 0, .9f, {0, 0, 10, 20}}},
#'                                          {{1, 0, {0, 0, 10, 10}}}, {1}, 0, .5, true);
#' const auto ap = r.interpolated.item(); // 1
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For malformed coordinates/IDs, nonfinite scores, duplicate selected images or invalid label/cutoff.
#' @references - Everingham et al. (2010), The PASCAL Visual Object Classes (VOC) Challenge, https://doi.org/10.1007/s11263-009-0275-4; COCO reference evaluator, https://github.com/cocodataset/cocoapi/blob/master/PythonAPI/pycocotools/cocoeval.py
#' @seealso EvaluateDetectionDataset()
#' @md
#'
`EvaluateDetectionClass` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_751`, NULL, list(...))
#' Average dataset box AP over categories with selected nonignored positives.
#'
#' Calls EvaluateDetectionClass at .50:.05:.95 in COCO mode, or at .50 in
#' VOC mode. Absent or entirely ignored categories are excluded. Uses exact
#' .75 for the AP75 cutoff. COCO values are a limited all-area evaluator, not
#' the complete official evaluation suite. No parameter mutation or fitting.
#' @usage
#' EvaluateDetectionDataset(predictions, truth, images, coco, inclusive_voc = FALSE)
#' @param predictions `vector<DetectionEvaluationPrediction>`. Scored boxes; no model inference or score filtering is performed.
#' @param truth `vector<DetectionEvaluationTruth>`. Annotated boxes, including difficult and crowd flags.
#' @param images `vector<integer>`. Unique selected nonnegative image IDs, in tie-breaking order.
#' @param coco `logical`. True for all-area COCO-style box AP; false for VOC integral/11-point AP.
#' @param inclusive_voc `logical`. Forward the synthetic-scene inclusive VOC cutoff option; false by default.
#' @return `DetectionDatasetEvaluation`: Float64 tensor means and per-category AP50; empty eligible categories give zero means.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace m = dm::nn::models;
#' const auto r = m::EvaluateDetectionDataset({{1, 0, .9f, {0, 0, 10, 10}}},
#'                                            {{1, 0, {0, 0, 10, 10}}}, {1}, true);
#' const auto ap = r.ap.item(); // 1
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For malformed records or selected image IDs as in EvaluateDetectionClass().
#' @references - Everingham et al. (2010), The PASCAL Visual Object Classes (VOC) Challenge, https://doi.org/10.1007/s11263-009-0275-4; COCO reference evaluator, https://github.com/cocodataset/cocoapi/blob/master/PythonAPI/pycocotools/cocoeval.py
#' @seealso EvaluateDetectionClass()
#' @md
#'
`EvaluateDetectionDataset` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_752`, NULL, list(...))
#' Generate detection scenes using tensor interpolation, quantization and compositing.
#'
#' Each object gets up to thirty placement attempts. Cells use half-pixel bilinear
#' sampling with border clamping, then positive half-up byte rounding. Boxes bound
#' pixels strictly above32. Accepted patches combine by maximum, not addition.
#' Discrete draws preserve legacy mt19937_64 draw order. Float64 tensor arithmetic
#' replaces host interpolation; borderline rounding may differ by one byte.
#' Input graphs are not retained; the routine neither fits nor mutates inputs.
#' Work is proportional to scene pixels and attempted cell pixels.
#' @usage
#' MakeTensorDetectionScenes(digits, labels, cfg = DetectionSceneConfig$new())
#' @param digits `Tensor`. Float32/64 \[N,28,28,1\] in \[0,1\], N positive; restored to nearest source byte before resampling.
#' @param labels `Tensor`. Int64 \[N\] digit classes in \[0,9\], matching digits.
#' @param cfg `DetectionSceneConfig`. Positive valid scene dimensions, placement limits, overlap and seed.
#' @return `TensorDetectionScenes`: Detached normalized scene images and aligned per-image box/label tensors.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace n = dm::nn;
#' n::models::DetectionSceneConfig cfg;
#' cfg.scenes = 2;
#' const auto scenes = n::models::MakeTensorDetectionScenes(n::ones({1, 28, 28, 1}),
#'                                                          n::zeros({1}, n::DType::Int64), cfg);
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
