#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid rank, last dimension or dtype.
#' @references - Tian et al. (2019), FCOS: Fully Convolutional One-Stage Object Detection, https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.01355
#' @seealso MakeFcosTargets()
#' @md
#'
`FcosCenterness` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_798`, NULL, list(...))
#' Compute source FCOS IoU loss with plus-one area smoothing.
#'
#' The additive one is area smoothing, not a small epsilon. Distances share a
#' reference point, so intersection sides sum minima. No mutation or fitting.
#' @usage
#' FcosIouLoss(prediction, target)
#' @param prediction `Tensor`. Float32/64 \[N,P,4\] nonnegative l,t,r,b distances; finite values are caller requirement.
#' @param target `Tensor`. Same-shape/dtype nonnegative target distances.
#' @return `Tensor`: \[N,P\] -log((intersection+1)/(union+1)), with gradients to both arguments.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' const auto loss =
#'     dm::nn::models::FcosIouLoss(dm::nn::ones({1, 2, 4}), dm::nn::full({1, 2, 4}, 2.));
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
