`YoloV5Loss` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_859`, NULL, list(...))
#' Assign ratio-matched priors to base and eligible axial neighbour cells using tensors.
#'
#' A prior matches iff every dimension ratio<4; if none, best shape IoU
#' (first ties) is fallback. Each matched prior assigns base plus one vertical
#' and one horizontal neighbour when fractional centre is below/above.5.
#' Exact.5 copies neither axis. Slot conflicts keep greater shape IoU, first
#' truth on ties. Current input pixels=coarse_grid*32. No fitting or random draws.
#' @usage
#' MakeYoloV5Targets(raw, priors, scenes, rows)
#' @param raw `vector<Tensor>`. Three same-dtype \[N,G,G,3,5+C\] heads with grids doubling coarse to fine.
#' @param priors `Tensor`. Same-dtype positive finite \[9,2\] input-pixel height,width priors.
#' @param scenes `TensorDetectionScenes`. Valid same-dtype grayscale scene metadata with in-canvas positive boxes and Int64 labels<C.
#' @param rows `vector<integer>`. Dataset IDs matching batch order.
#' @return `YoloV5Targets`: Detached target levels and discarded/replaced candidate collision count.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace n = dm::nn;
#' std::array<n::Tensor, 3> raw = {n::zeros({1, 2, 2, 3, 7}), n::zeros({1, 4, 4, 3, 7}),
#'                                 n::zeros({1, 8, 8, 3, 7})};
#' const auto priors = n::full({9, 2}, 8.);
#' n::models::TensorDetectionScenes data;
#' data.images = n::zeros({1, 64, 64, 1});
#' data.boxes = {n::tensor({22., 22., 30., 30.}, {1, 4})};
#' data.labels = {n::ones({1}, n::DType::Int64)};
#' const auto targets = n::models::MakeYoloV5Targets(raw, priors, data, {0});
#' ```
