#' @return `Tensor`: Same-dtype sparse NHWC output with gradients to values only.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace n = dm::nn;
#' const auto record = n::models::SegNetPoolWithIndices(n::ones({2, 5, 7, 2}));
#' const auto restored = n::models::SegNetIndexUnpool(record.values, record);
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid geometry,dtypes,indices or configuration.
#' @references - Badrinarayanan,Kendall and Cipolla(2015), SegNet: A Deep Convolutional Encoder-Decoder Architecture for Image Segmentation, https://arxiv.org/abs/1511.00561; original implementation https://github.com/alexgkendall/SegNet-Tutorial.
#' @seealso SegNetPoolWithIndices()
#' @md
