#' @param label `integer`. In-range class channel.
#' @param box `Tensor`. Floating\[4\] finite ordered pixel edges,ymin,xmin,ymax,xmax;converted to probability dtype.
#' @param height `integer`. Positive output canvas height.
#' @param width `integer`. Positive output canvas width.
#' @return `Tensor`: Detached Bool\[height,width\] support after inclusive probability threshold.5.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace n = dm::nn;
#' const auto mask = n::models::PasteInstanceMask(n::full({2, 2, 1}, .75), 0,
#'                                                n::tensor({1., 1., 5., 5.}), 6, 6);
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid shapes,dtypes,classes or scene geometry.
#' @references - He et al.(2017), Mask R-CNN, https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.06870; synthetic support/paste/AP conventions from examples/nn/common/instance_segmentation.hpp. MNIST source LeCun et al.(1998), https://doi.org/10.1109/5.726791.
#' @seealso InstanceMaskIoU()
#' @md
#'
`PasteInstanceMask` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_913`, NULL, list(...))
#' Evaluate class-mean integral all-point AP of scored binary instance supports.
#'
#' Predictions sort by descending confidence with stable original-order ties.
#' Each selects its highest-IoU same-class/same-image truth,first on ties,even
#' if that truth was already used;duplicates become false positives rather than
#' rematching another target. True/false-positive cumsums and the suffix precision
#' envelope integrate all recall changes. Absent target classes are excluded.
#' Mask intersections use exact Float64 products/counts of Boolean indicators.
#' This is the source small-scene integral metric,not official COCO101-point/
#' crowd/area/maxDets evaluation. No fitting,randomness or input mutation.
#' @usage
#' InstanceMaskAveragePrecision(predictions, scenes, classes, threshold = 0.5)
#' @param predictions `TensorMaskDetections`. Aligned finite floating scores,Int64 class/image IDs,Bool\[M,H,W\] masks;boxes\[M,4\] are ignored geometrically.
#' @param scenes `TensorInstanceScenes`. Aligned grayscale scene metadata and Bool\[Ki,H,W\] instance supports,including empty objects.
#' @param classes `integer`. Positive class count;all truth/prediction labels in\[0,classes).
#' @param threshold `numeric`. Finite mask IoU threshold in\[0,1\],default.5;matching is inclusive.
#' @return `Tensor`: Detached Float64 scalar mean AP across classes with targets,or0 if none.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace n = dm::nn;
#' n::models::TensorInstanceScenes data;
#' data.images = n::zeros({1, 2, 2, 1});
#' data.boxes = {n::tensor({0., 0., 2., 2.}, {1, 4})};
#' data.labels = {n::zeros({1}, n::DType::Int64)};
#' data.masks = {n::ones({1, 2, 2}, n::DType::Bool)};
