#' @param threshold `numeric`. Finite overlap cutoff in\[0,1\],default.5;strictly greater overlap suppresses.
#' @param top_k `integer`. Nonnegative per-image/class descending-score budget,default200.
#' @param limit `integer`. Nonnegative final per-image detection budget,default100.
#' @return `Tensor`: Detached Int64 selected input indices,image order then descending score.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace n = dm::nn;
#' n::models::TensorDetections d{
#'     n::tensor({0., 0., 10., 10., 0., 4., 10., 14., 0., 8., 10., 18.}, {3, 4}),
#'     n::tensor({.9, .8, .7}), n::zeros({3}, n::DType::Int64), n::zeros({3}, n::DType::Int64)};
#' const auto kept = n::models::TensorFastNms(d, .3);
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid settings,shapes,dtypes,nonfinite predictions or out-of-range IDs.
#' @references - Bolya et al.(2019), YOLACT: Real-time Instance Segmentation, https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.02689; teaching pixel-centre crops and mask pasting follow examples/nn/common/yolact.hpp.
#' @seealso SuppressDetectionCandidates(), DecodeTensorYolact()
#' @md
#'
`TensorFastNms` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_931`, NULL, list(...))
#' Decode YOLACT class boxes,Fast NMS and cropped shared-prototype instance masks.
#'
#' Background last is excluded. Decode default-variance offsets/log scales
#' clipped4,clip boxes to canvas,discard zero area,retain class score>.05.
#' Fast NMS.5/top200 per class/cap100 per image selects candidates. Combine
#' matching coefficients with same-image prototypes,clip logits\[-80,80\],
#' sigmoid,crop on prototype pixel centres,no one-pixel box expansion,then
#' bilinearly paste full-canvas probabilities and threshold>=.5. Inference
#' products form in model dtype then sum in Float64,matching the old source
#' accumulation policy. No learned updates,fitting or retained gradients.
#' @usage
#' DecodeTensorYolact(net, anchors, rows, height, width)
#' @param net `YolactOutputs`. Consistent finite YOLACT probability/delta/coefficient/prototype outputs for rows.
#' @param anchors `Tensor`. Same-dtype\[A,4\] prior boxes in network anchor order.
