#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For nonpositive requested output time.
#' @references - Zhang,Zhao and LeCun(2015),Character-level Convolutional Networks for Text Classification, https://arxiv.org/abs/1509.01626. Source binary MR adaptation keeps six7/7/3/3/3/3 convolutions,three VALID3pools,two dense/ReLU/dropout layers and the69-slot alphabet. Teaching source uses He-uniform conv/Glorot dense initialization,not a claim of exact paper training or benchmark accuracy.
#' @seealso CharacterAlphabet, CharacterCnn()
#' @md
#'
`CharacterEncode` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_979`, NULL, list(...))
#' Compute the exact retained length after six VALID convolutions and three pools.
