#' CharacterCnn(p, ids, lengths, config = CharacterConfig$new(), training = FALSE, keep = 1.0, gen = NULL)
#' @param p `ParameterStore`. Mutable learned store;warm all18 leaves before optimizer creation.
#' @param ids `Tensor`. Int32/64\[N,time\] categorical IDs-1..alphabet-1,N>0;unknown/PAD=-1.
#' @param lengths `Tensor`. Int32/64\[N\] observed lengths0..time;outside-length positions mask to0.
#' @param config `CharacterConfig`. Valid retained time,positive conv/dense widths and onehot depth.
#' @param training `logical`. False by default;true activates caller-generator dropout after both dense ReLUs.
#' @param keep `numeric`. Finite dropout keep probability(0,1\],default1;source fit.5.
#' @param gen `Generator or NULL`. Required mutable generator only when training&&keep<1;otherwise unused.
#' @return `CharacterOutput`: Raw binary logits,masked onehot inputs,flattened pool and all9temporal stages.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace n = dm::nn;
#' namespace m = n::models;
#' n::ParameterStore p(2);
#' const auto out =
#'     m::CharacterCnn(p, n::zeros({2, 256}, n::DType::Int32),
#'                     n::full({2}, 200., n::DType::Int32), m::CharacterConfig{256, 16, 64, 69});
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid architecture,input IDs/lengths,dropout policy or stored leaves.
#' @references - Zhang,Zhao and LeCun(2015),Character-level Convolutional Networks for Text Classification, https://arxiv.org/abs/1509.01626. Source binary MR adaptation keeps six7/7/3/3/3/3 convolutions,three VALID3pools,two dense/ReLU/dropout layers and the69-slot alphabet. Teaching source uses He-uniform conv/Glorot dense initialization,not a claim of exact paper training or benchmark accuracy.
#' @seealso CharacterEncode(), CharacterFinalLength()
#' @md
#'
