#'
#' Uses decoder/W\[latent,hidden\], decoder/b\[hidden\], output/W\[hidden,features\],
#' output/b\[features\], ordinary Glorot-uniform weights and zero biases. The same
#' names are used by BetaVariationalAutoencoder(); reuse its store for inference.
#' Only code enters, with no image, posterior, RNG or hidden sigmoid. Finite signed
#' or zero matching Float32/64 codes retain code/parameter gradients and strides.
#' Input checks precede leaf creation; incompatible stored leaves can fail later.
#' Nonfinite computed values propagate. Inputs unchanged; output owns lifetime.
#' Work O(B*hidden*(latent+features)); shared stores need external synchronization.
#' @usage
#' GaussianVaeDecode(parameters, code, features = 784, latent = 4, hidden = 32)
#' @param parameters `ParameterStore`. Mutable floating store containing or creating decoder leaves.
#' @param code `Tensor`. Finite nonempty \[B,latent\] code with store dtype.
#' @param features `integer`. Positive output width, default784.
#' @param latent `integer`. Positive code width, default4.
#' @param hidden `integer`. Positive ReLU width, default32.
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning differentiable logits \[B,features\]; sigmoid gives probabilities.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(2237);
#' const auto probabilities=n::sigmoid(n::models::GaussianVaeDecode(p,n::zeros({2,4})));
#' // [2,784] probabilities, not sampled Bernoulli pixels.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid widths/code/dtype or incompatible leaves.
#' @references - Kingma and Welling (2013/2014), https://arxiv.org/abs/1312.6114 . This small
#'   migrated ReLU decoder is an educational architecture, not a benchmark reproduction.
#' @seealso BetaVariationalAutoencoder(), GaussianReparameterize()
#' @md
#'
`GaussianVaeDecode` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1010`, NULL, list(...))
#' Evaluate a beta-weighted diagonal-Gaussian VAE with caller-supplied posterior noise.
#'
#' Architecture: features->hidden ReLU->separate linear mu/log_variance heads,
#' sample z=mu+exp(log_variance/2)*epsilon, then GaussianVaeDecode(). Names/order
#' are encoder/W,b; mu/W,b; log_variance/W,b; decoder/W,b; output/W,b. Ordinary
#' Glorot-uniform weights and zero biases give10 leaves/51416 default scalars.
#' Pixel NLL and latent KL are SUMMED, then images are averaged. beta=1 is a
#' single-draw negative ELBO; beta>1 strengthens KL but does not guarantee
#' disentanglement. No annealing, sampling, training, clipping or factor labels
#' are hidden. Independent explicit noise banks are the caller's responsibility.
#'
#' Finite unit-range images and finite noise must match store Float32/64 dtype.
#' Continuous image, epsilon and all leaf derivatives are retained. Input/beta
#' checks precede creation; incompatible stored leaves/nonfinite computed states
#' can fail later. beta must remain finite positive when cast to store dtype.
#' No inputs mutated; output owns lifetime. Work O(B*hidden*(features+latent)),
#' activation storage O(B*(features+hidden+latent)); synchronize shared stores.
#' @usage
#' BetaVariationalAutoencoder(parameters, image, epsilon, beta = 1.0, features = 784, latent = 4, hidden = 32)
#' @param parameters `ParameterStore`. Mutable floating parameter store.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Finite nonempty \[B,features\] pixel rows in \[0,1\].
#' @param epsilon `Tensor`. Explicit finite \[B,latent\] standard-normal noise, same dtype.
#' @param beta `numeric`. Finite positive KL weight, default1.
#' @param features `integer`. Positive pixel width, default784.
#' @param latent `integer`. Positive latent width, default4.
#' @param hidden `integer`. Positive encoder/decoder ReLU width, default32.
#' @return `GaussianVaeOutput`: Owning nine-field GaussianVaeOutput including weighted/unweighted losses.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(2237);
#' const auto
#' noise=n::cast(n::select(n::models::GaussianNoise({2,4},1,2252),0,0),n::DType::Float32); const
#' auto out=n::models::BetaVariationalAutoencoder(p,n::full({2,784},.2),noise,4); const auto
#' gradients=n::grad(out.loss,p.parameters()); // all10 leaves; no update is hidden.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs/options or incompatible leaves;
#'   nonfinite computed posterior/logits may fail validation later.
#' @references - Kingma and Welling (2013/2014), https://arxiv.org/abs/1312.6114 .
#' - Higgins et al. (2017), beta-VAE: Learning Basic Visual Concepts with a
#'   Constrained Variational Framework, https://openreview.net/forum?id=Sy2fzU9gl .
#'   Uses the migrated small ReLU/Bernoulli model, not the paper's benchmark metric.
#' @seealso GaussianVaeOutput, GaussianReparameterize(), DiagonalGaussianKl(), GaussianVaeDecode(), BernoulliPixelNll()
#' @md
#'
`BetaVariationalAutoencoder` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1011`, NULL, list(...))
#' Decode explicit Gaussian-latent codes through projection, nearest repetition and convolutions.
#'
#' Projects code with decoder_projection/W,b to (H/4)*(W/4)*base_channels ReLU
#' values, reshapes NHWC, repeats each spatial value2x2, applies same-padded3x3
#' base_channels->channels ReLU, repeats2x2 again and applies same-padded3x3
#' channels->1 linear logits. Names/order: decoder_projection/W,b; decoder1/W,b;
#' decoder2/W,b. Projection uses ordinary Glorot-uniform weights even with ReLU;
#' decoder1 uses He uniform, decoder2 Glorot uniform, all biases zero. Default
#' six leaves/957 scalars. This is neither transposed convolution nor a spatial
#' feature bypass. Signed/zero finite codes are accepted; only code enters.
#'
#' Positive H/W multiples of four and flattened widths are checked before leaf
#' creation. Strided Float32/64 codes match the store and retain code/parameter
#' gradients. Returned fields own lifetime; no input mutation, RNG, fitting,
#' clipping or implicit detachment. Incompatible stored leaves can fail later;
#' nonfinite parameters/computed values are not sanitized. Work/storage scale
#' linearly with B*H*W for fixed channel/latent widths. Synchronize shared stores.
#' @usage
#' ConvolutionalVaeDecode(parameters, code, height = 28, width = 28, latent = 2, channels = 8, base_channels = 4)
#' @param parameters `ParameterStore`. Mutable Float32/64 store containing/creating decoder leaves.
#' @param code `Tensor`. Finite nonempty \[B,latent\] code matching store dtype.
#' @param height `integer`. Positive output height divisible by four, default28.
#' @param width `integer`. Positive output width divisible by four, default28.
#' @param latent `integer`. Positive code width, default2.
#' @param channels `integer`. Positive first decoder hidden channels, default8.
#' @param base_channels `integer`. Positive quarter-resolution channels, default4.
#' @return `ConvolutionalVaeDecoderOutput`: Owning five-field decoder endpoints, with flattened probabilities.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(2011);
#' const auto out=n::models::ConvolutionalVaeDecode(p,n::ones({1,1}),4,4,1,2,1);
#' // Spatial logits[1,4,4,1], flattened logits[1,16], six leaves/41 scalars.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid geometry/code/dtype or incompatible leaves.
#' @references - Kingma and Welling (2013/2014), Auto-Encoding Variational Bayes,
#'   https://arxiv.org/abs/1312.6114 . This small repeat/convolution teaching
#'   architecture is repository-specific, not a benchmark configuration.
#' - He, Zhang, Ren and Sun (2015), Delving Deep into Rectifiers,
#'   https://arxiv.org/abs/1502.01852 , for the ReLU convolution initialization.
#' @seealso ConvolutionalVariationalAutoencoder(), upsample_nearest()
#' @md
#'
`ConvolutionalVaeDecode` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1012`, NULL, list(...))
#' Evaluate a spatial diagonal-Gaussian/Bernoulli VAE with explicit posterior noise and no skips.
#'
#' Encoder: same-padded3x3 grayscale->channels ReLU, nonoverlapping2x2 average
#' pool, same-padded3x3 channels->base_channels ReLU, another average pool, then
#' separate linear Gaussian mean/log-variance heads of width latent. Samples use
#' GaussianReparameterize(); ONLY z enters ConvolutionalVaeDecode(). The pooled
#' feature map is never forwarded as a deterministic decoder input. Fourteen
#' default leaves/2117 scalars have names/order encoder1/W,b; encoder2/W,b;
#' mu/W,b; log_variance/W,b; decoder_projection/W,b; decoder1/W,b; decoder2/W,b.
#' ReLU convolutions use He uniform; dense heads, ReLU dense projection and output
#' convolution use ordinary Glorot uniform; all biases zero.
#'
#' Bernoulli NLL sums H*W pixels and analytic Gaussian KL sums latent coordinates,
#' then images are averaged: loss=mean(NLL+KL), beta1. Binary targets give a
#' one-draw negative-ELBO estimate; soft \[0,1\] targets give cross-entropy, not a
#' continuous-observation likelihood density. Fixed N(0,I) prior, no annealing,
#' hidden sampling, labels, fitting, validation selection or clipping. Strides
#' and continuous image/epsilon/leaf gradients are retained. Input checks precede
#' creation; incompatible leaves/nonfinite computed states may fail later.
#' Returned fields own lifetime; inputs unchanged. Work/storage are linear in
#' B*H*W for fixed latent/channel widths. Shared stores require synchronization.
#' @usage
#' ConvolutionalVariationalAutoencoder(parameters, image, epsilon, latent = 2, channels = 8, base_channels = 4)
#' @param parameters `ParameterStore`. Mutable floating store matching image/epsilon dtype.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Finite nonempty Float32/64 NHWC \[B,H,W,1\] pixels in \[0,1\]; H/W positive multiples
#'   of four.
#' @param epsilon `Tensor`. Explicit finite \[B,latent\] standard-normal noise, same dtype/batch.
#' @param latent `integer`. Positive Gaussian code width, default2.
#' @param channels `integer`. Positive first encoder/decoder hidden channels, default8.
#' @param base_channels `integer`. Positive quarter-resolution channels, default4.
#' @return `ConvolutionalVaeOutput`: Owning sixteen-field Gaussian/spatial forward endpoints.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(2011);
#' const auto
#' out=n::models::ConvolutionalVariationalAutoencoder(p,n::full({2,28,28,1},.2),n::zeros({2,2}));
#' const auto gradients=n::grad(out.loss,p.parameters()); //14 gradients; no update is hidden.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid input/geometry/dtype or incompatible leaves;
#'   nonfinite computed posterior/logits can fail validation later.
#' @references - Kingma and Welling (2013/2014), https://arxiv.org/abs/1312.6114 .
#' - He et al. (2015), https://arxiv.org/abs/1502.01852 . This small pooled
#'   repeat-decoder architecture matches the migrated source, not a published benchmark.
#' @seealso ConvolutionalVaeOutput, ConvolutionalVaeDecode(), GaussianReparameterize(), DiagonalGaussianKl(), BernoulliPixelNll()
#' @md
#'
`ConvolutionalVariationalAutoencoder` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1013`, NULL, list(...))
#' Select nearest vectors and expose independent straight-through/dictionary/commitment paths.
#'
#' Distance is sum(encoded^2)+sum(book^2)-2*encoded*book^T in the input dtype.
#' Detached argmin chooses the lowest index on ties, including duplicate vectors.
#' An optional Int32 override with N elements replaces assignments; its shape
#' may be \[N\] or a grid. All IDs are checked before lookup. The forward surrogate
#' is stop(quantized)+(encoded-stop(encoded)), avoiding cancellation against
#' encoded; signed zero may normalize. Its identity encoded Jacobian is a
#' surrogate, not the derivative of nearest-neighbour selection. Reconstruction
#' through it gives no book gradient. Dictionary and commitment terms average
#' ALL N*D elements, with opposite targets detached. Available continuous higher
#' paths remain live; no derivative is defined through indices or tie changes.
#' Finite nonempty matching Float32/64 encoded\[N,D\],book\[K,D\] accept strides.
#' Overflowed computed distances are rejected; other computed overflow propagates.
#' Inputs unchanged; owning fields. Work O(N*K*D), storage O(N*K+N*D). No RNG/state.
#' @usage
#' VectorQuantize(encoded, book, entries = 16, dimensions = 4, override_indices = Tensor$new())
#' @param encoded `Tensor`. Finite nonempty floating matrix\[N,dimensions\].
#' @param book `Tensor`. Finite matching matrix\[entries,dimensions\].
#' @param entries `integer`. Positive Int32 vocabulary size, default16.
#' @param dimensions `integer`. Positive embedding width, default4.
#' @param override_indices `Tensor`. Optional valid Int32 tensor with N elements; undefined selects nearest.
#' @return `VectorQuantizedOutput`: Owning six-field quantization record with explicit gradient routing.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' auto e=n::tensor({{.2,.1}}).requires_grad_(),b=n::tensor({{0.,0.},{1.,0.}}).requires_grad_();
#' auto q=n::models::VectorQuantize(e,b,2,2);
#' const auto g=n::grad(n::sum(q.straight_through),{e,b},{.allow_unused=true});
#' // g[0] is [[1,1]], while g[1] is undefined: no reconstruction path to book.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid shapes/dtypes/values/IDs, distance overflow or
#'   products.
#' @references - van den Oord, Vinyals and Kavukcuoglu (2017), Neural Discrete Representation
#'   Learning, https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.00937 . Uses gradient dictionary updates,
#'   element-mean penalties and a detached identity surrogate, not EMA updates.
#' @seealso VqLookup(), VectorQuantizedOutput, straight_through()
#' @md
#'
`VectorQuantize` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1014`, NULL, list(...))
#' Look up a discrete image-by-token code grid without an encoder or targets.
#'
#' Int32 IDs\[B,T\] must be nonempty in \[0,K); book\[K,D\] must be finite nonempty
#' Float32/64. Returns flattened \[B*T,D\] in row-major order with live book paths,
#' accepting strides. IDs have no gradient. Inputs unchanged; owning result.
#' Work O(B*T*K*D), storage O(B*T*K+B*T*D), using the same one-hot matmul as VQ.
#' @usage
#' VqLookup(ids, book, entries = 16)
#' @param ids `Tensor`. Valid nonempty Int32\[B,T\] grid.
#' @param book `Tensor`. Finite floating\[K,D\] dictionary.
#' @param entries `integer`. Positive vocabulary size, default16, equal to book rows.
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning lookup vectors\[B*T,D\] differentiable to book.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' const auto
#' codes=n::models::VqLookup(n::from_vector(std::vector<int>{1,0},{1,2}),n::tensor({{0.,0.},{1.,2.}}),2);
#' // codes is [[1,2],[0,0]], flattened in image/token order.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid grid/book/dtype/values or overflowing products.
#' @references - van den Oord et al. (2017), https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.00937 , discrete dictionary lookup.
#' @seealso VectorQuantize(), VqDecoder()
#' @md
#'
`VqLookup` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1015`, NULL, list(...))
#' Decode a flattened quarter-resolution code lattice to Bernoulli logits.
#'
#' Reshapes codes\[B*T,D\] to \[B,H/4,W/4,D\], repeat2, same Conv3 D->C/ReLU,
#' repeat2, same Conv3 C->1/linear, then flattens pixels to \[B,H*W\]. T=H*W/16.
#' Uses decoder1/W,b (He uniform/zero bias) and output/W,b (ordinary Glorot/zero
#' bias), exactly shared with VectorQuantizedAutoencoder(). Default four leaves
#' contain369 scalars. Codes alone enter: no image, book, RNG draws or fit.
#' Finite Float32/64 codes must match store dtype; strides and all continuous
#' code/parameter paths remain. Geometry/input checks precede leaf creation;
#' incompatible existing leaves can fail later. Inputs unchanged; output owns
#' lifetime. Work O(B*H*W*9*C*(D+1)); synchronize mutations of a shared store.
#' @usage
#' VqDecoder(parameters, codes, height = 28, width = 28, dimensions = 4, channels = 8)
#' @param parameters `ParameterStore`. Mutable floating decoder parameter store.
#' @param codes `Tensor`. Finite nonempty flattened vectors\[B*T,dimensions\].
#' @param height `integer`. Positive output height divisible by four, default28.
#' @param width `integer`. Positive output width divisible by four, default28.
#' @param dimensions `integer`. Positive embedding width, default4.
#' @param channels `integer`. Positive hidden channels, default8.
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning differentiable logits\[B,H*W\], without sigmoid clipping.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(2707);
#' const auto probability=n::sigmoid(n::models::VqDecoder(p,n::zeros({49,4})));
#' // One target-free probability image[1,784]; four decoder leaves.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid geometry/input/dtype/products or incompatible leaves.
#' @references - van den Oord et al. (2017), https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.00937 . Compact
#'   repeat/convolution teaching architecture, not the paper's full model.
#' @seealso VqLookup(), VectorQuantizedAutoencoder()
#' @md
#'
`VqDecoder` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1016`, NULL, list(...))
#' Evaluate a compact spatial VQ-VAE with explicit surrogate gradient routes.
#'
#' Unit-range grayscale NHWC\[B,H,W,1\], B>0, H/W divisible by four: same Conv3
#' 1->C/ReLU, avg2, same Conv3 C->D/ReLU, avg2, nearest K-vector dictionary,
#' then VqDecoder(). He-uniform encoder/hidden decoder, ordinary Glorot output,
#' zero biases, codebook U(-.5,.5). Creation order is encoder1/W,b, encoder2/W,b,
#' codebook, decoder1/W,b, output/W,b; default9 leaves/805 scalars. Loss averages
#' pixel-summed stable Bernoulli NLL over B, adds element-mean dictionary square
#' and beta times element-mean commitment square. Reconstruction follows the
#' identity surrogate to encoded and skips book; neither an exact argmin
#' derivative nor a Gaussian/pixel likelihood ELBO is claimed. No EMA, resets,
#' prior fitting, sampling, RNG noise or optimizer is hidden. Parameter creation
#' uses the caller's store initializer stream. Finite matching Float32/64 inputs
#' accept strides and preserve intended gradients. Checks precede leaf creation;
#' incompatible stored leaves/computed overflow can fail later. Owning outputs;
#' inputs unchanged. Work O(B*H*W*9*C*(D+1)+B*H*W*K*D/16); synchronize shared stores.
#' @usage
#' VectorQuantizedAutoencoder(parameters, image, entries = 16, dimensions = 4, channels = 8, commitment_beta = 0.25)
#' @param parameters `ParameterStore`. Mutable floating store creating/reusing all nine leaves.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Finite unit-range nonempty Float32/64 grayscale NHWC\[B,H,W,1\].
#' @param entries `integer`. Positive Int32 vocabulary size, default16.
#' @param dimensions `integer`. Positive embedding width, default4.
#' @param channels `integer`. Positive hidden channel width, default8.
#' @param commitment_beta `numeric`. Finite nonnegative commitment multiplier, default0.25, representable in
#'   dtype.
#' @return `VectorQuantizedAutoencoderOutput`: Owning spatial/quantization/probability/objective record.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(2707);
#' auto out=n::models::VectorQuantizedAutoencoder(p,n::full({2,28,28,1},.3));
#' const auto gradients=n::grad(out.loss,p.parameters());
#' // All nine leaves are available to the caller's optimizer; no update occurs here.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs/options/products or incompatible leaves.
#' @references - van den Oord, Vinyals and Kavukcuoglu (2017), Neural Discrete Representation
#'   Learning, https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.00937 . Compact Bernoulli experiment,
#'   gradient-updated codebook and element-mean penalties; no PixelCNN prior.
#' @seealso VectorQuantize(), VqDecoder(), VqMarkovPrior
#' @md
#'
`VectorQuantizedAutoencoder` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1017`, NULL, list(...))
#' Count valid code symbols and return pooled empirical usage perplexity.
#'
#' Any nonempty Int32 shape is flattened; counts fit Int32 by limiting numel to
#' INT32_MAX. Zero-probability terms are omitted. A single used symbol gives1,
#' uniform use of K symbols gives K. Unused codes remain visible. Inputs unchanged;
#' owning counts, no gradients or shared state. Work O(N+K), storage O(N+K).
#' @usage
#' VqUsage(ids, entries = 16)
#' @param ids `Tensor`. Nonempty valid Int32 code tensor, any shape/strides.
#' @param entries `integer`. Positive Int32 vocabulary size, default16.
#' @return `VqCodeUsage`: Owning counts\[K\] and pooled usage perplexity, not a compression/likelihood score.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' const auto usage=dm::nn::models::VqUsage(dm::nn::zeros({2,3},dm::nn::DType::Int32));
#' // counts[0]=6, the other fifteen counts are0; perplexity=1.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid input, symbols, vocabulary or count overflow.
#' @references - van den Oord et al. (2017), https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.00937 , code-use diagnostics.
#' @seealso VqCodeUsage, VqMarkovPrior
#' @md
#'
`VqUsage` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1018`, NULL, list(...))
#' Decode flattened coarse vectors into the shared fine-resolution conditioning feature.
#'
#' Reshapes top\[B*T,D\] to \[B,H/4,W/4,D\], repeats spatially by two and applies
#' same Conv3 D->D/ReLU with top_decoder/W,b (He uniform/zero bias). T=H*W/16.
#' Defaults create two leaves/148 scalars and return\[B,14,14,4\]. Codes alone
#' enter; no image, dictionary, target, optimizer or random bank is required.
#' Finite matching Float32/64 codes accept strides and retain continuous first/
#' higher paths. Geometry/input checks precede leaves; incompatible stored
#' leaves can fail later. Inputs unchanged; owning output, no mode change.
#' Work O(B*H*W*9*D*D); synchronize shared-store mutations.
#' @usage
#' Vq2TopDecoder(parameters, top, height = 28, width = 28, dimensions = 4)
#' @param parameters `ParameterStore`. Mutable matching floating store with shared top_decoder leaves.
#' @param top `Tensor`. Finite nonempty flattened coarse vectors\[B*T,dimensions\].
#' @param height `integer`. Positive output image height divisible by four, default28.
#' @param width `integer`. Positive output image width divisible by four, default28.
#' @param dimensions `integer`. Positive embedding width, default4.
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning differentiable coarse-conditioned feature\[B,H/2,W/2,D\].
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(2801);
