`StarDomainLoss` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1082`, NULL, list(...))
#' Evaluate the explicit two-store three-domain game with a shared-generator round trip.
#'
#' Distinct matching Float32/64 G/D stores; finite signed matching CPU
#' source\[N,28,28,1\], positive N, strides allowed. Int32/64 CPU original/target\[N\]
#' in0..2; each may differ by row and target may equal original. Validate all
#' supplied images/domains and aliases before leaves. Source seeds6301/6311,
#' G1609/10 and D688/8 values/leaves,2297/18 total. G(source,target) returns fake;
#' G(fake,original) reconstructs source with the SAME G. D reads image alone.
#' G=(full fake-to1 source mean+fake-domain CE)+10*mean(abs(reconstruction-source));
#' D=half(real-to1 source mean+fake-to0 source mean)+real-domain CE. Preserve source
#' grouping; known transformed images/digit labels never enter either loss.
#' All applicable first/higher source/parameter paths live, including BOTH G calls
#' in reconstruction and current D in G partials. No hidden detach/capture,
#' optimizer, fitting, no-grad, batch state, noise or RNG after initialization.
#' Caller captures/steps D, then makes a fresh G forward through updated D with
#' same source/original/target batch and steps only G. Existing leaves/inputs
#' unchanged, only missing leaves initialize. Owning fields retain storage/graphs.
#' Stored-leaf/math errors may follow initialization. O(N) fixed-map work/storage;
#' synchronize shared stores.
#' @usage
#' StarGan(generator, critic, source, original, target)
#' @param generator `ParameterStore`. Distinct floating G store, source seed6301.
#' @param critic `ParameterStore`. Distinct same-dtype D store, source seed6311.
#' @param source `Tensor`. Finite signed matching floating CPU\[N,28,28,1\], positive N.
#' @param original `Tensor`. Aligned integer CPU\[N\] observed source domains0..2.
#' @param target `Tensor`. Aligned integer CPU\[N\] requested output domains0..2.
#' @return `StarGanOutput`: Owning StarGanOutput with fifteen live source fields and explicit objectives.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;n::ParameterStore g(6301),d(6311);
#' auto x=n::zeros({2,28,28,1});auto
#' o=n::zeros({2},n::DType::Int32),t=n::ones({2},n::DType::Int32); auto
#' out=n::models::StarGan(g,d,x,o,t);auto dd=n::grad(out.discriminator_loss,d.parameters());
#' // Caller applies D partials, makes a fresh forward, then captures/applies G partials.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid geometry, dtype, values, domain IDs or alignment.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Choi,Choi,Kim,Ha,Kim and Choo (2018), StarGAN: Unified Generative Adversarial Networks for
#'   Multi-Domain Image-to-Image Translation, https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.09020 . Compact teaching
#'   domains/maps differ from the paper architecture.
#' @seealso StarGanGenerate(), StarGanDiscriminate(), StarDomainLoss(), SplitStarDomains()
#' @md
#'
`StarGan` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1083`, NULL, list(...))
#' Evaluate stable relativistic-average logistic losses with live opposite-pool means.
#'
#' Finite matching Float32/64 CPU real\[N,1\],fake\[M,1\], positive counts; unequal
#' pools and strides allowed. rr=real-mean(fake),rf=fake-mean(real).
#' D=.5*(mean softplus(-rr)+mean softplus(rf));
#' G=.5*(mean softplus(rr)+mean softplus(-rf)), preserving source grouping.
#' Opposite-pool means remain live at every derivative order. A common score shift
#' cancels up to floating rounding. No sigmoid/log clipping, hidden detach, mutation,
#' RNG, fitting or optimizer. Owning outputs retain graphs/storage; inputs unchanged.
#' Nonfinite computed relatives/losses rejected. O(N+M) work/storage; synchronize
#' external writes. These source halves differ from LogisticGanObjectives defaults.
#' @usage
#' RelativisticAverageGan(real, fake)
#' @param real `Tensor`. Finite floating CPU\[N,1\] real raw scores, N>0.
#' @param fake `Tensor`. Finite matching floating CPU\[M,1\] fake raw scores, M>0.
#' @return `RelativisticGanLoss`: Owning RelativisticGanLoss with both losses and live rr/rf.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' auto real=n::tensor({-2.,0.,3.},{3,1},n::DType::Float64).requires_grad_();
#' auto fake=n::tensor({-1.,2.},{2,1},n::DType::Float64).requires_grad_();
#' auto loss=n::models::RelativisticAverageGan(real,fake);
#' auto partial=n::grad(loss.generator,{real,fake});
#' // G has nonzero partials through BOTH pools, including their cross-pool means.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid geometry, dtype, values, alignment, products, aliased
#'   stores or incompatible leaves.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Jolicoeur-Martineau(2018), The relativistic discriminator: a key element missing from standard
#'   GAN, https://arxiv.org/abs/1807.00734 ; Wang et al.(2018), https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.00219 .
#'   Source SR teaching game keeps explicit half-scaled pool means.
#' @seealso RelativisticGanLoss, LogisticGanObjectives(), AdversarialSR()
#' @md
#'
`RelativisticAverageGan` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1084`, NULL, list(...))
#' Generate compact x2 SRGAN/ESRGAN residual pixels using explicit bicubic input and BN mode.
