#' // Supplied zero-kernel fixture gives all1 features; real runs load official VGG values.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid geometry, dtype, values, alignment, products, aliased
#'   stores or incompatible leaves.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Simonyan and Zisserman(2015), Very Deep Convolutional Networks for Large-Scale Image
#'   Recognition, https://arxiv.org/abs/1409.1556 ; Ledig et al.(2017),
#'   https://arxiv.org/abs/1609.04802 ; Wang et al.(2018), https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.00219 . Source
#'   first-layer content features are a compact teaching adaptation.
#' @seealso VggImageNetInput(), AdversarialSR()
#' @md
#'
`AdversarialSRFeatures` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1087`, NULL, list(...))
#' Evaluate explicit compact SRGAN/ESRGAN pixel/content/adversarial phases without fitting.
#'
#' Three distinct matching Float32/64 G,D,stats stores. Finite signed matching
#' CPU lr\[N,16,16,3\],target/bicubic\[N,32,32,3\], N>0 aligned; frozen matching1792
#' feature values as AdversarialSRFeatures. All supplied inputs/aliases/products
#' validate before leaves. Source seeds7001/7013/0. Both saved-statistic and batch-
#' statistic G paths always evaluate; stats unchanged beyond initialization.
#' G1591/25,D1673/8,BN40/10(default SRGAN), or G3511/40,D1672/7,no BN(ESRGAN).
#' Objectives read training G: SRGAN pixelMSE, post-ReLU featureMSE; ESRGAN pixelL1,
#' pre-activation featureL1. Both feature tensors divide by255 BEFORE loss. Frozen
#' weights/bias always stop; target extracted features stop, target pixel/real-score
#' paths remain live. SRGAN D is full real/fake logistic mean sum, G adversarial
#' is full nonsaturating mean. ESRGAN uses live relativistic means and half-scaled
#' D/G terms. gan_loss=content+double(float(.001 or .005))*adversarial;
#' ESRGAN adds double(float(.01))*pixel. g_loss=(1-phase)*pixel+phase*gan_loss,
#' phase=adversarial?1:0, computing all components even during warm-up.
#' No fitting, hidden no-grad, partial capture, weight/statistic write or later RNG.
#' Only missing leaves initialize. Caller owns16 pixel-only G steps, resets BOTH
#' Adam states without changing weights/stats, then D capture/write followed by a
#' fresh G capture/write on the same batch. After each G weight write, explicitly
#' commit BN moving candidates from the detached moments captured WITH that G
#' partial, momentum double(.9f). Never recompute moments after writing weights.
#' BN state and1792 frozen feature values are excluded from optimizers; no generator
#' weight EMA exists. Applicable first/higher paths remain live. Owning fields keep
#' storage/graphs; stored-leaf/state/math errors may follow initialization. O(N)
#' fixed-map work/storage, largest features\[N,32,32,64\]; synchronize stores.
#' @usage
#' AdversarialSR(generator, critic, stats, lr, target, bicubic, feature_weight, feature_bias, enhanced = FALSE, adversarial = FALSE)
#' @param generator `ParameterStore`. Caller-owned floating G store, source seed7001.
#' @param critic `ParameterStore`. Distinct same-dtype D store, source seed7013.
#' @param stats `ParameterStore`. Distinct same-dtype saved BN store, source seed0; excluded from optimizers.
#' @param lr `Tensor`. Finite matching CPU\[N,16,16,3\] low-resolution inputs.
#' @param target `Tensor`. Finite aligned matching CPU\[N,32,32,3\] HR targets, never G inputs.
#' @param bicubic `Tensor`. Finite aligned matching CPU\[N,32,32,3\] external LR-derived image shortcut.
#' @param feature_weight `Tensor`. Finite matching CPU\[3,3,3,64\] actual frozen feature values.
#' @param feature_bias `Tensor`. Finite matching CPU\[64\] actual frozen bias.
#' @param enhanced `logical`. Select ESRGAN(true), otherwise SRGAN(false default).
#' @param adversarial `logical`. Select content/adversarial G objective(true), otherwise pixel warm-up(false
#'   default).
#' @return `AdversarialSROutput`: Owning AdversarialSROutput with all source fields and detached optional BN captures.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;n::ParameterStore g(7001),d(7013),s(0);
#' auto lr=n::zeros({2,16,16,3}),hr=n::zeros({2,32,32,3});
#' auto out=n::models::AdversarialSR(g,d,s,lr,hr,hr,n::zeros({3,3,3,64}),n::zeros({64}),true,true);
#' auto partial=n::grad(out.d_loss,d.parameters());
#' // Caller applies D, reruns G, applies G, then commits same-capture BN moments if present.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid geometry, dtype, values, alignment, products, aliased
#'   stores or incompatible leaves.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage.
#' @references - Ledig et al.(2017), Photo-Realistic Single Image Super-Resolution Using a Generative
#'   Adversarial Network, https://arxiv.org/abs/1609.04802 ; Wang et al.(2018), ESRGAN: Enhanced
#'   Super-Resolution Generative Adversarial Networks, https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.00219 . Fixed-width
#'   x2 teaching adaptations with a bicubic image shortcut, not pretrained benchmark models.
#' @seealso AdversarialSRGenerate(), AdversarialSRFeatures(), RelativisticAverageGan(), batch_norm_moving_values()
#' @md
#'
`AdversarialSR` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1088`, NULL, list(...))
#' Draw one explicit Gaussian stream, optionally sharing each pixel across RGB.
#'
#' Uses GaussianNoise's local raw MT19937 midpoint Box-Muller stream in NHWC
#' order. Shared mode draws\[N,H,W,1\], casts once, then tiles the last axis;
#' independent mode draws\[N,H,W,3\] in a single stream. Default Float32 matches
#' the source SinGAN pyramid. Returns owned detached data; no global RNG,
#' parameter store, optimizer, fitted state or input graph is retained.
#' Work/storage O(rows*height*width). Concurrent calls have independent local RNGs.
#' @usage
#' SingleImageNoise(rows, height, width, shared_rgb, seed, dtype = "Float32")
#' @param rows `integer`. Positive number of images N.
#' @param height `integer`. Positive spatial height H.
#' @param width `integer`. Positive spatial width W.
#' @param shared_rgb `logical`. True for coarse-scale identical RGB channels; false for independent RGB.
#' @param seed `integer`. Local uint32 MT seed, used without a global stream.
#' @param dtype `character (DType)`. Float32(default) or Float64 result computation type.
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning detached finite CPU\[N,H,W,3\] Gaussian noise.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' auto z=dm::nn::models::SingleImageNoise(1,16,16,true,7411);
#' // z[1,16,16,3]; all three channels at each pixel are identical.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For nonpositive axes, product overflow or nonfloating dtype.
#' @references - Rott Shaham, Dekel and Michaeli (2019), SinGAN: Learning a Generative Model
#'   from a Single Natural Image, https://arxiv.org/abs/1905.01164 . Source teaching
#'   example uses three small scales and this explicit Gaussian stream.
#' @seealso GaussianNoise(), SingleImageGenerate(), SingleImageAmplitude()
#' @md
#'
`SingleImageNoise` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1089`, NULL, list(...))
#' Measure a detached fixed scale amplitude from reconstruction RMS error.
#'
#' Computes factor*sqrt(sum((Double(previous)-Double(real))^2)/numel) and
#' casts once to the matching input dtype. The owning result has shape\[1\],
#' preserving the source example's one-element scalar convention. Inputs are
#' finite matching positive RGB CPU rectangles with arbitrary strides and signed
#' pixels. Both image paths are stopped before arithmetic. Factor defaults .1;
#' zero is allowed. No fitting, sampling, moving state or store mutation occurs.
#' Work/storage O(real.numel()); independent calls share no mutable state.
#' @usage
#' SingleImageAmplitude(real, previous_reconstruction, factor = 0.10000000000000001)
#' @param real `Tensor`. Finite floating CPU\[N,H,W,3\] target at this scale.
#' @param previous_reconstruction `Tensor`. Matching frozen lower-scale reconstruction already resized.
#' @param factor `numeric`. Finite nonnegative RMS multiplier, default .1.
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning detached finite\[1\] amplitude in real's Float32/64 dtype.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' auto a=n::models::SingleImageAmplitude(n::ones({1,2,3,3}),n::zeros({1,2,3,3}));
#' // a[1] contains approximately .1; no image gradient path is retained.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For incompatible inputs, invalid factor or nonfinite result.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For unsupported storage.
#' @references - Rott Shaham, Dekel and Michaeli (2019), SinGAN: Learning a Generative Model
#'   from a Single Natural Image, https://arxiv.org/abs/1905.01164 . Coarse amplitude
#'   is separately chosen as one by the caller, rather than measured here.
#' @seealso SingleImageNoise(), SingleImageGenerate()
#' @md
#'
`SingleImageAmplitude` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1090`, NULL, list(...))
#' Generate previous plus a learned tanh correction from explicit scaled noise.
#'
#' Matching finite signed Float32/64 CPU previous/noise\[N,H,W,3\], positive axes,
#' arbitrary strides/rectangles. Amplitude is a matching finite scalar or\[1\],
#' signed or zero allowed. Validate supplied inputs before creating leaves.
#' Three biased3x3 SAME stride1 convolutions3->4->4->3 use source fan-in uniform
#' kernels; two leaky(.2) activations then tanh. Source seed7307 creates371 values
#' in6 named leaves, head/body/output W/b. Output is previous+tanh(correction),
#' without clipping, normalization, pooling, dropout or batch coupling. Only
#' missing leaves initialize; no later RNG, existing-leaf write, optimizer,
#' sampling or hidden no-grad. Applicable first/higher paths remain live through
#' the input mixture and residual skip. No target image is required. Work/storage
#' O(N*H*W) for fixed width; synchronize shared mutable parameter stores.
#' @usage
#' SingleImageGenerate(generator, previous, noise, amplitude)
#' @param generator `ParameterStore`. Caller-owned floating G store, source seed7307.
#' @param previous `Tensor`. Finite matching CPU\[N,H,W,3\] previous scale already resized.
#' @param noise `Tensor`. Explicit matching finite noise, never drawn internally.
#' @param amplitude `Tensor`. Matching finite scalar or\[1\] scale multiplier.
#' @return `SingleImageGenerated`: Owning SingleImageGenerated with all five actual boundaries.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;n::ParameterStore g(7307);
#' auto previous=n::zeros({2,20,24,3});auto z=n::models::SingleImageNoise(2,20,24,true,7411);
#' auto o=n::models::SingleImageGenerate(g,previous,z,n::ones({1}));
#' // Fully convolutional image[2,20,24,3]; G owns371 values,6 leaves.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For incompatible input geometry/dtype/products/values or leaves.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For unsupported storage.
#' @references - Rott Shaham, Dekel and Michaeli (2019), SinGAN: Learning a Generative Model
#'   from a Single Natural Image, https://arxiv.org/abs/1905.01164 . This preserves
#'   the compact source residual generator, rather than the full paper architecture.
#' @seealso SingleImageGenerated, SingleImageDiscriminate(), SingleImageGan(), SRConv()
#' @md
#'
`SingleImageGenerate` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1091`, NULL, list(...))
#' Score local RGB patches through three biased SAME convolutions.
#'
#' Finite signed matching Float32/64 CPU image\[N,H,W,3\], positive rectangular
#' axes and arbitrary strides. Three fan-in uniform3x3 stride1 convolutions
#' 3->4->4->1 with two leaky(.2) activations produce raw\[N,H,W,1\] scores,
#' nominal7x7 receptive field with zero padding at boundaries. Source seed7309
