#' validate before leaves; stored-leaf/math errors may follow initialization.
#' Only missing leaves initialize; no existing-leaf writes, later RNG, optimizer
#' or hidden no-grad. Owning output retains applicable first/higher image/weight
#' paths. Fixed-width work/storage O(N*H*W); synchronize shared mutable stores.
#' @usage
#' SingleImageDiscriminate(discriminator, image)
#' @param discriminator `ParameterStore`. Caller-owned matching floating D store, source seed7309.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Finite matching CPU\[N,H,W,3\] signed RGB image batch.
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning live raw patch scores\[N,H,W,1\], with no probability transform.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;n::ParameterStore d(7309);
#' auto score=n::models::SingleImageDiscriminate(d,n::zeros({2,30,36,3}));
#' // score[2,30,36,1]; D owns297 values,6 leaves.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For incompatible geometry/dtype/products/values or leaves.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For unsupported storage.
#' @references - Rott Shaham, Dekel and Michaeli (2019), SinGAN: Learning a Generative Model
#'   from a Single Natural Image, https://arxiv.org/abs/1905.01164 . Compact source
#'   critic uses width4 and raw local least-squares scores.
#' @seealso SingleImageGenerate(), SingleImageGan()
#' @md
#'
`SingleImageDiscriminate` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1092`, NULL, list(...))
#' Evaluate one explicit single-image least-squares game with shared reconstruction weights.
#'
#' Distinct matching Float32/64 G/D stores; finite positive RGB CPU rectangles
#' with common H/W, arbitrary strides. Previous/noise have identical geometry;
#' rec_previous/rec_noise exactly match real. Random and real batch counts may
#' differ; each score pool has its own mean. Matching scalar or\[1\] amplitude is
#' shared by both G calls. Validate all supplied inputs before parameter leaves.
#' Random fake and fixed reconstruction share the same371 G values; image-only
#' D(real)/D(fake) share297 D values. Full G LSGAN+10MSE and half D LSGAN match
#' the source. No gradient penalty, normalization, target-conditioned critic,
#' clipping, stop-gradient, fitted state, optimizer or sampling is hidden.
#' First/higher input/weight paths remain live, including both G uses. Caller
#' must freeze/detach lower scales and measure fixed amplitudes separately, then
#' take D followed by a fresh G capture. Only missing leaves initialize; inputs
#' and existing leaves are unchanged. Work/storage O((Nreal+Nfake)*H*W);
#' synchronize shared mutable stores. Returned Tensor fields own graph/storage.
#' @usage
#' SingleImageGan(generator, discriminator, real, previous, noise, rec_previous, rec_noise, amplitude)
#' @param generator `ParameterStore`. Caller-owned G store, source seed7307.
#' @param discriminator `ParameterStore`. Distinct matching D store, source seed7309.
#' @param real `Tensor`. Finite matching CPU\[Nreal,H,W,3\] reconstruction target and D real input.
#' @param previous `Tensor`. Finite matching CPU\[Nfake,H,W,3\] random lower-scale draw already resized.
#' @param noise `Tensor`. Matching explicit random noise, shared RGB at the coarsest source scale.
#' @param rec_previous `Tensor`. Finite matching real-shaped frozen reconstruction already resized.
#' @param rec_noise `Tensor`. Real-shaped explicit fixed noise; source uses zeros above the coarse scale.
#' @param amplitude `Tensor`. Matching finite scalar or\[1\], signed or zero allowed.
#' @return `SingleImageGanOutput`: Owning eight-field SingleImageGanOutput with two images, two scores and four losses.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;n::ParameterStore g(7307),d(7309);
#' auto x=n::zeros({1,4,6,3});auto z=n::models::SingleImageNoise(1,4,6,true,7411);
#' auto o=n::models::SingleImageGan(g,d,x,x,z,x,z,n::ones({1}));
#' // Capture o.d_loss for D; after its write, re-evaluate and capture o.g_loss for G.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For aliased stores, incompatible inputs/dtypes/values/products or leaves.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For unsupported storage.
#' @references - Rott Shaham, Dekel and Michaeli (2019), SinGAN: Learning a Generative Model
#'   from a Single Natural Image, https://arxiv.org/abs/1905.01164 . Compact source
#'   variant has three scales, width4, LSGAN and a fixed10-times reconstruction weight.
#' @seealso SingleImageGanOutput, SingleImageGenerate(), SingleImageDiscriminate(), SingleImageAmplitude()
#' @md
#'
`SingleImageGan` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1093`, NULL, list(...))
#' Compare unbiased feature moments by the exact low-rank Gaussian Frechet formula.
#'
#' Finite Float32/64 CPU real\[N,F\],fake\[M,F\], N,M>=2,F>0; unequal pool sizes
#' and dtypes/strides allowed. Detach and promote to Float64, center each pool
#' and divide by sqrt(its row count-1). Compute thin SVD of the\[N,M\] cross
#' product, rather than forming two\[F,F\] covariances. The singular-value sum
#' equals the Gaussian covariance cross trace, including rank-deficient pools.
#' Raw distance is squared mean difference+both covariance traces-2*cross trace.
#' Clamp only nonnegative round-off: raw<-1e-7 throws; a tiny negative result
#' becomes zero. This fixed source tolerance is absolute, not scale-adaptive.
#' Work O(NMF+NM*min(N,M)); cross storage O(NM), plus centered inputs/SVD.
#' No data/model mutation, fitting, sampling, hidden extractor or autograd path.
#' Independent calls share no mutable state. FID terminology applies only when
#' features actually use the specified pretrained Inception protocol; arbitrary
#' features still define a Gaussian Frechet moment distance.
#' @usage
#' GaussianFrechet(real, fake)
#' @param real `Tensor`. Finite floating CPU\[N,F\] reference feature pool, at least two rows.
#' @param fake `Tensor`. Finite floating CPU\[M,F\] candidate pool with matching positive width.
#' @return `GaussianFrechetOutput`: Owning detached seven-field Float64 GaussianFrechetOutput.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' #include <datamunge/nn/generative_metrics.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;auto t=n::DType::Float64;
#' auto a=n::tensor({-1.,-1.,-1.,1.,1.,-1.,1.,1.},{4,2},t);
#' auto b=n::tensor({-2.,-1.,0.,2.,1.,1.},{3,2},t);
#' auto out=n::models::GaussianFrechet(a,b); // Unequal pools; no extractor or fit.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs, incompatible widths/products or raw<-1e-7.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage or unsupported primitive execution.
#' @references - Heusel et al.(2017), GANs Trained by a Two Time-Scale Update Rule Converge
#'   to a Local Nash Equilibrium, https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.08500 . Low-rank form
#'   uses the nuclear norm of the two centered data factors' cross product.
#' @seealso GaussianFrechetOutput, InceptionScore(), datamunge::nn::svd()
#' @md
#'
`GaussianFrechet` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1094`, NULL, list(...))
#' Measure exp(mean conditional-to-marginal class KL) from supplied probabilities.
#'
#' Finite floating CPU\[N,C\], N>0,C>1; signed logits rejected, values in\[0,1\],
#' row sums within3e-6 of one. Arbitrary strides allowed. Stop inputs and cast
#' to Float64; marginal=mean over rows. Evaluate exp(mean(sum(p*(logp-logm))))
#' with both log arguments floored at1e-300, so zero classes contribute zero.
#' Does not renormalize rows. No extractor, sampling, fitting or state mutation;
#' output is an owning detached Float64 scalar. Work/storage O(NC), independent
#' calls share no mutable state. Uniform uncertain and fully class-collapsed
#' distributions both score one; a balanced confident C-class pool scores C.
#' This score is not accuracy, recall, image uniqueness or proof against copying.
#' @usage
#' InceptionScore(probability)
#' @param probability `Tensor`. Finite normalized floating CPU\[N,C\] class probabilities.
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning detached Float64 scalar Inception score.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' #include <datamunge/nn/generative_metrics.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' auto p=n::tensor({1.,0.,0.,1.},{2,2});
#' auto score=n::models::InceptionScore(p); // Approximately2; no network is run.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid geometry, range, normalization or nonfinite result.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For non-CPU storage or unsupported primitive execution.
#' @references - Salimans et al.(2016), Improved Techniques for Training GANs,
#'   https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.03498 .
#' @seealso InceptionScoreSplits(), GaussianFrechet()
#' @md
#'
`InceptionScore` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1095`, NULL, list(...))
#' Score consecutive source-order partitions without shuffling or dropping any row.
