`MadeMasks` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1110`, NULL, list(...))
#' Apply a live biased dense projection with an explicit stopped structural mask.
#'
#' Finite matching Float32/64 CPU input\[N,In\] and mask\[In,Out\], positive axes,
#' arbitrary strides; mask must contain exact zeros/ones. Create missing
#' name/W normal(0,.1) and name/b zeros, then bias_add(input@@(W*mask),b).
#' Mask is structural and detached; applicable input/W/b first/higher paths
#' stay live. Masked coordinates have exact zero partials of every order.
#' This primitive alone guarantees no full-network causal order. Validate
#' supplied arguments before leaves; stored-leaf/math errors may follow creation.
#' Only missing leaves initialize; no existing-leaf writes, activation, optimizer,
#' fitting, sampling, RNG after initialization or hidden no-grad. Owning live
#' output survives store collection. Work O(N*In*Out), storage O(N*Out+In*Out);
#' synchronize shared mutable stores. Nonfinite output is rejected.
#' @usage
#' MaskedDensityDense(parameters, name, input, mask)
#' @param parameters `ParameterStore`. Caller-owned matching floating parameter store.
#' @param name `character`. Nonempty leaf prefix, followed by /W and /b.
#' @param input `Tensor`. Finite signed matching floating CPU\[N,In\] input features.
#' @param mask `Tensor`. Matching finite floating CPU\[In,Out\] exact zero/one structural mask.
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning live floating CPU\[N,Out\] masked affine features.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;n::ParameterStore p(8803);
#' auto y=n::models::MaskedDensityDense(p,"toy",n::ones({2,3}),n::ones({3,4}));
#' // y[2,4]; p has12 kernel+4 bias values in two leaves.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid name/inputs/products/values/leaves or nonfinite output.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For unsupported storage or primitive execution.
#' @references - Germain et al.(2015), MADE: Masked Autoencoder for Distribution Estimation,
#'   https://arxiv.org/abs/1502.03509 . Mask multiplication remains inside the graph.
#' @seealso AutoregressiveDegreeMask(), MadeDensity(), MaskedPixelConv()
#' @md
#'
`MaskedDensityDense` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1111`, NULL, list(...))
#' Evaluate the source64-pixel degree-masked Bernoulli joint density.
#'
#' Finite signed matching Float32/64 CPU image\[N,8,8,1\],N>0, arbitrary strides.
#' Flatten64 pixels; two16-unit sigmoid layers and a64-logit head use MadeMasks'
#' <=,<=,strict< degree masks. Source seed8803 creates2400 values in6 named
#' leaves: input/hidden/output W,b. Missing W normal(0,.1), biases zero;1144
#' forbidden kernel coordinates,1256 active values. First output in the chosen
#' order has no input paths, only its bias. Strict own/future exclusion is in
#' raster order or reverse order; raw output layout is always8x8 raster.
#'
#' Reverse is explicit per call, not retained. The source fits separate stores
#' for each order; reusing one store with changed masks is a different protocol.
#' All supplied inputs validate before leaves; stored-leaf/math errors may follow
#' creation. Only missing leaves initialize; no existing-leaf writes, fitting,
#' optimizer, sampling, normalization, batch coupling, dropout or hidden no-grad.
#' Three owning fields retain applicable first/higher image/weight paths; masks
#' are stopped structural data. Fixed-width work/storage O(N*64*16); synchronize
#' shared mutable stores. Caller supplies binary targets to BernoulliPixels.
#' @usage
#' MadeDensity(parameters, image, reverse = FALSE)
#' @param parameters `ParameterStore`. Caller-owned matching floating store, source seed8803.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Finite signed matching CPU\[N,8,8,1\] image/canvas.
#' @param reverse `logical`. False(default) for top-left first; true for bottom-right first.
#' @return `MadeDensityOutput`: Owning three-field MadeDensityOutput, including logits\[N,8,8,1\].
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;n::ParameterStore p(8803);
#' auto o=n::models::MadeDensity(p,n::zeros({2,8,8,1}),true);
#' // Reverse-order predictions; sampling ordinal j writes raw site63-j.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For incompatible geometry/dtype/values/products or stored leaves.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For unsupported storage or primitive execution.
#' @references - Germain et al.(2015), MADE: Masked Autoencoder for Distribution Estimation,
#'   https://arxiv.org/abs/1502.03509 . Source fits two independent fixed orders,
#'   not one shared-weight order-agnostic model.
#' @seealso MadeDensityOutput, MadeMasks(), MaskedDensityDense(), EqualDensityMixture()
#' @md
#'
`MadeDensity` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1112`, NULL, list(...))
#' Mix normalized joint densities equally by stable logmeanexp of negative NLLs.
#'
#' Finite Float32/64 CPU per_model_nll\[N,K\],N>0,K>0, arbitrary strides; signed
#' NLLs allowed for continuous densities. Cast to Float64 and compute
#' -log(sum_k exp(-nll_k)/K) for each observation, with a stopped row maximum
#' for stability. Return joint NLLs, their mean and softmax(-nll) component
#' responsibilities. Applicable first/higher paths remain live, including to
#' Float32 inputs through the cast; the stabilizing maximum is stopped.
#' K=1 preserves the supplied NLL. No clipping, model evaluation, fitting,
#' sampling, mutation or hidden no-grad. Three owning fields survive input/
#' parent collection. Work/storage O(NK); local independent calls.
#'
#' A normalized mixture interpretation requires every supplied column to be a
#' normalized joint density of the same observations/base measure. The function
#' cannot establish that fact from numbers. Use per-image sums for image joints,
#' not mean pixel losses. This is not the arithmetic mean of component NLLs:
#' posterior responsibility is its derivative with respect to each component NLL.
#' Source report evaluates fitted orders; no shared-weight training is implied.
#' @usage
#' EqualDensityMixture(per_model_nll)
#' @param per_model_nll `Tensor`. Finite floating CPU\[N,K\] per-observation joint NLLs, one component per column.
#' @return `DensityMixtureOutput`: Owning live Float64 DensityMixtureOutput with\[N\],scalar,\[N,K\] fields.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;auto t=n::DType::Float64;
#' auto o=n::models::EqualDensityMixture(-n::log(n::tensor({.8,.2},{1,2},t)));
#' // Mixture probability=.5, NLL=log(2), responsibilities(.8,.2).
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs or nonfinite returned NLL/mean/weights.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For unsupported storage or primitive execution.
#' @references - Equal-probability finite-mixture identity p(x)=sum_k p_k(x)/K, evaluated
#'   with logsumexp; source MADE teaching experiment mixes two fixed-order joints.
#' @seealso DensityMixtureOutput, MadeDensity(), logsumexp()
#' @md
#'
`EqualDensityMixture` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1113`, NULL, list(...))
#' Average disjoint integer RGB blocks and round to nearest half-up byte codes.
#'
#' Int32/64 CPU original\[N,H,W,3\], all axes positive, values0..255, arbitrary
#' strides. Positive block_size(default4) must divide H/W. Sum each disjoint
#' square in integer arithmetic, round its mean half-up to an Int32 code, then
#' compute double(code)/127.5-1 and cast once to Float32. For32x32 and block4
#' this is the original compact PixelCNN++8x8 preparation, preserving exact
#' quantized source values. This is not bilinear resizing. No source mutation,
#' split selection, normalization fitting, RNG or input gradient. Independent
#' owning outputs, work O(NHW), storage O(NHW/block_size^2); calls share no state.
#' @usage
#' RgbAreaPixels(original, block_size = 4)
#' @param original `Tensor`. Integer CPU NHWC byte-valued RGB source batch.
#' @param block_size `integer`. Positive square block extent dividing H/W, default4.
#' @return `QuantizedRgbData`: Owning stopped QuantizedRgbData with codes and signed images.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' auto raw=dm::nn::from_vector(std::vector<std::int32_t>{0,0,0,1,1,1,0,0,0,1,1,1},{1,2,2,3});
#' auto out=dm::nn::models::RgbAreaPixels(raw,2);
#' // A mean of.5 rounds up: all three codes=1, images=float(1/127.5-1).
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid geometry/type/range or unsafe integer block sum.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For unsupported storage or primitive execution.
#' @references - Preserves the source compact RGB density protocol:4x4 integer area means,
#'   nearest half-up codes and signed8-bit-code representation; no learned transform.
#' @seealso QuantizedRgbData, DiscretizedLogisticRGB(), PixelCnnPP()
#' @md
#'
`RgbAreaPixels` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1114`, NULL, list(...))
#' Evaluate a discretized RGB logistic mixture with triangular within-pixel coupling.
#'
#' Matching finite Float32/64 CPU image\[...,3\] and parameters\[...,10*K\], same
#' leading axes, each positive, arbitrary strides, K=mixtures>0(default3).
#' Image values must be in\[-1,1\]; exact8-bit observations use code/127.5-1.
#' Interior continuous values are permitted for differentiation but do not
#' identify a separate normalized categorical grid. Component-major parameter
#' layout is logit, meanR/G/B, logscaleR/G/B, coefficientRG/BR/BG. Clip logscales
#' from below at-7(ties retain the raw-parameter derivative), tanh coefficients,
#' then add coefficientRG*observedR to meanG and coefficientBR*observedR plus
#' coefficientBG*observedG to meanB. Means are not clipped.
#'
#' For each channel use hi=(x-mean+step)*exp(-s),lo=(x-mean-step)*exp(-s),
#' delta=width*exp(-s), middle=hi-softplus(hi)-softplus(lo)+log(-expm1(-delta)).
#' Low x<=float(-.999) uses -softplus(-hi); high x>=float(.999) uses
#' -softplus(lo), extending the endpoint bins to infinity. Source-compatible
#' step=float(1/255),width=float(2/255) are promoted even for Float64. No small-mass
#' fallback or CDF subtraction. Sum channel log masses, add log_softmax mixture
#' weights, then stable logsumexp with a stopped maximum. All applicable first/
#' higher paths remain live; returned mean loss is nats per RGB channel.
#'
#' Outputs flatten leading axes to P; owning handles outlive the inputs. No
#' mutation, fitting, RNG, sampling, store or hidden no-grad; O(PK) work/storage,
#' local independent calls. Invalid input rejects before math. Extremely large
#' finite parameters may overflow/underflow intermediate masses; nonfinite
#' returned fields reject rather than silently clipping more of the density.
#' @usage
#' DiscretizedLogisticRGB(image, parameters, mixtures = 3)
#' @param image `Tensor`. Finite floating CPU\[...,3\] signed RGB observations in\[-1,1\].
#' @param parameters `Tensor`. Matching finite CPU\[...,10*K\] component-major parameters.
#' @param mixtures `integer`. Positive K(default3) with representable10*K.
#' @return `LogisticRgbOutput`: Owning live LogisticRgbOutput, preserving input floating dtype.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' auto p=n::zeros({1,10},n::DType::Float64).requires_grad_();
#' auto o=n::models::DiscretizedLogisticRGB(n::zeros({1,3},n::DType::Float64),p,1);
#' auto g=n::grad(o.mean_channel_nll,{p})[0];
#' // Three center-bin logistic masses; finite live gradient[1,10].
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For incompatible geometry/dtype/range, unsafe K or nonfinite outputs.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For unsupported storage or primitive execution.
#' @references - Salimans, Karpathy, Chen and Kingma(2017), PixelCNN++: Improving the PixelCNN
#'   with Discretized Logistic Mixture Likelihood and Other Modifications,
#'   https://arxiv.org/abs/1701.05517 . Uses the teaching source's stable exact-bin
#'   identity and minimum log scale; no published multiscale architecture claim.
#' @seealso LogisticRgbOutput, PixelCnnPP(), log_softmax(), expm1()
#' @md
#'
`DiscretizedLogisticRGB` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1115`, NULL, list(...))
#' Evaluate the compact three-block whole-pixel-causal RGB logistic mixture density.
#'
#' Finite matching Float32/64 CPU image\[N,H,W,3\], positive axes, values\[-1,1\],
#' arbitrary strides, caller-owned matching floating ParameterStore. Three
#' dual-stream width4 gated blocks feed a30-channel head for three logistic
#' components. Whole current/future raw pixels are excluded from every head
#' parameter; within-pixel R/G dependence belongs to the separate likelihood.
#' Source8x8 geometry and seed8609 yield1410 stored values in23 ordered leaves,
#' 962 active and448 structurally masked. Other positive rectangles are supported.
#' No labels, dropout, multiscale stack, learned initial state or batch coupling.
#'
#' Missing leaves initialize normal(.1) kernels/zero biases in source order;
#' existing leaves are reused. Input validates before leaves. Applicable first/
#' higher image/store paths stay live and all twelve outputs own storage/graphs.
#' No fitting, optimizer, sampling, RNG bank, global mutation or hidden no-grad;
#' O(NHW) fixed-width work/storage. Independent stores can run concurrently;
#' callers synchronize writes to a shared store. Finite input may still produce
#' overflowing arithmetic: nonfinite context/likelihood output rejects.
#' @usage
#' PixelCnnPP(parameters, image)
#' @param parameters `ParameterStore`. Caller-owned matching floating store, initialized/reused in gated source order.
#' @param image `Tensor`. Finite matching CPU\[N,H,W,3\] signed RGB observations in\[-1,1\].
#' @return `PixelCnnPPOutput`: Owning live PixelCnnPPOutput with scalar nats/channel and summed image joint NLLs.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;n::ParameterStore p(8609);
#' auto o=n::models::PixelCnnPP(p,n::zeros({1,8,8,3}));
#' auto g=n::grad(o.loss,p.parameters());
#' // p.count()==1410, p.size()==23; optimizer and complete training loop remain explicit.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid input, incompatible existing leaves or nonfinite output fields.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For unsupported storage or primitive execution.
#' @references - Salimans, Karpathy, Chen and Kingma(2017), PixelCNN++: Improving the PixelCNN
#'   with Discretized Logistic Mixture Likelihood and Other Modifications,
#'   https://arxiv.org/abs/1701.05517 . Compact teaching context, not the published
#'   multiscale network; retains exact RGB mixture and whole-pixel causal semantics.
#' @seealso PixelCnnPPOutput, DiscretizedLogisticRGB(), GatedPixelConvolutional(), RgbAreaPixels()
#' @md
