`PixelCnnPP` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1116`, NULL, list(...))
#' Transform explicit standard-normal coordinates into detached banana observations.
#'
#' For finite Float32/64 CPU standard\[N,2\], compute x0=u and
#' x1=v+curvature*(u*u-1) in Double, then cast once to dtype(default Float32).
#' Curvature is any finite real, including zero/negative values. This invertible
#' triangular map has determinant one. The caller supplies the complete noise
#' bank; this function does not sample, split rows, fit or retain RNG state.
#' Arbitrary strides accepted; result owns stopped contiguous storage and never
#' mutates/retains the input graph. O(N) work/storage; independent calls share no
#' mutable state. Double or final Float32 overflow is rejected without clipping.
#' @usage
#' BananaPoints(standard, curvature = 0.5, dtype = "Float32")
#' @param standard `Tensor`. Finite floating CPU\[N,2\] explicit normal-coordinate bank.
#' @param curvature `numeric`. Finite quadratic bend coefficient, default .5.
#' @param dtype `character (DType)`. Float32(default) or Float64 final observation dtype.
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning detached finite CPU\[N,2\] banana coordinates.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' auto u=n::from_vector(std::vector<double>{0,0,2,1},{2,2});
#' auto x=n::models::BananaPoints(u);
#' // x is Float32 [[0,-.5],[2,2.5]]. No gradient is retained.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs/options or nonfinite computed coordinates.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For unsupported primitive execution.
#' @references - Original compact normalizing-flow teaching protocol: x0=u, x1=v+.5*(u*u-1),
#'   with explicit Box-Muller Double coordinates; not an external dataset.
#' @seealso BananaLogProbability(), GaussianNoise(), NiceDensity()
#' @md
#'
`BananaPoints` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1117`, NULL, list(...))
#' Evaluate the analytic unit-determinant banana log density in Double.
#'
#' Finite Float32/64 CPU points\[N,2\] and finite curvature(default .5). Invert
#' u=x0, v=x1-curvature*(x0*x0-1), then return -log(2*pi)-.5*(u*u+v*v).
#' Uses the full Double log constant, independently of the model's optional
#' legacy rounded constant. Live first/higher input paths survive conversion
#' to Double and parent collection. Arbitrary strides, no mutation, sampling,
#' fitting or global state. O(N) work/storage; nonfinite results are rejected.
#' @usage
#' BananaLogProbability(points, curvature = 0.5)
#' @param points `Tensor`. Finite floating CPU\[N,2\] observations in coordinate units.
#' @param curvature `numeric`. Finite quadratic bend coefficient, default .5.
#' @return `Tensor`: Owning live Float64 CPU\[N\] analytic log probabilities in nats.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' auto x=dm::nn::from_vector(std::vector<double>{0,-.5},{1,2});
#' auto logp=dm::nn::models::BananaLogProbability(x);
#' // logp[0]=-log(2*pi), approximately -1.8378770664.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' Signals an R error (from the C++ exception):
#'
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid inputs/curvature or nonfinite results.
#' * `std::logic_error`: For unsupported primitive execution.
#' @references - Original compact flow protocol's analytic triangular banana map with unit determinant.
#' @seealso BananaPoints(), StandardNormalLogProbability()
#' @md
#'
`BananaLogProbability` <- function(...) .Call(`.rs_1118`, NULL, list(...))
#' Evaluate a factorized standard Gaussian log density without sampling.
#'
#' Finite floating CPU latent\[N,D\], positive axes and arbitrary strides.
#' Return -.5*sum(z*z,axis1)-.5*D*log(2*pi), in the input Float32/64 dtype.
