#' Counts of true-class rows and predicted-class columns, with SVG rendering.
#'
#' Accumulates observations without retaining their tensors. Const rendering does
#' not mutate counts or perform model inference. Concurrent mutation needs external
#' synchronization. Ratios and empty-support behavior follow the metric methods.
#' @section Constructor:
#' `ConfusionMatrix$new(classes)`
#'
#' Allocates a zero-filled square count matrix for a positive number of classes.
#'
#' * `classes` (`integer`)
#' @section Methods:
#' * `$add(truth, prediction)`
#'
#'   Increments the cell at the true-class row and predicted-class column.
#'
#'   Adds every pair from two integer tensors of equal size.
#'
#' * `$cells()` -> `vector<vector<integer>>`
#'
#'   Borrows the square count table, indexed by truth then prediction.
#'
#' * `$classes()` -> `integer`
#'
#'   Returns the configured number of classes.
#'
#' * `$per_class(c)` -> `ClassMetrics`
#'
#'   Computes one class's precision, recall, F1, IoU, and true support.
#'
#' * `$accuracy()` -> `numeric`
#'
#'   Returns the fraction of observations on the diagonal.
#'
#' * `$macro()` -> `ClassMetrics`
#'
#'   Unweighted mean over classes (IoU over classes where it is defined).
#'
#' * `$to_tensor()` -> `Tensor`
#'
#'   As an int64 tensor \[classes, classes\], truth rows.
#'
#' * `$to_svg(options = <default>)` -> `character`
#'
#'   Render counts or normalized values as a labeled, accessible SVG heatmap.
#'   - `options`: Labels, normalization, cell/font size, colors and heading.
#'   - Returns: Standalone UTF-8 SVG text; save it as a local figure, not report output.
#'
#' * `$save_svg(path, options = <default>)`
#'
#'   Save the annotated confusion-matrix SVG to a local file.
#'   - `path`: Relative or absolute destination filename.
#'   - `options`: Labels, normalization, cell/font size, colors and heading.
#' @section Static methods:
#' * `ConfusionMatrix$from_counts(counts)` -> `ConfusionMatrix`
#'
#'   Own validated integer counts from an existing square tensor.
#'   - `counts`: Nonempty square \[C,C\] Int32/Int64 tensor with nonnegative counts.
#'   - Returns: Independent confusion matrix containing exactly those counts.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' dm::nn::ConfusionMatrix matrix(2);
