#' Own eleven Wasserstein endpoints, including symbolic and analytic critic input gradients.
#'
#' All fields own storage/applicable graphs after parent/store collection.
#' interpolation is detached; penalty stops all external real/alpha/G paths.
#' symbolic/penalty retain critic parameter history only when requested, while
#' input_gradient is a separately computed analytic Jacobian diagnostic. Base
#' critic loss still has a G path, so choose update groups explicitly. No mode,
#' optimizer, update counter or clipping callback is retained.
#' @section Constructor:
#' `WassersteinGanOutput$new()`
#' @section Fields:
#' * `$fake` (`Tensor`): Owning live G coordinates\[N,2\].
#' * `$real_score` (`Tensor`): Owning live real critic scores\[N,1\].
#' * `$fake_score` (`Tensor`): Owning live generated critic scores\[N,1\].
#' * `$interpolation` (`Tensor`): Owning detached alpha*real+(1-alpha)*stop(fake)\[N,2\].
#' * `$input_gradient` (`Tensor`): Owning analytic critic Jacobian\[N,2\], with detached interpolation.
#' * `$symbolic_input_gradient` (`Tensor`): Owning autograd critic Jacobian\[N,2\]; optional critic history.
#' * `$norm` (`Tensor`): Owning sqrt(sum(symbolic_gradient^2,axis1)+1e-12)\[N\].
#' * `$penalty` (`Tensor`): Owning mean(square(norm-1)) scalar; no external real/alpha/G path.
#' * `$critic_gap` (`Tensor`): Owning mean(real_score)-mean(fake_score), an unconverged game diagnostic.
#' * `$generator_loss` (`Tensor`): Owning -mean(fake_score) scalar, unaffected by penalty weight.
#' * `$critic_loss` (`Tensor`): Owning -gap, plus positive penalty_weight*penalty when selected.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore g(5501),c(5503);
#' auto out=n::models::WassersteinGan(g,c,n::ones({2,2}),n::zeros({2,2}),n::full({2,1},.5));
#' // out.norm is[2]; penalty is the mean squared distance of each norm from1.
#' ```
#' @references - Gulrajani et al. (2017), https://arxiv.org/abs/1704.00028 .
#' @seealso WassersteinGan(), WassersteinGenerate(), WassersteinCritic()
#' @md
#'
`WassersteinGanOutput` <- R6::R6Class("WassersteinGanOutput", inherit = `.rosetta_object`, cloneable = FALSE,
