#'
#' The initial channel width is twice growth_rate. Compression floors retained
#' width after each block; it may not eliminate all channels. ImageNet presets
#' select block counts, not a growth rate: the released DenseNet-161 uses growth
#' 48, while the default is 32. No learned tensors live in this value.
#' @section Constructor:
#' `DenseNetConfig$new()`
#' @section Fields:
#' * `$depth` (`integer`): ImageNet preset or CIFAR 6n+4 (bottleneck) / 3n+4 (basic).
#' * `$growth_rate` (`integer`)
#' * `$classes` (`integer`): At least two output logits.
#' * `$cifar_layout` (`logical`)
#' * `$bottleneck` (`logical`): Use 4k reductions if true; mandatory for ImageNet presets.
#' * `$compression` (`numeric`): Retained transition fraction in (0,1\], rounded down.
#' * `$momentum` (`numeric`): Finite BN old-value EMA retention in \[0,1).
#' * `$update_stats` (`logical`): Update moving moments only on training calls when true.
#' @section Methods:
#' * `$BlockCounts()` -> `vector<integer>`
#'
#'   Resolve three CIFAR repetition counts or the four ImageNet block counts.
#'   - Returns: Positive dense-layer counts, without mutating this configuration.
#'
#' * `$Validate()`
#'
#'   Validate depth, growth, class count, BN momentum and nonempty compressed widths.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace n = dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(17), state(17);
#' n::models::DenseNetConfig cfg;
#' cfg.cifar_layout = true;
#' cfg.depth = 10;
#' cfg.growth_rate = 2;
#' cfg.classes = 3;
#' cfg.Validate();
#' ```
#' @references - Huang et al. (2017), Densely Connected Convolutional Networks, https://arxiv.org/abs/1608.06993; released model, https://github.com/liuzhuang13/DenseNet/blob/master/models/densenet.lua
#' @seealso DenseNet()
#' @md
#'
`DenseNetConfig` <- R6::R6Class("DenseNetConfig", inherit = `.rosetta_object`, cloneable = FALSE,
  public = list(
