#' Primary/digit capsules, scores and an optional true/predicted-mask decoder.
#'
#' Tensor handles retain graphs. The decoder closure captures the digit tensor
#' and a POINTER to the borrowed parameter store; that store and unchanged
#' leaves must outlive closure calls/backward. A new forward is needed after
#' optimizer/checkpoint mutation. The callable is empty when decoder=false.
#' @section Constructor:
#' `CapsNetOutputs$new()`
#' @section Fields:
#' * `$primary` (`Tensor`): \[N,1152,8\] squashed 32-type primary capsules.
#' * `$digits` (`Tensor`): \[N,10,16\] routed digit vectors.
#' * `$lengths` (`Tensor`): \[N,10\] stabilized capsule lengths, sqrt(sum(v²)+1e-9).
#' * `$logits` (`Tensor`): log(lengths); softmax gives normalized lengths, not calibrated probabilities.
#' @section Methods:
#' * `$Reconstruct(mask)` -> `Tensor`
#'
#'   Decoder output \[N, 784\] in (0, 1) from the digit capsules masked by `mask` \[N, 10\].
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' namespace n = dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(17);
#' const auto y = n::models::CapsNet(p, n::ones({1, 28, 28, 1}));
#' const auto image = y.reconstruct(n::one_hot(n::argmax(y.logits, 1), 10));
#' ```
#' @references - Sabour, Frosst and Hinton (2017), https://arxiv.org/abs/1710.09829
#' @seealso CapsNet(), CapsuleLengths(), MarginLoss()
#' @md
