#' Fit a fine raster prior conditioned on parent-aligned coarse symbols and the previous fine symbol.
#'
#' Coarse grids\[B,Ht*Wt\] pair with fine grids\[B,4*Ht*Wt\], interpreted as raster
#' Ht×Wt and 2Ht×2Wt. For fine position(r,c), parent=(r/2)*Wt+c/2 using integer
#' division. Each image starts previous=BOS=K; transitions are counted by
#' \[parent_code,previous_fine,current_fine\]. Positive Dirichlet smoothing gives
#' p=(count+s)/(context_total+K*s). Defaults K16,Ht=Wt=7,s=0.5 preserve the source.
#' The caller supplies fitting codes only and enforces provenance; no image,
#' neural prior, model update or RNG is involved. This first-order baseline
#' conditions on one aligned top symbol, not the full coarse grid or fine prefix.
#' Construction copies state; exports are independent. Read-only methods are
#' thread-safe. Work O(B*4*Ht*Wt+K^3), storage O(B*4*Ht*Wt+K^3).
#' @section Constructor:
#' `Vq2ConditionalPrior$new(top, bottom, top_height = 7, top_width = 7, entries = 16, smoothing = 0.5)`
#'
#' Copy paired fitting-code grids into a parent/previous-symbol transition table.
#'
#' * `top` (`Tensor`): Fitting-only valid Int32\[B,top_height*top_width\] coarse codes.
#' * `bottom` (`Tensor`): Matching fitting-only Int32\[B,4*top_height*top_width\] fine codes.
#' * `top_height` (`integer`): Positive coarse height, default7.
#' * `top_width` (`integer`): Positive coarse width, default7.
#' * `entries` (`integer`): Positive Int32 vocabulary size for both grids, default16.
#' * `smoothing` (`numeric`): Finite positive representable pseudocount, default0.5.
#' @section Methods:
#' * `$counts()` -> `Tensor`
#'
#'   Export independent Int32\[K,K+1,K\] parent/previous/current counts.
#'   - Returns: Owning table; changing it does not mutate the prior.
#'
#' * `$probabilities()` -> `Tensor`
#'
#'   Export independent Float64\[K,K+1,K\] normalized transition rows.
#'   - Returns: Owning positive probabilities; previous=K is the BOS row per parent.
#'
#' * `$Sample(top, uniforms)` -> `Tensor`
#'
#'   Sample a fine grid from a supplied coarse grid and explicit uniform values.
#'   - `top`: Valid nonempty Int32\[B,top_tokens\] coarse codes, accepting strides.
#'   - `uniforms`: Explicit finite Float64\[B,bottom_tokens\] values in\[0,1).
#'   - Returns: Owning detached Int32\[B,bottom_tokens\] fine IDs.
#'
#' * `$Nll(top, bottom)` -> `numeric`
#'
#'   Score paired coarse/fine grids in mean conditional nats per complete fine grid.
#'   - `top`: Valid nonempty Int32\[B,top_tokens\] coarse codes.
#'   - `bottom`: Matching valid Int32\[B,bottom_tokens\] fine codes.
#'   - Returns: Mean natural-log conditional code NLL per image/grid.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::models::Vq2ConditionalPrior
#' prior(n::zeros({1,1},n::DType::Int32),n::zeros({1,4},n::DType::Int32),1,1,2); const auto
#' ids=prior.Sample(n::zeros({1,1},n::DType::Int32),n::full({1,4},.2,n::DType::Float64));
