#' Own all kernel matrices and scalar terms of the signed unbiased IMQ MMD estimate.
#'
#' Every field owns lifetime and retains its continuous input paths. No fitting
#' state or random draws are stored. The finite-sample estimate may be negative;
#' it is MMD squared, not its square root or a calibrated hypothesis-test p-value.
#' @section Constructor:
#' `MmdOutput$new()`
#' @section Fields:
#' * `$xx` (`Tensor`): Owning within-first kernel matrix\[N,N\], including its unit diagonal.
#' * `$yy` (`Tensor`): Owning within-second kernel matrix\[M,M\], including its unit diagonal.
#' * `$xy` (`Tensor`): Owning cross kernel matrix\[N,M\], with every pair included.
#' * `$within_x` (`Tensor`): Owning(sum(xx)-N)/(N*(N-1)), excluding self-pairs only.
#' * `$within_y` (`Tensor`): Owning(sum(yy)-M)/(M*(M-1)), excluding self-pairs only.
#' * `$cross` (`Tensor`): Owning mean(xy), including corresponding-index pairs when N=M.
#' * `$value` (`Tensor`): Owning signed scalar within_x+within_y-2*cross, unbiased MMD squared.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' const auto out=n::models::ImqMmd(n::zeros({2,1}),n::zeros({3,1}));
#' // xx[2,2], yy[3,3], xy[2,3] are all one; value is exactly zero.
#' ```
#' @seealso ImqMmd(), ImqKernel(), InfoVariationalAutoencoder()
