#' Own all eighteen Gaussian, conditional-flow, density and reconstruction endpoints.
#'
#' Every Tensor owns its lifetime and preserves continuous gradients. Per-row
#' density/reconstruction values are in nats; loss alone averages the batch.
#' Inverse endpoints are diagnostics and are not part of the training loss.
#' @section Constructor:
#' `FlowVaeOutput$new()`
#' @section Fields:
#' * `$context` (`Tensor`): Encoder ReLU context \[B,hidden\], shared by both conditioners.
#' * `$mu` (`Tensor`): Base Gaussian mean \[B,L\], independent of epsilon.
#' * `$log_variance` (`Tensor`): Base Gaussian log variance \[B,L\], independent of epsilon.
#' * `$z0` (`Tensor`): Base sample mu+exp(log_variance/2)*epsilon \[B,L\].
#' * `$z1` (`Tensor`): First coupling output \[B,L\].
#' * `$z` (`Tensor`): Second coupling output \[B,L\], the sole decoder input.
#' * `$logdet0` (`Tensor`): First forward log absolute determinant \[B\].
#' * `$logdet1` (`Tensor`): Second forward log absolute determinant \[B\].
#' * `$logdet` (`Tensor`): Sum of the two forward log determinants \[B\].
#' * `$logq0` (`Tensor`): Base diagonal-Gaussian log density evaluated at z0 \[B\].
#' * `$logq` (`Tensor`): Flowed posterior log density logq0-logdet \[B\].
#' * `$logp` (`Tensor`): Standard-normal prior log density evaluated at final z \[B\].
#' * `$logratio` (`Tensor`): Signed logq-logp per supplied sample \[B\], not analytic KL.
#' * `$probability` (`Tensor`): Sigmoid Bernoulli probabilities \[B,features\], not sampled pixels.
#' * `$nll` (`Tensor`): Summed pixel Bernoulli NLL (binary) or cross-entropy (soft) \[B\].
#' * `$loss` (`Tensor`): Scalar mean(nll+logratio), sampled negative ELBO.
#' * `$inverse_z0` (`Tensor`): Second inverse then first inverse recover z0 \[B,L\] up to roundoff.
#' * `$inverse_logdet` (`Tensor`): Sum of inverse log determinants \[B\], cancelling forward up to roundoff.
#' @section Methods:
#' * `$Named()` -> `vector<list(character, Tensor)>`
#'
#'   Copy the eighteen endpoint handles into their stable named archive order.
#'   - Returns: Owning NamedTensors from context through inverse_logdet, in field declaration order.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(3001);
#' const auto out=n::models::FlowVariationalAutoencoder(
#'     p,n::zeros({2,784}),n::zeros({2,4}));
#' // out.z0 equals mu; out.z is flowed mu, not generally a posterior mean.
#' ```
