#' Own eleven sample-major Gaussian IWAE endpoints without fitting or sampling state.
#'
#' All fields own lifetime and preserve autograd history. Sample-major rows are
#' flattened for Gaussian/decoder endpoints; bound/ESS have B rows, weights\[K,B\].
#' Analytic kl is diagnostic only and does not enter loss. Decode(mu) is not the
#' posterior predictive mean. Caller owns supplied noise and any optimizer.
#' @section Constructor:
#' `ImportanceWeightedAutoencoderOutput$new()`
#' @section Fields:
#' * `$mu` (`Tensor`): Owning posterior means\[KB,L\], re-encoded per draw.
#' * `$log_variance` (`Tensor`): Owning posterior log variances\[KB,L\].
#' * `$z` (`Tensor`): Owning explicitly reparameterized latent samples\[KB,L\].
#' * `$probability` (`Tensor`): Owning decoder sigmoid probabilities\[KB,F\], not sampled pixels.
#' * `$nll` (`Tensor`): Owning per-draw summed Bernoulli pixel NLL\[KB\], nats.
#' * `$kl` (`Tensor`): Owning analytic per-row standard-normal KL\[KB\], diagnostic only.
#' * `$loss` (`Tensor`): Owning scalar mean per-case sampled negative IWAE bound, nats.
#' * `$negative_bound` (`Tensor`): Owning per-case sampled negative bound\[B\], nats.
#' * `$log_weights` (`Tensor`): Owning sampled density ratios\[K,B\], nats.
#' * `$normalized_weights` (`Tensor`): Owning sample-normalized importance weights\[K,B\].
#' * `$effective_samples` (`Tensor`): Owning effective sample sizes\[B\].
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;
#' n::ParameterStore p(2237);
#' const auto out=n::models::ImportanceWeightedAutoencoder(p,n::full({2,784},.2),
#'     n::zeros({5,2,4}));
