#' Own live RGB logistic-mixture probabilities and their actual intermediate fields.
#'
#' Eight flat handles keep applicable image/parameter first and higher paths
#' alive after parent collection. P is the product of image axes before its
#' final RGB axis, K is the positive component count. All fields match the
#' input floating dtype; pixel ordering follows contiguous flattened NHWC.
#' No model/store, fitting, sampling or mutation is retained.
#' @section Constructor:
#' `LogisticRgbOutput$new()`
#' @section Fields:
#' * `$pixel_log_probability` (`Tensor`): Owning live\[P\] joint log probability of each RGB pixel.
#' * `$component_log_probability` (`Tensor`): Owning live\[P,K\] sum of three conditional channel log masses.
#' * `$mixture_log_probability` (`Tensor`): Owning live\[P,K\] normalized log weights, log_softmax(raw logits).
#' * `$means` (`Tensor`): Owning live\[P,K,3\] means after teacher-forced R/G coupling.
#' * `$log_scales` (`Tensor`): Owning live\[P,K,3\] raw log scales lower-clipped at-7.
#' * `$coefficients` (`Tensor`): Owning live\[P,K,3\] tanh coefficients RG,BR,BG in that order.
#' * `$channel_log_mass` (`Tensor`): Owning live\[P,K,3\] stable8-bit bin log masses including infinite tails.
#' * `$mean_channel_nll` (`Tensor`): Owning live scalar -mean(pixel_log_probability)/3, nats per RGB channel.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' auto o=dm::nn::models::DiscretizedLogisticRGB(dm::nn::zeros({2,3}),dm::nn::zeros({2,30}));
#' // pixel_log_probability[2], channel_log_mass[2,3,3], scalar mean_channel_nll.
#' ```
#' @references - Salimans, Karpathy, Chen and Kingma(2017), PixelCNN++: Improving the PixelCNN
#'   with Discretized Logistic Mixture Likelihood and Other Modifications,
#'   https://arxiv.org/abs/1701.05517 . Stable exact-bin compact teaching variant.
#' @seealso DiscretizedLogisticRGB(), PixelCnnPPOutput, PixelCnnPP()
#' @md
#'
`LogisticRgbOutput` <- R6::R6Class("LogisticRgbOutput", inherit = `.rosetta_object`, cloneable = FALSE,
