#' Own fixed WaveStack weights and circular histories for one categorical code stream.
#'
#' Snapshot required finite Float32 CPU leaves from a warmed ParameterStore;
#' later store writes/collection cannot affect this cache. Each block retains
#' its OWN input at its dilation, not a raw-code history or another block's
#' residual. Input uses previous/current code taps; the last residual projection
#' is absent. Skip summation, ReLU/post/ReLU/head match WaveStack. One next(code)
#' consumes one code and returns the logits for the following code. The source
#' scalar Float32 multiply/add order and tanh(filter)/(1.f+exp(-gate)) arithmetic
#' are retained; cached/full-convolution results may differ by roundoff.
#'
#' Fixed weights and mutable state own all storage. C++ copies and clone() fork
#' independent streams at the current position. Output Tensors own detached
#' storage and outlive the cache. No fitting, optimizer, RNG, categorical draw,
#' codec, parameter writes or autograd path. Distinct caches are independent;
#' callers synchronize access to one cache. Reset restores the true beginning
#' with zero feature histories and no previous code, not code-zero padding.
#' Memory is copied weights plus R*cycles*(2^levels-1) floats for rings. Per-code
#' work is O(R*classes+blocks*(R^2+R*skip)+skip^2+skip*classes), independent of
#' generated length; scratch is O(blocks*R+skip+classes). Failed invalid-code,
#' count-limit or nonfinite-candidate steps preserve the previous state.
#' @section Constructor:
#' `WaveStackCache$new(parameters, config)`
#'
#' Snapshot the required Float32 leaves and initialize empty per-layer histories.
#'
#' * `parameters` (`ParameterStore`): Read-only warmed Float32 store with all required finite CPU leaves.
#' * `config` (`WaveStackConfig`): Explicit matching WaveStackConfig, copied by value; no implicit architecture inference.
#' @section Methods:
#' * `$next_code(code)` -> `Tensor`
#'
#'   Consume one observed/generated code and return detached scores for the next code.
#'   - `code`: Integer code in\[0,classes); code128 is the source cold-start seed for256 classes.
#'   - Returns: Owning detached Float32 CPU\[classes\] logits predicting the following code.
#'
#' * `$reset()`
#'
#'   Clear every feature ring and previous-code tap without changing the weight snapshot.
#'
#' * `$consumed()` -> `integer`
#'
#'   Count successfully consumed codes since construction or the most recent reset.
#'   - Returns: Nonnegative Int64 count; failed next calls do not increment it.
#'
#' * `$clone()` -> `WaveStackCache`
#'
#'   Fork an independent weight snapshot and all current circular state by value.
#'   - Returns: Owning independent WaveStackCache at the same stream position.
#' @section Examples (C++):
#' ```cpp
#' #include <dm/dm.hpp>
#' namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;
#' m::WaveStackConfig c{4,8,5,1,256};n::ParameterStore p(541);
#' m::WaveStack(p,n::one_hot(n::zeros({1,2},n::DType::Int32),256),c);
#' m::WaveStackCache cache(p,c);auto logits=cache.next(128);
#' // Owning detached Float32[256]; cache.consumed()==1. Choose/feed the next code explicitly.
#' ```
#' @section Errors:
#' * `std::invalid_argument`: For invalid config, missing/misshaped/nonfinite/non-CPU or non-Float32 leaves.
#' @references - van den Oord et al.(2016), WaveNet: A Generative Model for Raw Audio,
#'   https://arxiv.org/abs/1609.03499 . Circular block-input histories implement
#'   the repository's two-tap unconditional teaching stack, not conditioned TTS.
#' @seealso WaveStack(), WaveStackField(), WaveNll(), next(), reset(), clone()
#' @md
#'
`WaveStackCache` <- R6::R6Class("WaveStackCache", inherit = `.rosetta_object`, cloneable = FALSE,
  public = list(
    initialize = function(...) {
      if (...length() == 1L && inherits(..1, "rosetta_ptr")) self$.ptr <- ..1
      else { if (!is.null(self$.ptr)) stop("native object already initialized"); self$.ptr <- .Call(`.rs_6123`, list(...)) }
      invisible(self)
    },
    `next_code` = function(...) .Call(`.rs_6119`, self, list(...)),
    `reset` = function(...) invisible(.Call(`.rs_6120`, self, list(...))),
    `consumed` = function(...) .Call(`.rs_6121`, self, list(...))
  )
)
`WaveStackCache`$set("public", "clone", function(...) .Call(`.rs_6122`, self, list(...)))
